\s1 The Conquest of Canaan Proceeds
\r \ref Joshua 13:1–7|JOS 13:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb After|אַחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb the death|מ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Joshua,|יְהוֹשֻׁ֔עַ\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb inquired|וַֽיִּשְׁאֲלוּ֙\rb* \rb of the LORD,|בַּיהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb will be the first|בַּתְּחִלָּ֖ה\rb* \rb to go up|יַעֲלֶה־\rb* \rb and fight|לְהִלָּ֥חֶם\rb* \rb for us|לָּ֧נוּ\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Canaanites?”|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֛י\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb “Judah|יְהוּדָ֣ה\rb* \rb shall go up,”|יַעֲלֶ֑ה\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb “Indeed,|הִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb I have delivered|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into their hands.”|בְּיָדֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Then the men of Judah|יְהוּדָה֩\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to their brothers|אָחִ֜יו\rb* \rb the Simeonites,|לְשִׁמְע֨וֹן\rb* \rb “Come up|עֲלֵ֧ה\rb* \rb with us|אִתִּ֣י\rb* \rb to our allotted territory,|בְגוֹרָלִ֗י\rb* \rb and let us fight|וְנִֽלָּחֲמָה֙\rb* \rb against the Canaanites.|בַּֽכְּנַעֲנִ֔י\rb* \rb And we|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb likewise|גַם־\rb* \rb will go|וְהָלַכְתִּ֧י\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּךָ֖\rb* \rb to your territory.”|בְּגוֹרָלֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb So the Simeonites|שִׁמְעֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb with them.|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb When Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb attacked,|וַיַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb delivered|וַיִּתֵּ֧ן\rb* \rb the Canaanites|הַכְּנַעֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb and Perizzites|וְהַפְּרִזִּ֖י\rb* \rb into their hands,|בְּיָדָ֑ם\rb* \rb and they struck down|וַיַּכּ֣וּם\rb* \rb ten|עֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb men|אִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb at Bezek.|בְּבֶ֔זֶק\rb* \v 5 \rb And there|בְּבֶ֔זֶק\rb* \rb they found|וַֽ֠יִּמְצְאוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb Adoni-bezek|בֶ֙זֶק֙\rb* \rb and fought|וַיִּֽלָּחֲמ֖וּ\rb* \rb against him,|בּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb striking down|וַיַּכּ֕וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֖י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Perizzites.|הַפְּרִזִּֽי׃\rb* \v 6 \rb As Adoni-bezek|אֲדֹ֣נִי\rb*
\p \rb |בֶ֔זֶק\rb* \rb fled,|וַיָּ֙נָס֙\rb* \rb they pursued him,|וַֽיִּרְדְּפ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרָ֑יו\rb* \rb seized him,|וַיֹּאחֲז֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and cut off|וַֽיְקַצְּצ֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his thumbs|בְּהֹנ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |יָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb and big toes.|וְרַגְלָֽיו׃\rb* \v 7 \rb Then Adoni-bezek|בֶ֗זֶק\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Seventy|שִׁבְעִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb kings|מְלָכִ֡ים\rb* \rb with their thumbs|בְּֽהֹנוֹת֩\rb*\rb |יְדֵיהֶ֨ם\rb* \rb and big toes|וְרַגְלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb cut off|מְקֻצָּצִ֗ים\rb*\rb |הָי֤וּ\rb* \rb have gathered the scraps|מְלַקְּטִים֙\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb my table.|שֻׁלְחָנִ֔י\rb* \rb As|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have done to them,|עָשִׂ֔יתִי\rb* \rb so|כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb has repaid|שִׁלַּם־\rb* \rb me.”|לִ֖י\rb* \rb And they brought him|וַיְבִיאֻ֥הוּ\rb* \rb to Jerusalem,|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb where he died.|וַיָּ֥מָת\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Capture of Jerusalem and Hebron
\r \ref Joshua 15:13–19|JOS 15:13-19\ref*)
\p \v 8 \rb Then the men|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb fought|וַיִּלָּחֲמ֤וּ\rb* \rb against Jerusalem|בִּיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb and captured it.|וַיִּלְכְּד֣וּ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb They put the city|וַיַּכּ֖וּהָ\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword|חָ֑רֶב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and set|שִׁלְּח֥וּ\rb* \rb it|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb on fire.|בָאֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \v 9 \rb Afterward,|וְאַחַ֗ר\rb* \rb the men|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb marched down|יָֽרְדוּ֙\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֖ם\rb* \rb against the Canaanites|בַּֽכְּנַעֲנִ֑י\rb* \rb living|יוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in the hill country,|הָהָ֔ר\rb* \rb in the Negev,|וְהַנֶּ֖גֶב\rb* \rb and in the foothills.|וְהַשְּׁפֵלָֽה׃\rb*\f + \fr 1:9 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shephelah \ft or \fqa lowlands\ft ; that is, the western foothills of Judea\f*
\p \v 10 \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb also marched|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִי֙\rb* \rb who were living|הַיּוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in Hebron|בְּחֶבְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb |חֶבְר֥וֹן\rb* \rb (formerly|לְפָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb known as|וְשֵׁם־\rb*\rb |קִרְיַ֣ת\rb* \rb Kiriath-arba),|אַרְבַּ֑ע\rb* \rb and they struck down|וַיַּכּ֛וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Sheshai,|שֵׁשַׁ֥י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ahiman,|אֲחִימַ֖ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Talmai.|תַּלְמָֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb From there|מִשָּׁ֔ם\rb* \rb they marched|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the inhabitants|יוֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Debir|דְּבִ֑יר\rb* \rb |דְּבִ֥יר\rb* \rb (formerly|לְפָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb known as|וְשֵׁם־\rb*\rb |קִרְיַת־\rb* \rb Kiriath-sepher).|סֵֽפֶר׃\rb* \v 12 \rb And Caleb|כָּלֵ֔ב\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “To the man|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb who strikes down|יַכֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |קִרְיַת־\rb* \rb Kiriath-sepher|סֵ֖פֶר\rb* \rb and captures it,|וּלְכָדָ֑הּ\rb* \rb I will give|וְנָתַ֥תִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my daughter|בִתִּ֖י\rb* \rb Acsah|עַכְסָ֥ה\rb* \rb in marriage.”|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb* \v 13 \rb So Othniel|עָתְנִיאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Caleb’s|כָלֵ֖ב\rb* \rb younger|הַקָּטֹ֣ן\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֑נּוּ\rb* \rb brother|אֲחִ֥י\rb* \rb Kenaz|קְנַ֔ז\rb* \rb captured the city,|וַֽיִּלְכְּדָהּ֙\rb* \rb and Caleb gave|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his daughter|בִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Acsah|עַכְסָ֥ה\rb* \rb to him|ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb in marriage.|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb One day|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb Acsah came to Othniel|בְּבוֹאָ֗הּ\rb* \rb and urged him|וַתְּסִיתֵ֙הוּ֙\rb*\f + \fr 1:14 \ft Hebrew; LXX and Vulgate \fqa and he urged her\ft ; see \ref Joshua 15:18|JOS 15:18\ref*.\f* \rb to ask|לִשְׁא֤וֹל\rb*\rb |מֵֽאֵת־\rb* \rb her father|אָבִ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb for a field.|הַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb When she got off|וַתִּצְנַ֖ח\rb*\rb |מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb her donkey,|הַחֲמ֑וֹר\rb* \rb Caleb|כָּלֵ֖ב\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּֽאמֶר־\rb* \rb her,|לָ֥הּ\rb* \rb “What|מַה־\rb* \rb do you desire?”|לָּֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb “Give|הָֽבָה־\rb* \rb me|לִּ֣י\rb* \rb a blessing,”|בְרָכָ֗ה\rb* \rb she answered.|וַתֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb “Since|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you have given me|נְתַתָּ֔נִי\rb* \rb land|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb in the Negev,|הַנֶּ֙גֶב֙\rb* \rb give|וְנָתַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb me|לִ֖י\rb* \rb springs|גֻּלֹּ֣ת\rb* \rb of water as well.”|מָ֑יִם\rb*
\p \rb So Caleb|כָּלֵ֗ב\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb her|לָ֣הּ\rb* \rb both the upper|עִלִּ֔ית\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |גֻּלֹּ֥ת\rb* \rb and lower|תַּחְתִּֽית׃פ\rb* \rb springs.|גֻּלֹּ֣ת\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Now the descendants|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Moses’|מֹשֶׁ֜ה\rb* \rb father-in-law,|חֹתֵ֨ן\rb* \rb the Kenite,|קֵינִי֩\rb* \rb went up|עָל֨וּ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the men|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb from the City|מֵעִ֤יר\rb* \rb of Palms|הַתְּמָרִים֙\rb*\f + \fr 1:16 \ft That is, Jericho\f* \rb to the Wilderness|מִדְבַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the Negev|בְּנֶ֣גֶב\rb* \rb near Arad.|עֲרָ֑ד\rb* \rb They went|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb to live|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb among|אֶת־\rb* \rb the people.|הָעָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Then the men of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb their brothers|אָחִ֔יו\rb* \rb the Simeonites,|שִׁמְע֣וֹן\rb* \rb attacked|וַיַּכּ֕וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb living|יוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in Zephath,|צְפַ֑ת\rb* \rb and devoted the city to destruction.|וַיַּחֲרִ֣ימוּ\rb*\f + \fr 1:17 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f* \rb |אוֹתָ֔הּ\rb*\rb So it was called|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שֵׁם־\rb*\rb |הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb Hormah.|חָרְמָֽה׃\rb*\f + \fr 1:17 \fqa Hormah \ft means \fqa destruction\ft .\f* \v 18 \rb And Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb also captured|וַיִּלְכֹּ֤ד\rb*\f + \fr 1:18 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa But Judah did not capture\f* \rb Gaza,|עַזָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |גְּבוּלָ֔הּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb Ashkelon,|אַשְׁקְל֖וֹן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |גְּבוּלָ֑הּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Ekron—|עֶקְר֖וֹן\rb*  \rb each with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb its territory.|גְּבוּלָֽהּ׃\rb* \v 19 \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb with|אֶתּ־\rb* \rb Judah,|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and they took possession|וַיֹּ֖רֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the hill country;|הָהָ֑ר\rb* \rb but|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they could not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb drive out|לְהוֹרִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the plains|הָעֵ֔מֶק\rb* \rb because|כִּי־\rb* \rb they had|לָהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb chariots|רֶ֥כֶב\rb* \rb of iron.|בַּרְזֶ֖ל\rb*
