\p \v 21 \rb The Benjamites,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בִנְיָמִ֑ן\rb* \rb however,|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb failed to|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb drive out|הוֹרִ֖ישׁוּ\rb* \rb the Jebusites|הַיְבוּסִי֙\rb* \rb living|יֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in Jerusalem.|יְרֽוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb So to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃ס\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb the Jebusites|הַיְבוּסִ֜י\rb* \rb live|וַיֵּ֨שֶׁב\rb* \rb there|בִּיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb among|אֶת־\rb* \rb the Benjamites.|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |בִנְיָמִן֙\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb The house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵ֛ף\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb*\rb |הֵ֖ם\rb* \rb attacked|וַיַּעֲל֧וּ\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel,|אֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb was with them.|עִמָּֽם׃\rb* \v 23 \rb They|בֵית־\rb*\rb |יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb sent spies|וַיָּתִ֥ירוּ\rb* \rb to Bethel|אֵ֑ל\rb* \rb (formerly|לְפָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb known as|וְשֵׁם־\rb* \rb Luz),|לֽוּז׃\rb* \v 24 \rb and when the spies|הַשֹּׁ֣מְרִ֔ים\rb* \rb saw|וַיִּרְאוּ֙\rb* \rb a man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb coming out|יוֹצֵ֣א\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the city,|הָעִ֑יר\rb* \rb they said|וַיֹּ֣אמְרוּ\rb* \rb to him,|ל֗וֹ\rb* \rb “Please|נָא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb show us|הַרְאֵ֤נוּ\rb* \rb how to get into|מְב֣וֹא\rb* \rb the city,|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb and we will treat|וְעָשִׂ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb you|עִמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb kindly.”|חָֽסֶד׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb So the man showed them|וַיַּרְאֵם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the entrance|מְב֣וֹא\rb* \rb to the city,|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb and they put|וַיַּכּ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword|חָ֑רֶב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb but released|שִׁלֵּֽחוּ׃\rb* \rb that man|הָאִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his family.|מִשְׁפַּחְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \v 26 \rb And the man|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb to the land|אֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Hittites,|הַחִתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb built|וַיִּ֣בֶן\rb* \rb a city,|עִ֗יר\rb* \rb and called it|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb*\rb |שְׁמָהּ֙\rb* \rb Luz,|ל֔וּז\rb* \rb which|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb is its name|שְׁמָ֔הּ\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb day.|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*
\s1 The Failure to Complete the Conquest
\p \v 27 \rb At that time Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb failed|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb to drive out the inhabitants|הוֹרִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |בֵּית־\rb* \rb of Beth-shean,|שְׁאָ֣ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |בְּנוֹתֶיהָ֮\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Taanach,|תַּעְנַ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |בְּנֹתֶיהָ֒\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |יֹשֵׁב\rb* \rb Dor,|ד֜וֹר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |בְּנוֹתֶ֗יהָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |יוֹשְׁבֵ֤י\rb* \rb Ibleam,|יִבְלְעָם֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |בְּנֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |יוֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb Megiddo,|מְגִדּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and their villages;|בְּנוֹתֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb for the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֔י\rb* \rb were determined|וַיּ֙וֹאֶל֙\rb* \rb to dwell|לָשֶׁ֖בֶת\rb* \rb in that|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb land.|בָּאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \v 28 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb became stronger,|חָזַ֣ק\rb* \rb they pressed|וַיָּ֥שֶׂם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb into forced labor,|לָמַ֑ס\rb* \rb but they never|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb drove them out|וְהוֹרֵ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb completely.|הוֹרִישֽׁוֹ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb Ephraim|וְאֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb also failed|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb to drive out|הוֹרִ֔ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb living|הַיּוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in Gezer;|בְּגָ֑זֶר\rb* \rb so the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb continued to dwell|וַיֵּ֧שֶׁב\rb* \rb among them|בְּקִרְבּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb in Gezer.|בְּגָֽזֶר׃פ\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb Zebulun|זְבוּלֻ֗ן\rb* \rb failed|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb to drive out|הוֹרִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the inhabitants|יוֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Kitron|קִטְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |יוֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb Nahalol;|נַהֲלֹ֑ל\rb* \rb so the Canaanites|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִי֙\rb* \rb lived|וַיֵּ֤שֶׁב\rb* \rb among them|בְּקִרְבּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and served|וַיִּֽהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb as forced laborers.|לָמַֽס׃ס\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb Asher|אָשֵׁ֗ר\rb* \rb failed|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb to drive out|הוֹרִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Acco,|עַכּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |יוֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb Sidon,|צִיד֑וֹן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ahlab,|אַחְלָ֤ב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Achzib,|אַכְזִיב֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Helbah,|חֶלְבָּ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Aphik,|אֲפִ֖יק\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Rehob.|רְחֹֽב׃\rb* \v 32 \rb So the Asherites|הָאָ֣שֵׁרִ֔י\rb* \rb lived|וַיֵּ֙שֶׁב֙\rb* \rb among|בְּקֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb the Canaanite|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the land,|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb because|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb they did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb drive them out.|הוֹרִישֽׁוֹ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִ֗י\rb* \rb failed|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to drive out|הוֹרִ֞ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֵ֤י\rb*\rb |בֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Beth-shemesh|שֶׁ֙מֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בֵית־\rb* \rb Beth-anath.|עֲנָ֔ת\rb* \rb So the Naphtalites also lived|וַיֵּ֕שֶׁב\rb* \rb among|בְּקֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb the Canaanite|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb inhabitants|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the land,|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb but the inhabitants|וְיֹשְׁבֵ֤י\rb*\rb |בֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Beth-shemesh|שֶׁ֙מֶשׁ֙\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb and Beth-anath|עֲנָ֔ת\rb* \rb served|הָי֥וּ\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb as forced laborers.|לָמַֽס׃ס\rb*
\p \v 34 \rb The Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb forced|וַיִּלְחֲצ֧וּ\rb* \rb the Danites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |דָ֖ן\rb* \rb into the hill country|הָהָ֑רָה\rb* \rb and|כִּי־\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb allow them|נְתָנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to come down|לָרֶ֥דֶת\rb* \rb into the plain.|לָעֵֽמֶק׃\rb* \v 35 \rb And the Amorites|הָֽאֱמֹרִי֙\rb* \rb were determined|וַיּ֤וֹאֶל\rb* \rb to dwell|לָשֶׁ֣בֶת\rb* \rb in Mount|בְּהַר־\rb* \rb Heres,|חֶ֔רֶס\rb* \rb Aijalon,|בְּאַיָּל֖וֹן\rb* \rb and Shaalbim.|וּבְשַֽׁעַלְבִ֑ים\rb* \rb But when the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵ֔ף\rb* \rb grew|וַתִּכְבַּד֙\rb* \rb in strength,|יַ֣ד\rb* \rb they pressed the Amorites|וַיִּהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb into forced labor.|לָמַֽס׃\rb* \v 36 \rb And the border|וּגְבוּל֙\rb* \rb of the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb* \rb extended from the Ascent|מִֽמַּעֲלֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of Akrabbim|עַקְרַבִּ֑ים\rb*\f + \fr 1:36 \ft Or \fqa the Ascent of Scorpions \ft or \fqa Scorpion Pass\f* \rb to Sela|מֵהַסֶּ֖לַע\rb* \rb and beyond.|וָמָֽעְלָה׃פ\rb*
\c 2
\s1 Israel Rebuked at Bochim
\p \v 1 \rb Now the angel|מַלְאַךְ־\rb*\f + \fr 2:1 \ft Or \fqa Angel\ft ; also in verse 4\f* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֧עַל\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Gilgal|הַגִּלְגָּ֖ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Bochim|הַבֹּכִ֑ים פ\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb “I brought you up|אַעֲלֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb and led|וָאָבִ֤יא\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb you into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I had promised|נִשְׁבַּ֙עְתִּי֙\rb* \rb to your fathers,|לַאֲבֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and I said,|וָאֹמַ֕ר\rb* \rb ‘I will never|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb break|אָפֵ֧ר\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֛י\rb* \rb with you,|אִתְּכֶ֖ם\rb* \v 2 \rb and you|וְאַתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb are not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to make|תִכְרְת֤וּ\rb* \rb a covenant|בְרִית֙\rb* \rb with the people|לְיֽוֹשְׁבֵי֙\rb* \rb of this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb land,|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb but you shall tear down|תִּתֹּצ֑וּן\rb* \rb their altars.’|מִזְבְּחוֹתֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \rb Yet you have not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb obeyed|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb My voice.|בְּקֹלִ֖י\rb* \rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb is this|זֹּ֥את\rb* \rb you have done?|עֲשִׂיתֶֽם׃\rb* \v 3 \rb So now|וְגַ֣ם\rb* \rb I tell you|אָמַ֔רְתִּי\rb* \rb that I will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb drive out these people|אֲגָרֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb before you;|מִפְּנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb they will be thorns|וְהָי֤וּ\rb* \rb in your|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb sides,|לְצִדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and their gods|וֵאלֹ֣הֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb will be|יִהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb a snare|לְמוֹקֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb to you.”|לָכֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb When the angel|מַלְאַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had spoken|כְּדַבֵּ֞ר\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites,|בְּנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb lifted up|וַיִּשְׂא֥וּ\rb* \rb their voices|קוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb and wept.|וַיִּבְכּֽוּ׃\rb* \v 5 \rb So they called|וַֽיִּקְרְא֛וּ\rb*\rb |שֵֽׁם־\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb Bochim|בֹּכִ֑ים\rb*\f + \fr 2:5 \fqa Bochim \ft means \fqa weepers\ft .\f* \rb and offered sacrifices|וַיִּזְבְּחוּ־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַֽיהוָֽה׃פ\rb*
\s1 Joshua’s Death and Burial
