\p \v 6 \rb After Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb* \rb had dismissed|וַיְשַׁלַּ֥ח\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּלְכ֧וּ\rb* \rb to take possession of|לָרֶ֥שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land,|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb each|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to his own inheritance.|לְנַחֲלָת֖וֹ\rb* \v 7 \rb And the people|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb served|וַיַּעַבְד֤וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb throughout|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֑עַ\rb* \rb and|וְכֹ֣ל׀\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the elders|הַזְּקֵנִ֗ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb outlived|הֶאֱרִ֤יכוּ\rb*\rb |יָמִים֙\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb him,|יְהוֹשׁ֔וּעַ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had seen|רָא֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the great|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb works|מַעֲשֵׂ֤ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb for Israel.|לְיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb And Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֥עַ\rb* \rb son|בִּן־\rb* \rb of Nun,|נ֖וּן\rb* \rb the servant|עֶ֣בֶד\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֛מָת\rb* \rb at the age|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנִֽים׃\rb* \rb of 110.|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וָעֶ֖שֶׂר\rb* \v 9 \rb They buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֤וּ\rb* \rb him|אוֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb in the land|בִּגְב֣וּל\rb* \rb of his inheritance,|נַחֲלָת֔וֹ\rb*\rb |בְּתִמְנַת־\rb* \rb at Timnath-heres|חֶ֖רֶס\rb*\f + \fr 2:9 \fqa Timnath-heres \ft is also known as \fqa Timnath-serah\ft ; see \ref Joshua 19:50|JOS 19:50\ref* and Joshua 24:30.\f* \rb in the hill country|בְּהַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Ephraim,|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb north|מִצְּפ֖וֹן\rb* \rb of Mount|לְהַר־\rb* \rb Gaash.|גָּֽעַשׁ׃\rb*
\s1 Israel’s Unfaithfulness
\r \ref Isaiah 43:22–28|ISA 43:22-28\ref*; \ref Jeremiah 2:23–37|JER 2:23-37\ref*)
\p \v 10 \rb After that|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb generation|הַדּ֣וֹר\rb*\rb |הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb had also|וְגַם֙\rb* \rb been gathered|נֶאֶסְפ֖וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their fathers,|אֲבוֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb another|אַחֵ֜ר\rb* \rb generation|דּ֨וֹר\rb* \rb rose up|וַיָּקָם֩\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb know|יָֽדְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb or|וְגַם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the works|הַֽמַּעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He had done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb for Israel.|לְיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb* \v 11 \rb And the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb did|וַיַּעֲשׂ֧וּ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and served|וַיַּעַבְד֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Baals.|הַבְּעָלִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Thus they forsook|וַיַּעַזְב֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of their fathers,|אֲבוֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb who had brought them|הַמּוֹצִ֣יא\rb*\rb |אוֹתָם֮\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרַיִם֒\rb* \rb and they followed|וַיֵּלְכ֞וּ\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb various|אֲחֵרִ֗ים\rb*\rb |מֵאֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb of the peoples|הָֽעַמִּים֙\rb* \rb around them.|סְבִיב֣וֹתֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb They bowed down|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּחֲו֖וּ\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and provoked|וַיַּכְעִ֖סוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD to anger,|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 13 \rb for they forsook|וַיַּעַזְב֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Him|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and served|וַיַּעַבְד֥וּ\rb* \rb Baal|לַבַּ֖עַל\rb* \rb and the Ashtoreths.|וְלָעַשְׁתָּרֽוֹת׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Then the anger|אַ֤ף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb against Israel,|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and He delivered them|וַֽיִּתְּנֵם֙\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַד־\rb*\rb |שֹׁסִ֔ים\rb* \rb of those who plundered|וַיָּשֹׁ֖סּוּ\rb* \rb them.|אוֹתָ֑ם\rb*\f + \fr 2:14 \ft Literally \fqa of plunderers who plundered them\f* \rb He sold them|וַֽיִּמְכְּרֵ֞ם\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַ֤ד\rb* \rb of their enemies|אֽוֹיְבֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb all around,|מִסָּבִ֔יב\rb* \rb whom they were|יָכְל֣וּ\rb* \rb no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֔וֹד\rb* \rb able to resist.|לַעֲמֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |אוֹיְבֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 15 \rb Wherever|בְּכֹ֣ל׀\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Israel marched out,|יָצְא֗וּ\rb* \rb the hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb was|הָיְתָה־\rb* \rb against them|בָּ֣ם\rb* \rb to bring calamity,|לְרָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb just as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְכַאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb*\rb |דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb had sworn|נִשְׁבַּ֥ע\rb*\rb |יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb to them.|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb So they were greatly distressed.|וַיֵּ֥צֶר\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb*
\s1 Judges Raised Up
\p \v 16 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb raised up|וַיָּ֥קֶם\rb* \rb judges,|שֹֽׁפְטִ֑ים\rb*\f + \fr 2:16 \ft Or \fqa governors \ft or \fqa leaders\ft ; here and throughout the book of Judges\f* \rb who saved them|וַיּ֣וֹשִׁיע֔וּם\rb* \rb from the hands|מִיַּ֖ד\rb* \rb of those who plundered them.|שֹׁסֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Israel, however,|וְגַ֤ם\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמֵ֔עוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their judges.|שֹֽׁפְטֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb Instead,|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they prostituted|זָנ֗וּ\rb* \rb themselves with|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb and bowed down|וַיִּֽשְׁתַּחֲו֖וּ\rb* \rb to them.|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb They quickly|מַהֵ֗ר\rb* \rb turned|סָ֣רוּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the way|הַדֶּ֜רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb of their fathers,|אֲבוֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb who had walked|הָלְכ֧וּ\rb* \rb in obedience|לִשְׁמֹ֥עַ\rb* \rb to the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb commandments;|מִצְוֺת־\rb* \rb they did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb do as their fathers had done.|עָ֥שׂוּ\rb*\rb |כֵֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Whenever|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה׀\rb* \rb raised up|הֵקִ֨ים\rb* \rb a judge|שֹֽׁפְטִים֒\rb* \rb for the Israelites,|לָהֶם֮\rb* \rb He|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb was|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb that judge|הַשֹּׁפֵ֔ט\rb* \rb and saved them|וְהֽוֹשִׁיעָם֙\rb* \rb from the hands|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of their enemies|אֹֽיְבֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb while the judge|הַשּׁוֹפֵ֑ט\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb was still alive;|כֹּ֖ל\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb for the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb was moved to pity|יִנָּחֵ֤ם\rb* \rb by their groaning|מִנַּֽאֲקָתָ֔ם\rb* \rb under those|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb who oppressed them|לֹחֲצֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and afflicted them.|וְדֹחֲקֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 19 \rb But when|וְהָיָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the judge|הַשּׁוֹפֵ֗ט\rb*\rb |יָשֻׁ֙בוּ֙\rb* \rb died,|בְּמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb the Israelites became even more corrupt|וְהִשְׁחִ֣יתוּ\rb* \rb than their fathers,|מֵֽאֲבוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb going|לָלֶ֗כֶת\rb* \rb after|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb to serve them|לְעָבְדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and bow down|וּלְהִשְׁתַּחֲוֺ֣ת\rb* \rb to them.|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb They would not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb give up|הִפִּ֙ילוּ֙\rb* \rb their evil practices|מִמַּ֣עַלְלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and stubborn|הַקָּשָֽׁה׃\rb* \rb ways.|וּמִדַּרְכָּ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb So the anger|אַ֥ף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb against Israel,|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and He said,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Because|יַעַן֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb nation|הַגּ֣וֹי\rb* \rb has transgressed|עָבְר֜וּ\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִיתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I laid down|צִוִּ֣יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for their fathers|אֲבוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and has not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb heeded|שָׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb My voice,|לְקוֹלִֽי׃\rb* \v 21 \rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb will no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb longer|אוֹסִ֔יף\rb* \rb drive out|לְהוֹרִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb before them|מִן־\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb any|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֖עַ\rb* \rb left|עָזַ֥ב\rb* \rb when he died.|וַיָּמֹֽת׃\rb* \v 22 \rb In this way|לְמַ֛עַן\rb* \rb I will test|נַסּ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb whether|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹֽא׃\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |הֵם֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will keep|הֲשֹׁמְרִ֣ים\rb* \rb the way|דֶּ֨רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb by walking|לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb in it|בָּ֗ם\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb*\rb |שָׁמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb their fathers did.”|אֲבוֹתָ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb That is why the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had left those|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֣ם\rb* \rb in place|וַיַּנַּ֤ח\rb* \rb and had not|לְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb driven them out|הוֹרִישָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb immediately|מַהֵ֑ר\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb by delivering them|נְתָנָ֖ם\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of Joshua.|יְהוֹשֻֽׁעַ׃פ\rb*
\c 3
\s1 Nations Left to Test Israel
\p \v 1 \rb These|וְאֵ֤לֶּה\rb* \rb are the nations|הַגּוֹיִם֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb left|הִנִּ֣יחַ\rb* \rb to test|לְנַסּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb known|יָדְע֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb of the wars|מִלְחֲמ֥וֹת\rb* \rb in Canaan,|כְּנָֽעַן׃\rb* \v 2 \rb if only|רַ֗ק\rb*\rb |לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb*\rb |דַּ֚עַת\rb* \rb to teach|לְלַמְּדָ֖ם\rb* \rb warfare|מִלְחָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb to the subsequent generations|דֹּר֣וֹת\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb especially|רַ֥ק\rb* \rb to those who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb known it|יְדָעֽוּם׃\rb* \rb formerly:|לְפָנִ֖ים\rb* \v 3 \rb the five|חֲמֵ֣שֶׁת׀\rb* \rb rulers|סַרְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Philistines,|פְלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Canaanites,|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִי֙\rb* \rb the Sidonians,|וְהַצִּ֣ידֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb and the Hivites|וְהַ֣חִוִּ֔י\rb* \rb who lived|יֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in the mountains|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Lebanon|הַלְּבָנ֑וֹן\rb* \rb from Mount|מֵהַר֙\rb*\rb |בַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb Baal-hermon|חֶרְמ֔וֹן\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb*\rb |לְב֥וֹא\rb* \rb Lebo-hamath.|חֲמָֽת׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb These nations were left|וַֽיִּהְי֕וּ\rb* \rb to test|לְנַסּ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |בָּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb to find out|לָדַ֗עַת\rb* \rb whether they would keep|הֲיִשְׁמְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb He had given|צִוָּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their fathers|אֲבוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Thus the Israelites|וּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb continued to live|יָשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb among|בְּקֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb the Canaanites,|הַֽכְּנַעֲנִ֑י\rb* \rb Hittites,|הַחִתִּ֤י\rb* \rb Amorites,|וְהָֽאֱמֹרִי֙\rb* \rb Perizzites,|וְהַפְּרִזִּ֔י\rb* \rb Hivites,|וְהַחִוִּ֖י\rb* \rb and Jebusites.|וְהַיְבוּסִֽי׃\rb* \v 6 \rb And they took|וַיִּקְח֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the daughters of these people|בְּנוֹתֵיהֶ֤ם\rb*\rb |לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb in marriage,|לְנָשִׁ֔ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb gave|נָתְנ֣וּ\rb* \rb their own daughters|בְּנוֹתֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to their sons,|לִבְנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and served|וַיַּעַבְד֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their gods.|אֱלֹהֵיהֶֽם׃פ\rb*
\s1 Othniel
\p \v 7 \rb So the Israelites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb did|וַיַּעֲשׂ֨וּ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַע֙\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD;|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb they forgot|וַֽיִּשְׁכְּח֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹֽהֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and served|וַיַּעַבְד֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Baals|הַבְּעָלִ֖ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the Asherahs.|הָאֲשֵׁרֽוֹת׃\rb* \v 8 \rb Then the anger|אַ֤ף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb against Israel,|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and He sold them|וַֽיִּמְכְּרֵ֗ם\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַד֙\rb*\rb |כּוּשַׁ֣ן\rb* \rb of Cushan-rishathaim|רִשְׁעָתַ֔יִם\rb* \rb king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲרַ֣ם\rb* \rb of Aram-naharaim,|נַהֲרָ֑יִם\rb*\f + \fr 3:8 \ft That is, Mesopotamia; \fqa Aram-naharaim \ft means \fqa Aram of the two rivers\ft , likely the region between the Euphrates and Balih Rivers in northwestern Mesopotamia.\f* \rb and the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb served|וַיַּעַבְד֧וּ\rb* \rb him|רִשְׁעָתַ֖יִם\rb* \rb eight|שְׁמֹנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנִֽים׃\rb*
