\s1 Shamgar
\p \v 31 \rb After Ehud|וְאַחֲרָ֤יו\rb* \rb came|הָיָה֙\rb* \rb Shamgar|שַׁמְגַּ֣ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Anath.|עֲנָ֔ת\rb* \rb And he too|ה֖וּא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saved|וַיֹּ֥שַׁע\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb* \rb striking down|וַיַּ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb six|שֵֽׁשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּים֙\rb* \rb with an oxgoad.|בְּמַלְמַ֖ד\rb*\rb |הַבָּקָ֑ר\rb*
\c 4
\s1 Deborah and Barak
\p \v 1 \rb After Ehud|וְאֵה֖וּד\rb* \rb died,|מֵֽת׃\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb again|וַיֹּסִ֙פוּ֙\rb* \rb did|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \v 2 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb sold them|וַיִּמְכְּרֵ֣ם\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb of Jabin|יָבִ֣ין\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Canaan,|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Hazor.|בְּחָצ֑וֹר\rb* \rb The commander|וְשַׂר־\rb* \rb of his forces|צְבָאוֹ֙\rb* \rb was Sisera,|סִֽיסְרָ֔א\rb* \rb who|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb lived|יוֹשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb in Harosheth-hagoyim.|בַּחֲרֹ֥שֶׁת\rb*\rb |הַגּוֹיִֽם׃\rb* \v 3 \rb Then the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb cried out|וַיִּצְעֲק֥וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb because|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb Jabin had|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb nine|תְּשַׁ֨ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֤וֹת\rb* \rb chariots|רֶֽכֶב־\rb* \rb of iron,|בַּרְזֶל֙\rb* \rb and he|וְ֠הוּא\rb* \rb had harshly|בְּחָזְקָ֖ה\rb* \rb oppressed|לָחַ֞ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֧י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb for twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Now Deborah,|וּדְבוֹרָה֙\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb a prophetess,|נְבִיאָ֔ה\rb* \rb the wife|אֵ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb of Lappidoth,|לַפִּיד֑וֹת\rb* \rb was judging|שֹׁפְטָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb at that|הִ֛יא\rb* \rb time.|בָּעֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |הַהִֽיא׃\rb* \v 5 \rb And she|וְ֠הִיא\rb* \rb would sit|יוֹשֶׁ֨בֶת\rb* \rb under|תַּֽחַת־\rb* \rb the Palm|תֹּ֜מֶר\rb* \rb of Deborah|דְּבוֹרָ֗ה\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֧ין\rb* \rb Ramah|הָרָמָ֛ה\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb and Bethel|אֵ֖ל\rb* \rb in the hill country|בְּהַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Ephraim,|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb where the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb would go up|וַיַּעֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֛יהָ\rb* \rb for judgment.|לַמִּשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb She summoned|וַתִּשְׁלַ֗ח\rb*\rb |וַתִּקְרָא֙\rb* \rb Barak|לְבָרָ֣ק\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Abinoam|אֲבִינֹ֔עַם\rb* \rb from Kedesh|מִקֶּ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb in Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִ֑י\rb* \rb and said|וַתֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb “Surely|הֲלֹ֥א\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb is commanding you:|צִוָּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb ‘Go|לֵ֤ךְ\rb* \rb and march|וּמָֽשַׁכְתָּ֙\rb* \rb to Mount|בְּהַ֣ר\rb* \rb Tabor,|תָּב֔וֹר\rb* \rb taking|וְלָקַחְתָּ֣\rb* \rb with you|עִמְּךָ֗\rb* \rb ten|עֲשֶׂ֤רֶת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִים֙\rb* \rb men|אִ֔ישׁ\rb*\rb |מִבְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִ֖י\rb*\rb |וּמִבְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb and Zebulun.|זְבֻלֽוּן׃\rb* \v 7 \rb And I will draw out|וּמָשַׁכְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb Sisera|סִֽיסְרָא֙\rb* \rb the commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of Jabin’s|יָבִ֔ין\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb army,|צְבָ֣א\rb* \rb his chariots,|רִכְבּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and his troops|הֲמוֹנ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the River|נַ֣חַל\rb* \rb Kishon,|קִישׁ֗וֹן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and I will deliver him|וּנְתַתִּ֖יהוּ\rb* \rb into your hand.’”|בְּיָדֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Barak|בָּרָ֔ק\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to her,|אֵלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb “If|אִם־\rb* \rb you will go|תֵּלְכִ֥י\rb* \rb with me,|עִמִּ֖י\rb* \rb I will go;|וְהָלָ֑כְתִּי\rb* \rb but if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb go|תֵלְכִ֛י\rb* \rb with me,|עִמִּ֖י\rb* \rb I will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb go.”|אֵלֵֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb “I will certainly go|הָלֹ֧ךְ\rb*\rb |אֵלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb with you,”|עִמָּ֗ךְ\rb* \rb Deborah replied,|וַתֹּ֜אמֶר\rb* \rb “but|אֶ֚פֶס\rb*\rb |כִּי֩\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the road|הַדֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb are taking|הוֹלֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb will bring you|תִֽהְיֶ֜ה\rb* \rb no|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb honor,|תִּֽפְאַרְתְּךָ֗\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will be selling|יִמְכֹּ֥ר\rb* \rb Sisera|סִֽיסְרָ֑א\rb* \rb into the hand|בְֽיַד־\rb* \rb of a woman.”|אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb So Deborah|דְּבוֹרָ֛ה\rb* \rb got up|וַתָּ֧קָם\rb* \rb and went|וַתֵּ֥לֶך\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Barak|בָּרָ֖ק\rb* \rb to Kedesh,|קֶֽדְשָׁה׃\rb* \v 10 \rb where he|בָּרָ֜ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb summoned|וַיַּזְעֵ֨ק\rb* \rb Zebulun|זְבוּלֻ֤ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Naphtali.|נַפְתָּלִי֙\rb*\rb |קֶ֔דְשָׁה\rb* \rb Ten|עֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb* \rb thousand|אַלְפֵ֖י\rb* \rb men|אִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb followed|וַיַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb him,|בְּרַגְלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and Deborah|דְּבוֹרָֽה׃\rb* \rb also went|וַתַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb with him.|עִמּ֖וֹ\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Now Heber|וְחֶ֤בֶר\rb* \rb the Kenite|הַקֵּינִי֙\rb* \rb had moved away|נִפְרָ֣ד\rb* \rb from the Kenites,|מִקַּ֔יִן\rb* \rb the descendants|מִבְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Hobab|חֹבָ֖ב\rb* \rb the father-in-law|חֹתֵ֣ן\rb*\f + \fr 4:11 \ft Or \fqa brother-in-law\f* \rb of Moses,|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb* \rb and had pitched|וַיֵּ֣ט\rb* \rb his tent|אָהֳל֔וֹ\rb* \rb by|עַד־\rb* \rb the great tree|אֵל֥וֹן\rb* \rb of Zaanannim,|בַּצְעַנִּים\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb was near|אֶת־\rb* \rb Kedesh.|קֶֽדֶשׁ׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb When Sisera|לְסִֽיסְרָ֑א\rb* \rb was told|וַיַּגִּ֖דוּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Barak|בָּרָ֥ק\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Abinoam|אֲבִינֹ֖עַם\rb* \rb had gone up|עָלָ֛ה\rb* \rb Mount|הַר־\rb* \rb Tabor,|תָּבֽוֹר׃ס\rb* \v 13 \rb he|סִֽיסְרָ֜א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb summoned|וַיַּזְעֵ֨ק\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |רִכְבּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb nine|תְּשַׁ֤ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵאוֹת֙\rb* \rb of his iron|בַּרְזֶ֔ל\rb* \rb chariots|רֶ֣כֶב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|הָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb with him,|אִתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb from Harosheth-hagoyim|מֵחֲרֹ֥שֶׁת\rb*\rb |הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the River|נַ֥חַל\rb* \rb Kishon.|קִישֽׁוֹן׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Then Deborah|דְּבֹרָ֨ה\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Barak,|בָּרָ֜ק\rb* \rb “Arise,|ק֗וּם\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this|זֶ֤ה\rb* \rb is the day|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has delivered|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb Sisera|סִֽיסְרָא֙\rb* \rb into your hand.|בְּיָדֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb Has not|הֲלֹ֥א\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb gone|יָצָ֣א\rb* \rb before you?”|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\p \rb So Barak|בָּרָק֙\rb* \rb came down|וַיֵּ֤רֶד\rb* \rb from Mount|מֵהַ֣ר\rb* \rb Tabor|תָּב֔וֹר\rb* \rb with ten|וַעֲשֶׂ֧רֶת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֛ים\rb* \rb men|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb following him.|אַחֲרָֽיו׃\rb* \v 15 \rb And in front of|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb him|בָרָ֑ק\rb* \rb the LORD|יְ֠הוָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb routed|וַיָּ֣הָם\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb with the sword|חֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb Sisera,|סִֽיסְרָ֨א\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his charioteers,|הָרֶ֧כֶב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his army.|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֛ה\rb* \rb Sisera|סִֽיסְרָ֛א\rb* \rb abandoned|וַיֵּ֧רֶד\rb*\rb |מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb his chariot|הַמֶּרְכָּבָ֖ה\rb* \rb and fled|וַיָּ֥נָס\rb* \rb on foot.|בְּרַגְלָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Then Barak|וּבָרָ֗ק\rb* \rb pursued|רָדַ֞ף\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֤י\rb* \rb the chariots|הָרֶ֙כֶב֙\rb*\rb |וְאַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb and army|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb as far as|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb Harosheth-hagoyim,|חֲרֹ֣שֶׁת\rb*\rb |הַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb* \rb and the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb army|מַחֲנֵ֤ה\rb* \rb of Sisera|סִֽיסְרָא֙\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפֹּ֞ל\rb* \rb by the sword;|חֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb a single|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb man was left.|נִשְׁאַ֖ר\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*
\s1 Jael Kills Sisera
\p \v 17 \rb Meanwhile, Sisera|וְסִֽיסְרָא֙\rb* \rb had fled|נָ֣ס\rb* \rb on foot|בְּרַגְלָ֔יו\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the tent|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb of Jael,|יָעֵ֔ל\rb* \rb the wife|אֵ֖שֶּׁת\rb* \rb of Heber|חֶ֣בֶר\rb* \rb the Kenite,|הַקֵּינִ֑י\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb there was peace|שָׁל֗וֹם\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֚ין\rb* \rb Jabin|יָבִ֣ין\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Hazor|חָצ֔וֹר\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֕ין\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb of Heber|חֶ֥בֶר\rb* \rb the Kenite.|הַקֵּינִֽי׃\rb* \v 18 \rb Jael|יָעֵל֮\rb*\rb |לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb went out to greet|וַתֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb Sisera|סִֽיסְרָא֒\rb* \rb and said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb “Come in,|סוּרָ֧ה\rb* \rb my lord.|אֲדֹנִ֛י\rb* \rb Come in|סוּרָ֥ה\rb* \rb with me.|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid.”|תִּירָ֑א\rb* \rb So he entered|וַיָּ֤סַר\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb her tent,|הָאֹ֔הֱלָה\rb* \rb and she covered him|וַתְּכַסֵּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb with a blanket.|בַּשְּׂמִיכָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Sisera said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to her,|אֵלֶ֛יהָ\rb* \rb “Please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb give me a little|מְעַט־\rb* \rb water|מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb to drink,|הַשְׁקִינִי־\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I am thirsty.”|צָמֵ֑אתִי\rb* \rb So she opened|וַתִּפְתַּ֞ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a container|נֹ֧אוד\rb* \rb of milk,|הֶחָלָ֛ב\rb* \rb gave him a drink,|וַתַּשְׁקֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb and covered him again.|וַתְּכַסֵּֽהוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb “Stand|עֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb to the tent,”|הָאֹ֑הֶל\rb* \rb he said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb “and|וְהָיָה֩\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb anyone|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb comes|יָב֜וֹא\rb* \rb and asks you,|וּשְׁאֵלֵ֗ךְ\rb* \rb ‘Is there|הֲיֵֽשׁ־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |וְאָמַ֥רְתְּ\rb* \rb here?’|פֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb say,|וְאָמַ֛ר\rb* \rb ‘No.’”|אָֽיִן׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb But as he|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb lay sleeping|נִרְדָּ֥ם\rb* \rb from exhaustion,|וַיָּ֖עַף\rb* \rb Heber’s|חֶ֠בֶר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb wife|אֵֽשֶׁת־\rb* \rb Jael|יָעֵ֣ל\rb* \rb took|וַתִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb a tent|הָאֹ֜הֶל\rb* \rb peg,|יְתַ֨ד\rb* \rb grabbed|וַתָּ֧שֶׂם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a hammer,|הַמַּקֶּ֣בֶת\rb*\rb |בְּיָדָ֗הּ\rb* \rb and went|וַתָּב֤וֹא\rb* \rb silently|בַּלָּ֔אט\rb* \rb to Sisera.|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb She drove|וַתִּתְקַ֤ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the peg|הַיָּתֵד֙\rb* \rb through his temple|בְּרַקָּת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and|וַתִּצְנַ֖ח\rb* \rb into the ground,|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb and he died.|וַיָּמֹֽת׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb When Barak|בָרָק֮\rb* \rb arrived in pursuit of|רֹדֵ֣ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Sisera,|סִֽיסְרָא֒\rb* \rb Jael|יָעֵל֙\rb* \rb went out|וַתֵּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb to greet him|לִקְרָאת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb “Come,|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and I will show you|וְאַרְאֶ֔ךָּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb are seeking.”|מְבַקֵּ֑שׁ\rb* \rb So he went in|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb with her,|אֵלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb and there|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb lay|נֹפֵ֣ל\rb* \rb Sisera|סִֽיסְרָא֙\rb* \rb dead,|מֵ֔ת\rb* \rb with a tent peg|וְהַיָּתֵ֖ד\rb* \rb through his temple.|בְּרַקָּתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb On that|הַה֔וּא\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb subdued|וַיַּכְנַ֤ע\rb* \rb Jabin|יָבִ֣ין\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Israelites.|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 24 \rb And the hand|יַ֤ד\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb grew stronger|וַתֵּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |הָל֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb and stronger|וְקָשָׁ֔ה\rb* \rb against|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb Jabin|יָבִ֣ין\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנָ֑עַן\rb* \rb until|עַ֚ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they destroyed|הִכְרִ֔יתוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb him.|יָבִ֥ין\rb*\rb |מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb*\rb |כְּנָֽעַן׃פ\rb*
\c 5
\s1 The Song of Deborah and Barak
\r \ref Exodus 15:1–21|EXO 15:1-21\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb On that|הַה֖וּא\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb Deborah|דְּבוֹרָ֔ה\rb* \rb and Barak|וּבָרָ֖ק\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Abinoam|אֲבִינֹ֑עַם\rb* \rb sang this song:|וַתָּ֣שַׁר\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb “When the princes|פְּרָעוֹת֙\rb* \rb take the lead|בִּפְרֹ֤עַ\rb* \rb in Israel,|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*
\q2 \rb when the people|עָ֑ם\rb* \rb volunteer,|בְּהִתְנַדֵּ֖ב\rb*
\q2 \rb bless|בָּרֲכ֖וּ\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb Listen,|שִׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb O kings!|מְלָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb Give ear,|הַאֲזִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb O princes!|רֹֽזְנִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb I|אָֽנֹכִ֗י\rb* \rb will sing|אָשִׁ֔ירָה\rb* \rb to the LORD;|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אָנֹכִ֣י\rb*
\q1 \rb I will sing praise|אֲזַמֵּ֕ר\rb* \rb to the LORD,|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb when You went out|בְּצֵאתְךָ֤\rb* \rb from Seir,|מִשֵּׂעִיר֙\rb*
\q2 \rb when You marched|בְּצַעְדְּךָ֙\rb* \rb from the land|מִשְּׂדֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Edom,|אֱד֔וֹם\rb*
\q1 \rb the earth|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb trembled,|רָעָ֔שָׁה\rb* \rb the heavens|שָׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb poured out rain,|נָטָ֑פוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb the clouds|עָבִ֖ים\rb* \rb poured down|נָ֥טְפוּ\rb* \rb water.|מָֽיִם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb The mountains|הָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb quaked|נָזְל֖וּ\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb the One|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb of Sinai,|סִינַ֔י\rb*
\q1 \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֕י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb In the days|בִּימֵ֞י\rb* \rb of Shamgar|שַׁמְגַּ֤ר\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Anath,|עֲנָת֙\rb*
\q2 \rb in the days|בִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jael,|יָעֵ֔ל\rb*
\q1 \rb the highways|אֳרָח֑וֹת\rb* \rb were deserted|חָדְל֖וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and the travelers|וְהֹלְכֵ֣י\rb*\rb |נְתִיב֔וֹת\rb* \rb took|יֵלְכ֕וּ\rb*\rb |אֳרָח֖וֹת\rb* \rb the byways.|עֲקַלְקַלּֽוֹת׃\rb*
