\p \v 7 \rb Now|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb cried out|זָעֲק֥וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb because of|עַ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֹד֥וֹת\rb* \rb Midian,|מִדְיָֽן׃\rb* \v 8 \rb He|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֧ח\rb* \rb them|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb a prophet,|נָבִ֖יא\rb* \rb who told|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb them,|לָהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֞י\rb* \rb brought|הֶעֱלֵ֤יתִי\rb* \rb you up out of|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb Egypt,|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |וָאֹצִ֥יא\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb out of the house|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of slavery.|עֲבָדִֽים׃\rb* \v 9 \rb I delivered|וָאַצִּ֤ל\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb out of the hands|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and|וּמִיַּ֖ד\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your oppressors.|לֹחֲצֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb I drove them out|וָאֲגָרֵ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb before you|מִפְּנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and gave|וָאֶתְּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their land.|אַרְצָֽם׃\rb* \v 10 \rb And I said|וָאֹמְרָ֣ה\rb* \rb to you:|לָכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb ‘I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb You must not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb fear|תִֽירְאוּ֙\rb*\f + \fr 6:10 \ft Or \fqa worship\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Amorites,|הָאֱמֹרִ֔י\rb* \rb in whose|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb land|בְּאַרְצָ֑ם\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb dwell.’|יוֹשְׁבִ֣ים\rb* \rb But you did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb obey Me.”|שְׁמַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |בְּקוֹלִֽי׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Call of Gideon
\p \v 11 \rb Then the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 6:11 \ft Or \fqa Angel\ft ; also in verses 12, 20, 21, and 22; corresponding pronouns may also be capitalized.\f* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֞א\rb* \rb and sat down|וַיֵּ֙שֶׁב֙\rb* \rb under|תַּ֤חַת\rb* \rb the oak|הָֽאֵלָה֙\rb*\f + \fr 6:11 \ft Or \fqa terebinth \ft or \fqa great tree\ft ; also in verse 19\f*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Ophrah|בְּעָפְרָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb belonged to Joash|לְיוֹאָ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֲבִ֣י\rb* \rb the Abiezrite,|הָֽעֶזְרִ֑י\rb* \rb where his son|בְּנ֗וֹ\rb* \rb Gideon|וְגִדְע֣וֹן\rb* \rb was threshing|חֹבֵ֤ט\rb* \rb wheat|חִטִּים֙\rb* \rb in a winepress|בַּגַּ֔ת\rb* \rb to hide it|לְהָנִ֖יס\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the Midianites.|מִדְיָֽן׃\rb* \v 12 \rb And the angel|מַלְּאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb appeared|וַיֵּרָ֥א\rb* \rb to Gideon|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb “The LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb is with you,|עִמְּךָ֖\rb* \rb O mighty man|גִּבּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb of valor.”|הֶחָֽיִל׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb “Please,|בִּ֣י\rb* \rb my Lord,”|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb Gideon|גִּדְעוֹן֙\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֤יו\rb* \rb “if the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb is|וְיֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb with us,|עִמָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb why|וְלָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb has all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|זֹ֑את\rb* \rb happened to us?|מְצָאַ֖תְנוּ\rb* \rb And where|וְאַיֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb are all|כָֽל־\rb* \rb His wonders|נִפְלְאֹתָ֡יו\rb* \rb of which|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb our fathers|אֲבוֹתֵ֜ינוּ\rb* \rb told|סִפְּרוּ־\rb* \rb us,|לָ֨נוּ\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘Has not|הֲלֹ֤א\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb brought us up|הֶעֱלָ֣נוּ\rb* \rb out of Egypt?’|מִמִּצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb But now|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has forsaken us|נְטָשָׁ֣נוּ\rb* \rb and delivered us|וַֽיִּתְּנֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּכַף־\rb* \rb of Midian.”|מִדְיָֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 6:14 \ft LXX \fqa The angel of the LORD \ft or \fqa The Angel of the LORD\ft ; also in verse 16\f* \rb turned|וַיִּ֤פֶן\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Go|לֵ֚ךְ\rb* \rb in the strength you have|בְּכֹחֲךָ֣\rb*\rb |זֶ֔ה\rb* \rb and save|וְהוֹשַׁעְתָּ֥\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb from the hand|מִכַּ֣ף\rb* \rb of Midian.|מִדְיָ֑ן\rb* \rb Am I not|הֲלֹ֖א\rb* \rb sending you?”|שְׁלַחְתִּֽיךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb “Please,|בִּ֣י\rb* \rb my Lord,”|אֲדֹנָ֔י\rb* \rb Gideon replied,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb “how|בַּמָּ֥ה\rb* \rb can I save|אוֹשִׁ֖יעַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel?|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb Indeed,|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb my clan|אַלְפִּי֙\rb* \rb is the weakest|הַדַּ֣ל\rb* \rb in Manasseh,|בִּמְנַשֶּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb and I|וְאָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb am the youngest|הַצָּעִ֖יר\rb* \rb in my father’s|אָבִֽי׃\rb* \rb house.”|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb “Surely|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I will be|אֶהְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb with you,”|עִמָּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb “and you will strike down|וְהִכִּיתָ֥\rb* \rb all the Midianites|מִדְיָ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb as one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb man.”|כְּאִ֥ישׁ\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Gideon answered,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb “If|אִם־\rb*\rb |נָ֛א\rb* \rb I have found|מָצָ֥אתִי\rb* \rb favor|חֵ֖ן\rb* \rb in Your sight,|בְּעֵינֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb give|וְעָשִׂ֤יתָ\rb* \rb me|לִּי֙\rb* \rb a sign|א֔וֹת\rb* \rb that it is You|שָׁאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb speaking|מְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb with me.|עִמִּֽי׃\rb* \v 18 \rb Please|נָ֨א\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb depart|תָמֻ֤שׁ\rb* \rb from this place|מִזֶּה֙\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb I return|בֹּאִ֣י\rb* \rb to You.|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb Let me bring|וְהֹֽצֵאתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my offering|מִנְחָתִ֔י\rb* \rb and set it|וְהִנַּחְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb before You.”|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\p \rb And the LORD said,|וַיֹּאמַ֕ר\rb* \rb “I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb will stay|אֵשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb until|עַ֥ד\rb* \rb you return.”|שׁוּבֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb So Gideon|וְגִדְע֣וֹן\rb* \rb went in|בָּ֗א\rb* \rb and prepared|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb a young goat|גְּדִֽי־\rb*\rb |עִזִּים֙\rb* \rb and unleavened bread|מַצּ֔וֹת\rb* \rb and an ephah|וְאֵיפַת־\rb* \rb of flour.|קֶ֣מַח\rb*\f + \fr 6:19 \fqa An ephah \ft is approximately 20 dry quarts or 22 liters (probably about 25.5 pounds or 11.6 kilograms of flour).\f* \rb He placed|שָׂ֣ם\rb* \rb the meat|הַבָּשָׂר֙\rb* \rb in a basket|בַּסַּ֔ל\rb* \rb and the broth|וְהַמָּרַ֖ק\rb*\rb |שָׂ֣ם\rb* \rb in a pot|בַּפָּר֑וּר\rb* \rb and brought them out|וַיּוֹצֵ֥א\rb* \rb to present|וַיַּגַּֽשׁ׃ס\rb* \rb to Him|אֵלָ֛יו\rb* \rb under|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the oak.|הָאֵלָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb And the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb “Take|קַ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the meat|הַבָּשָׂ֤ר\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the unleavened bread,|הַמַּצּוֹת֙\rb* \rb lay them|וְהַנַּח֙\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַלָּ֔ז\rb* \rb rock,|הַסֶּ֣לַע\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb pour out|שְׁפ֑וֹךְ\rb* \rb the broth.”|הַמָּרַ֖ק\rb* \rb And Gideon did|וַיַּ֖עַשׂ\rb* \rb so.|כֵּֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Then the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb extended|וַיִּשְׁלַ֞ח\rb* \rb the tip|קְצֵ֤ה\rb* \rb of the staff|הַמִּשְׁעֶ֙נֶת֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was in his hand|בְּיָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb and touched|וַיִּגַּ֥ע\rb* \rb the meat|בַּבָּשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb and the unleavened bread.|וּבַמַּצּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb And fire|הָאֵ֜שׁ\rb* \rb flared|וַתַּ֨עַל\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the rock|הַצּ֗וּר\rb* \rb and consumed|וַתֹּ֤אכַל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the meat|הַבָּשָׂר֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the unleavened bread.|הַמַּצּ֔וֹת\rb* \rb Then the angel|וּמַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb vanished|הָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb from his sight.|מֵעֵינָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb When Gideon|גִּדְע֔וֹן\rb* \rb realized|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it was|ה֑וּאס\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb he|גִּדְע֗וֹן\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Oh no,|אֲהָהּ֙\rb* \rb Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD!|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb I have seen|רָאִ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb face|פָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb face!”|פָּנִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|ל֧וֹ\rb* \rb “Peace be|שָׁל֥וֹם\rb* \rb with you.|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid,|תִּירָ֑א\rb* \rb for you will not|לֹ֖א\rb* \rb die.”|תָּמֽוּת׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb So Gideon|גִּדְע֤וֹן\rb* \rb built|וַיִּבֶן֩\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֨ם\rb* \rb and called|וַיִּקְרָא־\rb* \rb it|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb Is Peace.|שָׁל֑וֹם\rb*\f + \fr 6:24 \ft Hebrew \fqa YHWH Shalom\f* \rb To|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb it stands|עוֹדֶ֕נּוּ\rb* \rb in Ophrah|בְּעָפְרָ֖ת\rb*\rb |אֲבִ֥י\rb* \rb of the Abiezrites.|הָעֶזְרִֽי׃פ\rb*
\s1 Gideon Destroys Baal’s Altar
\p \v 25 \rb |וַיְהִי֮\rb* \rb On that very|הַהוּא֒\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to Gideon,|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb “Take|קַ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your father’s|לְאָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb young bull|פַּר־\rb*\rb |הַשּׁוֹר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb and a second|הַשֵּׁנִ֖י\rb* \rb bull|וּפַ֥ר\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb years old,|שָׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb tear down|וְהָרַסְתָּ֗\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your father’s|לְאָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb altar|מִזְבַּ֤ח\rb* \rb to Baal,|הַבַּ֙עַל֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and cut down|תִּכְרֹֽת׃\rb* \rb the Asherah pole|הָאֲשֵׁרָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb beside it.|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \v 26 \rb Then build|וּבָנִ֨יתָ\rb* \rb a proper|בַּמַּֽעֲרָכָ֑ה\rb* \rb altar|מִזְבֵּ֜חַ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb on|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb the top|רֹ֧אשׁ\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb stronghold.|הַמָּע֛וֹז\rb* \rb And with the wood|בַּעֲצֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Asherah pole|הָאֲשֵׁרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you cut down,|תִּכְרֹֽת׃\rb* \rb take|וְלָֽקַחְתָּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb bull|הַפָּ֣ר\rb* \rb and offer|וְהַעֲלִ֣יתָ\rb* \rb it as a burnt offering.”|עוֹלָ֔ה\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb So Gideon|גִּדְע֜וֹן\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb of his servants|מֵֽעֲבָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb and did|וַיַּ֕עַשׂ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֡י\rb* \rb had told him.|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb But because|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he was too afraid|יָרֵא֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of his father’s|אָבִ֜יו\rb* \rb household|בֵּ֨ית\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of the city,|הָעִ֛יר\rb* \rb he did it|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb by night|לָֽיְלָה׃\rb* \rb rather than|מֵעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb in the daytime.|יוֹמָ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb When the men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb got up|וַיַּשְׁכִּ֜ימוּ\rb* \rb in the morning,|בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb there was|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb Baal’s|הַבַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb torn down,|נֻתַּץ֙\rb* \rb with the Asherah pole|וְהָאֲשֵׁרָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb cut down|כֹּרָ֑תָה\rb* \rb beside it|עָלָ֖יו\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb bull|הַפָּ֣ר\rb* \rb offered up|הֹֽעֲלָ֔ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the newly built|הַבָּנֽוּי׃\rb* \rb altar.|הַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \v 29 \rb “Who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb did|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb this?”|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb they said|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb another.|רֵעֵ֔הוּ\rb*
\p \rb And after they had investigated thoroughly,|וַֽיִּדְרְשׁוּ֙\rb*\rb |וַיְבַקְשׁ֔וּ\rb* \rb they were told,|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “Gideon|גִּדְעוֹן֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Joash|יוֹאָ֔שׁ\rb* \rb did|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb it.”|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb Then the men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמְר֜וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joash,|יוֹאָ֔שׁ\rb* \rb “Bring out|הוֹצֵ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your son.|בִּנְךָ֖\rb* \rb He must die,|וְיָמֹ֑ת\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb he has torn down|נָתַץ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Baal’s|הַבַּ֔עַל\rb*\rb |וְכִ֥י\rb* \rb altar|מִזְבַּ֣ח\rb* \rb and cut down|כָרַ֖ת\rb* \rb the Asherah pole|הָאֲשֵׁרָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb beside it.”|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb But Joash|יוֹאָ֡שׁ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to all|לְכֹל֩\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb stood|עָמְד֨וּ\rb* \rb against him,|עָלָ֜יו\rb* \rb “Are you|הַאַתֶּ֣ם׀\rb* \rb contending|תְּרִיב֣וּן\rb* \rb for Baal?|לַבַּ֗עַל\rb* \rb Are you|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb trying to save him?|תּוֹשִׁיע֣וּן\rb*\rb |אוֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb Whoever|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb pleads his case|יָרִ֥יב\rb*\rb |ל֛וֹ\rb* \rb will be put to death|יוּמַ֖ת\rb* \rb by|עַד־\rb* \rb morning!|הַבֹּ֑קֶר\rb* \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb Baal|הוּא֙\rb* \rb is a god,|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb let him contend|יָ֣רֶב\rb* \rb for himself|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb with|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the one who has torn down|נָתַ֖ץ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb his altar.”|מִזְבְּחֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 32 \rb So on that day|בַיּוֹם־\rb*\rb |הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb Gideon was called|וַיִּקְרָא־\rb*\rb |ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb Jerubbaal,|יְרֻבַּ֣עַל\rb*\f + \fr 6:32 \fqa Jerubbaal \ft probably means \fqa let Baal contend\ft .\f* \rb that is to say,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Let Baal|הַבַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb contend|יָ֤רֶב\rb* \rb with him,”|בּוֹ֙\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he had torn down|נָתַ֖ץ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Baal’s altar.|מִזְבְּחֽוֹ׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Sign of the Fleece
\p \v 33 \rb Then all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Midianites,|מִדְיָ֧ן\rb* \rb Amalekites,|וַעֲמָלֵ֛ק\rb* \rb and other people|וּבְנֵי־\rb* \rb of the east|קֶ֖דֶם\rb* \rb gathered|נֶאֶסְפ֣וּ\rb* \rb together,|יַחְדָּ֑ו\rb* \rb crossed over the Jordan,|וַיַּעַבְר֥וּ\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּעֵ֥מֶק\rb* \rb of Jezreel.|יִזְרְעֶֽאל׃\rb*
\p \v 34 \rb So the Spirit|וְר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came upon|לָבְשָׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Gideon,|גִּדְע֑וֹן\rb* \rb who blew|וַיִּתְקַע֙\rb* \rb the ram’s horn|בַּשּׁוֹפָ֔ר\rb* \rb and rallied|וַיִזָּעֵ֥ק\rb* \rb the Abiezrites|אֲבִיעֶ֖זֶר\rb* \rb behind him.|אַחֲרָֽיו׃\rb* \v 35 \rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb Calling them|וַיִזָּעֵ֥ק\rb* \rb to arms,|אַחֲרָ֑יו\rb* \rb Gideon sent|שָׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb messengers|וּמַלְאָכִים֙\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb Manasseh,|מְנַשֶּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb as well as|גַּם־\rb*\rb |שָׁלַ֗ח\rb*\rb |וּמַלְאָכִ֣ים\rb* \rb Asher,|בְּאָשֵׁ֤ר\rb* \rb Zebulun,|וּבִזְבֻלוּן֙\rb* \rb and Naphtali,|וּבְנַפְתָּלִ֔י\rb* \rb so that they came up|וַֽיַּעֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb to meet him.|לִקְרָאתָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 36 \rb Then Gideon|גִּדְע֖וֹן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God,|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb “If|אִם־\rb*\rb |יֶשְׁךָ֞\rb* \rb You are going to save|מוֹשִׁ֧יעַ\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb by my hand,|בְּיָדִ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb You have said,|דִּבַּֽרְתָּ׃\rb* \v 37 \rb then behold,|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֗י\rb* \rb will place|מַצִּ֛יג\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a fleece|גִּזַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of wool|הַצֶּ֖מֶר\rb* \rb on the threshing floor.|בַּגֹּ֑רֶן\rb* \rb If|אִ֡ם\rb* \rb there is|יִהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb dew|טַל֩\rb* \rb only|לְבַדָּ֗הּ\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the fleece|הַגִּזָּ֜ה\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb is dry,|חֹ֔רֶב\rb* \rb then I will know|וְיָדַעְתִּ֗י\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb You are going to save|תוֹשִׁ֧יעַ\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb by my hand,|בְּיָדִ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb You have said.”|דִּבַּֽרְתָּ׃\rb*
\p \v 38 \rb And that is what|כֵ֕ן\rb* \rb happened.|וַיְהִי־\rb* \rb When Gideon arose|וַיַּשְׁכֵּם֙\rb* \rb the next morning,|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֔ת\rb* \rb he squeezed|וַיָּ֖זַר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the fleece|הַגִּזָּ֑ה\rb* \rb and wrung|וַיִּ֤מֶץ\rb* \rb out|מִן־\rb* \rb the dew—|טַל֙\rb*\rb |הַגִּזָּ֔ה\rb* \rb |מְל֥וֹא\rb* \rb a bowlful|הַסֵּ֖פֶל\rb* \rb of water.|מָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 39 \rb Then Gideon|גִּדְעוֹן֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb God,|הָ֣אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be angry|יִ֤חַר\rb*\rb |אַפְּךָ֙\rb* \rb with me;|בִּ֔י\rb* \rb let me speak|וַאֲדַבְּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb one more time.|אַ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |הַפָּ֑עַם\rb* \rb Please allow me|נָּא־\rb*\rb |רַק־\rb* \rb one more|הַפַּ֙עַם֙\rb* \rb test|אֲנַסֶּ֤ה\rb* \rb with the fleece.|בַּגִּזָּ֔ה\rb* \rb This time|נָ֨א\rb* \rb let it be|יְהִי־\rb* \rb dry,|חֹ֤רֶב\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַגִּזָּה֙\rb*\rb |לְבַדָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb and the ground|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb covered|כָּל־\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb with dew.”|טָּֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 40 \rb And that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb* \rb so.|כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb Only|לְבַדָּ֔הּ\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb the fleece|הַגִּזָּה֙\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִי־\rb* \rb dry,|חֹ֤רֶב\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb and dew|טָֽל׃פ\rb* \rb covered|הָ֥יָה\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb the ground.|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*
\c 7
\s1 Gideon’s Army of Three Hundred
\p \v 1 \rb Early in the morning|וַיַּשְׁכֵּ֨ם\rb* \rb Jerubbaal|יְרֻבַּ֜עַל\rb*\f + \fr 7:1 \fqa Jerubbaal \ft is another name for \fqa Gideon \ft and probably means \fqa let Baal contend\ft ; see \ref Judges 6:32|JDG 6:32\ref*.\f* \rb (that is,|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb Gideon)|גִדְע֗וֹן\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the men|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb beside|עַל־\rb*\rb |עֵ֣ין\rb* \rb the spring of Harod.|חֲרֹ֑ד\rb* \rb And the camp|וּמַחֲנֵ֤ה\rb* \rb of Midian|מִדְיָן֙\rb* \rb was|הָיָה־\rb* \rb north|מִצָּפ֔וֹן\rb* \rb of them|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb in the valley|בָּעֵֽמֶק׃\rb* \rb near the hill|מִגִּבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Moreh.|הַמּוֹרֶ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gideon,|גִּדְע֔וֹן\rb* \rb “You have|אִתָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb too many|רַ֗ב\rb* \rb men|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb for Me to deliver|מִתִּתִּ֥י\rb* \rb Midian|מִדְיָ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into their hands,|בְּיָדָ֑ם\rb* \rb lest|פֶּן־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb glorify themselves|יִתְפָּאֵ֨ר\rb* \rb over Me,|עָלַ֤י\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘My own hand|יָדִ֖י\rb* \rb has saved|הוֹשִׁ֥יעָה\rb* \rb me.’|לִּֽי׃\rb* \v 3 \rb Now,|נָ֜א\rb* \rb therefore,|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb proclaim|קְרָ֨א\rb* \rb in the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the men:|הָעָם֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘Whoever|מִֽי־\rb* \rb is fearful|יָרֵ֣א\rb* \rb and trembling|וְחָרֵ֔ד\rb* \rb may turn back|יָשֹׁ֥ב\rb* \rb and leave|וְיִצְפֹּ֖ר\rb* \rb Mount|מֵהַ֣ר\rb* \rb Gilead.’”|הַגִּלְעָ֑ד\rb*
\p \rb So twenty-two|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֔לֶף\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb of them|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb turned back,|וַיָּ֣שָׁב\rb* \rb but ten|וַעֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb remained.|נִשְׁאָֽרוּ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gideon,|גִּדְע֗וֹן\rb* \rb “There are still|עוֹד֮\rb* \rb too many|רָב֒\rb* \rb men.|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb Take them down|הוֹרֵ֤ד\rb*\rb |אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the water,|הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb and I will sift them|וְאֶצְרְפֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb for you|לְךָ֖\rb* \rb there.|שָׁ֑ם\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֡ה\rb* \rb If|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb I say|אֹמַ֨ר\rb* \rb to you,|אֵלֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb ‘This one|זֶ֣ה׀\rb* \rb shall go|יֵלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb with you,’|אִתָּ֗ךְ\rb* \rb he shall go.|יֵלֵ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |אִתָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb But|וְכֹ֨ל\rb* \rb if|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I say,|אֹמַ֜ר\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb ‘This one|זֶ֚ה\rb* \rb shall not|לֹא־\rb* \rb go|יֵלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb with you,’|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb he|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb shall not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb go.”|יֵלֵֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb So Gideon brought the men|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb down|וַיּ֥וֹרֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the water,|הַמָּ֑יִםס\rb* \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb him,|גִּדְע֗וֹן\rb* \rb “Separate|תַּצִּ֤יג\rb*\rb |אוֹתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |לְבָ֔ד\rb* \rb those|כֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb lap|יָלֹק֩\rb* \rb the water|הַמַּ֜יִם\rb* \rb with their tongues|בִּלְשׁוֹנ֨וֹ\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb like|כַּאֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb*\rb |יָלֹ֣ק\rb* \rb a dog|הַכֶּ֗לֶב\rb* \rb from those|וְכֹ֛ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb kneel|יִכְרַ֥ע\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |בִּרְכָּ֖יו\rb* \rb to drink.”|לִשְׁתּֽוֹת׃\rb* \v 6 \rb And the number|מִסְפַּ֞ר\rb* \rb of those who lapped the water|הַֽמֲלַקְקִ֤ים\rb* \rb with their hands|בְּיָדָם֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their mouths|פִּיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb men;|אִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb all|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the others|יֶ֣תֶר\rb*\rb |הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb knelt|כָּרְע֥וּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |בִּרְכֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to drink.|לִשְׁתּ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |מָֽיִם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gideon,|גִּדְע֗וֹן\rb* \rb “With the three|בִּשְׁלֹשׁ֩\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֨וֹת\rb* \rb men|הָאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb who lapped the water|הַֽמֲלַקְקִים֙\rb* \rb I will save|אוֹשִׁ֣יעַ\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and deliver|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb the Midianites|מִדְיָ֖ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into your hand.|בְּיָדֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb But all the others|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb are to go|יֵלְכ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb home.”|לִמְקֹמֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb So Gideon sent|שִׁלַּח֙\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb the rest of|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|אִ֤ישׁ\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb to their tents|לְאֹֽהָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb but kept|הֶֽחֱזִ֑יק\rb* \rb the three|וּבִשְׁלֹשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֥וֹת\rb* \rb men,|הָאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb who took|וַיִּקְח֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb charge of|בְּיָדָ֜ם\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the provisions|צֵדָה֩\rb* \rb and rams’ horns|שׁוֹפְרֹֽתֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb of the others.|הָעָ֨ם\rb* \rb And|וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb the camp|וּמַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Midian|מִדְיָ֔ן\rb* \rb lay|הָ֥יָה\rb* \rb below|מִתַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the valley.|בָּעֵֽמֶק׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Sword of Gideon
\p \v 9 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb That|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to Gideon,|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb “Get up|ק֖וּם\rb* \rb and go down|רֵ֣ד\rb* \rb against the camp,|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I have delivered it|נְתַתִּ֖יו\rb* \rb into your hand.|בְּיָדֶֽךָ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb are afraid|יָרֵ֥א\rb* \rb to do so,|לָרֶ֑דֶת\rb* \rb then go down|רֵ֥ד\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb*\rb |אַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb with your servant|נַעַרְךָ֖\rb* \rb Purah|וּפֻרָ֥ה\rb* \v 11 \rb and listen|וְשָֽׁמַעְתָּ֙\rb* \rb to what|מַה־\rb* \rb they are saying.|יְדַבֵּ֔רוּ\rb* \rb Then|וְאַחַר֙\rb* \rb your hands|יָדֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb will be strengthened|תֶּחֱזַ֣קְנָה\rb* \rb to attack|וְיָרַדְתָּ֖\rb* \rb the camp.”|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb* \rb So he|הוּא֙\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֤רֶד\rb* \rb with Purah|וּפֻרָ֣ה\rb* \rb his servant|נַעֲר֔וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the outposts|קְצֵ֥ה\rb* \rb where armed men|הַחֲמֻשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb were guarding|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the camp.|בַּֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Now the Midianites,|וּמִדְיָ֨ן\rb* \rb Amalekites,|וַעֲמָלֵ֤ק\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the other people|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb of the east|קֶ֙דֶם֙\rb* \rb had settled|נֹפְלִ֣ים\rb* \rb in the valley|בָּעֵ֔מֶק\rb* \rb like a swarm of|לָרֹ֑ב\rb* \rb locusts,|כָּאַרְבֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb and their camels|וְלִגְמַלֵּיהֶם֙\rb* \rb were as countless|אֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |מִסְפָּ֔ר\rb* \rb as the sand|כַּח֛וֹל\rb* \rb on|שֶׁעַל־\rb* \rb the seashore.|שְׂפַ֥ת\rb*\rb |הַיָּ֖ם\rb*\rb |לָרֹֽב׃\rb* \v 13 \rb And as Gideon|גִדְע֔וֹן\rb* \rb arrived,|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb a man|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb was telling|מְסַפֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb his friend|לְרֵעֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb about a dream.|חֲל֑וֹם\rb* \rb “Behold,|הִנֵּ֧ה\rb* \rb I had a dream,”|חֲל֣וֹם\rb*\rb |חָלַ֗מְתִּי\rb* \rb he said,|וַיֹּ֜אמֶר\rb* \rb “and I saw|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb a loaf|צְלוֹל\rb* \rb of barley|שְׂעֹרִים֙\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֤חֶם\rb* \rb come|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb tumbling|מִתְהַפֵּךְ֙\rb* \rb into the Midianite|מִדְיָ֔ן\rb* \rb camp.|בְּמַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb It struck|וַיַּכֵּ֧הוּ\rb* \rb the tent|הָ֠אֹהֶל\rb* \rb so hard that|וַיִּפֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb the tent|הָאֹֽהֶל׃\rb* \rb overturned|וַיַּהַפְכֵ֥הוּ\rb*\rb |לְמַ֖עְלָה\rb* \rb and collapsed.”|וְנָפַ֥ל\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb His friend|רֵעֵ֤הוּ\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb replied:|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb* \rb “This|זֹ֔את\rb* \rb is nothing|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb less than|בִּלְתִּ֗י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֛רֶב\rb* \rb of Gideon|גִּדְע֥וֹן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Joash,|יוֹאָ֖שׁ\rb* \rb the Israelite.|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb has delivered|נָתַ֤ן\rb* \rb Midian|מִדְיָ֖ן\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶֽה׃פ\rb* \rb into his hand.”|בְּיָד֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\s1 Gideon Defeats Midian
\p \v 15 \rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb When Gideon|גִּדְע֜וֹן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|כִשְׁמֹ֨עַ\rb*\rb |מִסְפַּ֧ר\rb* \rb the dream|הַחֲל֛וֹם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and its interpretation,|שִׁבְר֖וֹ\rb* \rb he bowed in worship.|וַיִּשְׁתָּ֑חוּ\rb* \rb He returned|וַיָּ֙שָׁב֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Get up,|ק֔וּמוּ\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has delivered|נָתַ֧ן\rb* \rb the camp|מַחֲנֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of Midian|מִדְיָֽן׃\rb* \rb into your hand.”|בְּיֶדְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 16 \rb And he divided|וַיַּ֛חַץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the three|שְׁלֹשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֥וֹת\rb* \rb men|הָאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb into three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb companies|רָאשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb and gave|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb each man|כֻּלָּם֙\rb* \rb a ram’s horn|שׁוֹפָר֤וֹת\rb* \rb in one hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb and a large|רֵקִ֔ים\rb* \rb jar in the other,|וְכַדִּ֣ים\rb* \rb containing|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb a torch.|וְלַפִּדִ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 7:16 \ft Literally \fqa and put rams’ horns and empty jars—large jars with torches inside—into the hand of all\f*\rb |הַכַּדִּֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb “Watch me|תִרְא֖וּ\rb* \rb and do|תַּעֲשׂ֑וּ\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb as I do,”|וְכֵ֣ן\rb* \rb Gideon said.|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֥נִּי\rb* \rb “When I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb come|בָא֙\rb* \rb to the outskirts|בִּקְצֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the camp,|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb do|אֶעֱשֶׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb exactly as|כַאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I do.|תַּעֲשֽׂוּן׃\rb* \v 18 \rb When I|אָנֹכִ֖י\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb who are|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֑י\rb* \rb blow|וְתָקַעְתִּי֙\rb* \rb our horns,|בַּשּׁוֹפָ֔ר\rb* \rb then you|אַתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb are also|גַּם־\rb* \rb to blow|וּתְקַעְתֶּ֨ם\rb* \rb your horns|בַּשּׁוֹפָר֜וֹת\rb* \rb from all|כָּל־\rb* \rb around|סְבִיבוֹת֙\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb and shout,|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb ‘For the LORD|לַיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb and for Gideon!’”|וּלְגִדְעֽוֹן׃פ\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Gideon|גִ֠דְעוֹן\rb* \rb and the hundred|וּמֵאָה־\rb* \rb men|אִ֨ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֜וֹ\rb* \rb reached|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb the outskirts|בִּקְצֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֗ה\rb* \rb at the beginning|רֹ֚אשׁ\rb* \rb of the middle|הַתִּֽיכוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb watch,|הָאַשְׁמֹ֣רֶת\rb* \rb just after|אַ֛ךְ\rb* \rb the changing|הָקֵ֥ם\rb*\rb |הֵקִ֖ימוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the guard.|הַשֹּֽׁמְרִ֑ים\rb* \rb They blew|וַֽיִּתְקְעוּ֙\rb* \rb their horns|בַּשּׁ֣וֹפָר֔וֹת\rb* \rb and broke|וְנָפ֥וֹץ\rb* \rb the jars|הַכַּדִּ֖ים\rb* \rb that were|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in their hands.|בְּיָדָֽם׃\rb* \v 20 \rb The three|שְׁלֹ֨שֶׁת\rb* \rb companies|הָרָאשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb blew|וַֽ֠יִּתְקְעוּ\rb* \rb their horns|בַּשּֽׁוֹפָרוֹת֮\rb* \rb and shattered|וַיִּשְׁבְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb their jars.|הַכַּדִּים֒\rb* \rb Holding|וַיַּחֲזִ֤יקוּ\rb* \rb the torches|בַּלַּפִּדִ֔ים\rb* \rb in their left|שְׂמאוֹלָם֙\rb* \rb hands|בְיַד־\rb* \rb and the horns|הַשּׁוֹפָר֖וֹת\rb*\rb |לִתְק֑וֹעַ\rb* \rb in their right|יְמִינָ֔ם\rb* \rb hands,|וּבְיַ֨ד־\rb* \rb they shouted,|וַֽיִּקְרְא֔וּ\rb* \rb “A sword|חֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and for Gideon!”|וּלְגִדְעֽוֹן׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Each Israelite|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb took|וַיַּֽעַמְדוּ֙\rb* \rb his position|תַּחְתָּ֔יו\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֖יב\rb* \rb the camp,|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb* \rb and the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb Midianite army|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֛ה\rb* \rb fled,|וַיָּ֧רָץ\rb* \rb crying out|וַיָּרִ֖יעוּ\rb* \rb as they ran.|וַיָּנִיסוּ׃\rb* \v 22 \rb And when the three|שְׁלֹשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb rams’ horns|הַשּׁוֹפָרוֹת֒\rb* \rb sounded,|וַֽיִּתְקְעוּ֮\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb set|וַיָּ֣שֶׂם\rb* \rb all the men|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb in the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֑ה\rb* \rb against one another|בְּרֵעֵ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb with their swords.|חֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb The army|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֜ה\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּ֨נָס\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb*\rb |בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb Beth-shittah|הַשִּׁטָּה֙\rb* \rb toward Zererah|צְֽרֵרָ֔תָה\rb*\f + \fr 7:22 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts \fqa Zeredah\f* \rb as|עַ֛ד\rb* \rb far as the border|שְׂפַת־\rb*\rb |אָבֵ֥ל\rb* \rb of Abel-meholah|מְחוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb* \rb Tabbath.|טַבָּֽת׃\rb* \v 23 \rb Then the men|אִֽישׁ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb were called out|וַיִּצָּעֵ֧ק\rb* \rb from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb Naphtali,|מִנַּפְתָּלִ֥י\rb* \rb Asher,|אָשֵׁ֖ר\rb* \rb and|וּמִן־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Manasseh,|מְנַשֶּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb and they pursued|וַֽיִּרְדְּפ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the Midianites.|מִדְיָֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb Gideon|גִּדְעוֹן֩\rb* \rb sent|שָׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb messengers|וּמַלְאָכִ֡ים\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the hill country|הַ֨ר\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֜יִם\rb* \rb to say,|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb “Come down|רְד֞וּ\rb* \rb against|לִקְרַ֤את\rb* \rb the Midianites|מִדְיָן֙\rb* \rb and seize|וְלִכְד֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the waters|הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb ahead of them|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb as far as|עַ֛ד\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb Beth-barah.”|בָּרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb So all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb were called out,|וַיִּצָּעֵ֞ק\rb* \rb and they captured|וַיִּלְכְּד֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the waters|הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb* \rb as far as|עַ֛ד\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb Beth-barah.|בָּרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \v 25 \rb They also captured|וַֽיִּלְכְּד֡וּ\rb* \rb Oreb|עֹרֵ֣ב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Zeeb,|זְאֵ֗ב\rb* \rb the two|שְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb princes|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Midian;|מִדְיָ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and they killed|וַיַּהַרְג֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Oreb|עוֹרֵ֤ב\rb* \rb at the rock|בְּצוּר־\rb* \rb of Oreb|עוֹרֵב֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Zeeb|זְאֵב֙\rb*\rb |הָרְג֣וּ\rb* \rb at the winepress|בְיֶֽקֶב־\rb* \rb of Zeeb.|זְאֵ֔ב\rb* \rb So they pursued|וַֽיִּרְדְּפ֖וּ\rb* \rb the Midianites|מִדְיָ֑ן\rb* \rb and brought|הֵבִ֙יאוּ֙\rb* \rb the heads|וְרֹאשׁ־\rb* \rb of Oreb|עֹרֵ֣ב\rb* \rb and Zeeb|וּזְאֵ֔ב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gideon|גִּדְע֔וֹן\rb* \rb on the other side|מֵעֵ֖בֶר\rb* \rb of the Jordan.|לַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb*
\c 8
\s1 Gideon Defeats Zebah and Zalmunna
\p \v 1 \rb Then the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֨וּ\rb* \rb to Gideon,|אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb “Why|מָֽה־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֤ר\rb* \rb have you done|עָשִׂ֣יתָ\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb to us?|לָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb Why did you fail|לְבִלְתִּי֙\rb* \rb to call|קְרֹ֣אות\rb* \rb us|לָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb when|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you went|הָלַ֖כְתָּ\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֣ם\rb* \rb against Midian?”|בְּמִדְיָ֑ן\rb* \rb And they contended|וַיְרִיב֥וּן\rb* \rb with him violently.|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |בְּחָזְקָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb But Gideon answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb them,|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb “Now|עַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb what|מֶה־\rb* \rb have I accomplished|עָשִׂ֥יתִי\rb* \rb compared to you?|כָּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb Are not|הֲל֗וֹא\rb* \rb the gleanings|עֹלְל֥וֹת\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb better|ט֛וֹב\rb* \rb than the grape harvest|מִבְצִ֥יר\rb* \rb of Abiezer?|אֲבִיעֶֽזֶר׃\rb* \v 3 \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has delivered|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb Oreb|עֹרֵ֣ב\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Zeeb,|זְאֵ֔ב\rb* \rb the two princes|שָׂרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Midian,|מִדְיָן֙\rb* \rb into your hand.|בְּיֶדְכֶם֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb What|וּמַה־\rb* \rb was I able|יָּכֹ֖לְתִּי\rb* \rb to do|עֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb compared to you?”|כָּכֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |אָ֗ז\rb* \rb When he had said|בְּדַבְּר֖וֹ\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb this,|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb their anger|רוּחָם֙\rb*\f + \fr 8:3 \ft Or \fqa their spirit\f* \rb against him|מֵֽעָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb subsided.|רָפְתָ֤ה\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Then Gideon|גִדְע֖וֹן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb and his|אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb three|וּשְׁלֹשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֤וֹת\rb* \rb men|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑נָה\rb* \rb and crossed it,|עֹבֵ֣ר\rb*\rb |ה֗וּא\rb* \rb exhausted|עֲיֵפִ֖ים\rb* \rb yet still in pursuit.|וְרֹדְפִֽים׃\rb* \v 5 \rb So Gideon said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to the men|לְאַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of Succoth,|סֻכּ֔וֹת\rb* \rb “Please|נָא֙\rb* \rb give|תְּנוּ־\rb* \rb my troops|לָעָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |בְּרַגְלָ֑י\rb* \rb some|כִּכְּר֣וֹת\rb* \rb bread,|לֶ֔חֶם\rb* \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb they|הֵ֔ם\rb* \rb are exhausted,|עֲיֵפִ֣ים\rb* \rb and I|וְאָנֹכִ֗י\rb* \rb am still pursuing|רֹדֵ֛ף\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֛י\rb* \rb Zebah|זֶ֥בַח\rb* \rb and Zalmunna,|וְצַלְמֻנָּ֖ע\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Midian.”|מִדְיָֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb But the leaders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Succoth|סֻכּ֔וֹת\rb* \rb asked,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “Are the hands|הֲ֠כַף\rb* \rb of Zebah|זֶ֧בַח\rb* \rb and Zalmunna|וְצַלְמֻנָּ֛ע\rb* \rb already|עַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb in your possession,|בְּיָדֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we should give|נִתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb bread|לָֽחֶם׃\rb* \rb to your army?”|לִֽצְבָאֲךָ֖\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb “Very well,”|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb Gideon|גִּדְע֔וֹן\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “when the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has delivered|בְּתֵ֧ת\rb* \rb Zebah|זֶ֥בַח\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Zalmunna|צַלְמֻנָּ֖ע\rb* \rb into my hand,|בְּיָדִ֑י\rb* \rb I will tear|וְדַשְׁתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your flesh|בְּשַׂרְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the thorns|קוֹצֵ֥י\rb* \rb and briers|הַֽבַּרְקֳנִֽים׃\rb* \rb of the wilderness!”|הַמִּדְבָּ֖ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb From there|מִשָּׁם֙\rb* \rb he went up|וַיַּ֤עַל\rb* \rb to Penuel|פְּנוּאֵ֔ל\rb*\f + \fr 8:8 \fqa Penuel \ft is a variant of \fqa Peniel\ft ; also in verses 9 and 17; see \ref Genesis 32:30|GEN 32:30\ref*.\f* \rb and asked|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb the same|כָּזֹ֑את\rb* \rb from them,|אֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb but the men|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of Penuel|פְנוּאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb gave the same response|וַיַּעֲנ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אוֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |עָנ֖וּ\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of Succoth.|סֻכּֽוֹת׃\rb* \v 9 \rb So Gideon|גַּם־\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb* \rb the men|לְאַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of Penuel,|פְנוּאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “When I return|בְּשׁוּבִ֣י\rb* \rb in triumph,|בְשָׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb I will tear down|אֶתֹּ֖ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb tower!”|הַמִּגְדָּ֥ל\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Now Zebah|וְזֶ֨בַח\rb* \rb and Zalmunna|וְצַלְמֻנָּ֜ע\rb* \rb were in Karkor|בַּקַּרְקֹ֗ר\rb* \rb with|עִמָּם֙\rb* \rb their army|וּמַחֲנֵיהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb of about fifteen|כַּחֲמֵ֤שֶׁת\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb thousand men—|אֶ֔לֶף\rb*  \rb all|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb that were left|הַנּ֣וֹתָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb of|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the armies|מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the people|בְנֵי־\rb* \rb of the east.|קֶ֑דֶם\rb* \rb A hundred|מֵאָ֨ה\rb* \rb and twenty|וְעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֛לֶף\rb* \rb swordsmen|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |שֹׁ֥לֵֽף\rb*\rb |חָֽרֶב׃\rb* \rb had already fallen.|וְהַנֹּ֣פְלִ֔ים\rb* \v 11 \rb And Gideon|גִּדְע֗וֹן\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb by way of the caravan|הַשְּׁכוּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בָֽאֳהָלִ֔ים\rb* \rb route|דֶּ֚רֶךְ\rb* \rb east|מִקֶּ֥דֶם\rb* \rb of Nobah|לְנֹ֖בַח\rb* \rb and Jogbehah,|וְיָגְבֳּהָ֑ה\rb* \rb and he attacked|וַיַּךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their army,|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb taking them|וְהַֽמַּחֲנֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |הָ֥יָה\rb* \rb by surprise.|בֶֽטַח׃\rb* \v 12 \rb When Zebah|זֶ֚בַח\rb* \rb and Zalmunna|וְצַלְמֻנָּ֔ע\rb* \rb fled,|וַיָּנ֗וּסוּ\rb* \rb Gideon pursued|וַיִּרְדֹּ֖ף\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and captured|וַיִּלְכֹּ֞ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these two|שְׁנֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Midian,|מִדְיָ֗ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |זֶ֙בַח֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |צַלְמֻנָּ֔ע\rb* \rb routing|הֶחֱרִֽיד׃\rb* \rb their entire|וְכָל־\rb* \rb army.|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb After this, Gideon|גִּדְע֥וֹן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Joash|יוֹאָ֖שׁ\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֛שָׁב\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb along the Ascent of|מִֽלְמַעֲלֵ֖ה\rb* \rb Heres.|הֶחָֽרֶס׃\rb* \v 14 \rb There he captured|וַיִּלְכָּד־\rb* \rb a young man|נַ֛עַר\rb*\rb |מֵאַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of Succoth|סֻכּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb and interrogated him.|וַיִּשְׁאָלֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb The young man wrote down|וַיִּכְתֹּ֨ב\rb* \rb for him|אֵלָ֜יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the names of the seventy-seven|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְשִׁבְעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb leaders|שָׂרֵ֤י\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb elders|זְקֵנֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb of Succoth.|סֻכּוֹת֙\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb And Gideon went|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of Succoth|סֻכּ֔וֹת\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “Here|הִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb are Zebah|זֶ֣בַח\rb* \rb and Zalmunna,|וְצַלְמֻנָּ֑ע\rb* \rb about whom|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb you taunted|חֵרַפְתֶּ֨ם\rb* \rb me,|אוֹתִ֜י\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb ‘Are the hands|הֲ֠כַף\rb* \rb of Zebah|זֶ֣בַח\rb* \rb and Zalmunna|וְצַלְמֻנָּ֤ע\rb* \rb already|עַתָּה֙\rb* \rb in your possession,|בְּיָדֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb we should give|נִתֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb bread|לָֽחֶם׃\rb* \rb to your weary|הַיְּעֵפִ֖ים\rb* \rb men?’”|לַאֲנָשֶׁ֥יךָ\rb* \v 16 \rb Then he took|וַיִּקַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the city,|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb and using|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the thorns|קוֹצֵ֥י\rb* \rb and briers|הַֽבַּרְקֳנִ֑ים\rb* \rb of the wilderness,|הַמִּדְבָּ֖ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |בָּהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb he disciplined|וַיֹּ֣דַע\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of Succoth.|סֻכּֽוֹת׃\rb* \v 17 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb He also pulled down|נָתָ֑ץ\rb* \rb the tower|מִגְדַּ֥ל\rb* \rb of Penuel|פְּנוּאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and killed|וַֽיַּהֲרֹ֖ג\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of the city.|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Next, Gideon asked|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Zebah|זֶ֙בַח֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and Zalmunna,|צַלְמֻנָּ֔ע\rb* \rb “What kind|אֵיפֹה֙\rb* \rb of men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb did you kill|הֲרַגְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb at Tabor?”|בְּתָב֑וֹר\rb*
\p \rb “Men like you,”|כָּמ֣וֹךָ\rb*\rb |כְמוֹהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb they answered,|וַֽיֹּאמרוּ֙\rb* \rb “each one|אֶחָ֕ד\rb* \rb resembling|כְּתֹ֖אַר\rb* \rb the son|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of a king.”|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb “They|הֵ֑ם\rb* \rb were my brothers,”|אַחַ֥י\rb* \rb Gideon replied,|וַיֹּאמַ֕ר\rb* \rb “the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of my mother!|אִמִּ֖י\rb* \rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb lives,|חַי־\rb* \rb if|ל֚וּ\rb* \rb you had let them live,|הַחֲיִתֶ֣ם\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb I would not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb kill|הָרַ֖גְתִּי\rb* \rb you.”|אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb So he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to Jether,|לְיֶ֣תֶר\rb* \rb his firstborn,|בְּכוֹר֔וֹ\rb* \rb “Get up|ק֖וּם\rb* \rb and kill them.”|הֲרֹ֣ג\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb But the young man|הַנַּ֤עַר\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb draw|שָׁלַ֨ף\rb* \rb his sword;|חַרְבּוֹ֙\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he was fearful|יָרֵ֔א\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he was still|עוֹדֶ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb a youth.|נָֽעַר׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Then Zebah|זֶ֣בַח\rb* \rb and Zalmunna|וְצַלְמֻנָּ֗ע\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֜אמֶר\rb* \rb “Get up|ק֤וּם\rb* \rb and kill|וּפְגַע־\rb* \rb us|בָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb yourself,|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb as the man is,|כָאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb so is his strength.”|גְּבוּרָת֑וֹ\rb* \rb So Gideon|גִּדְע֗וֹן\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb and killed|וַֽיַּהֲרֹג֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Zebah|זֶ֣בַח\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Zalmunna,|צַלְמֻנָּ֔ע\rb* \rb and he took|וַיִּקַּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the crescent ornaments|הַשַּׂ֣הֲרֹנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb from the necks|בְּצַוְּארֵ֥י\rb* \rb of their camels.|גְמַלֵּיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\s1 Gideon’s Ephod
\p \v 22 \rb Then the Israelites|אִֽישׁ־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֤וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gideon,|גִּדְע֔וֹן\rb* \rb “Rule|מְשָׁל־\rb* \rb over us—|בָּ֙נוּ֙\rb*  \rb you|אַתָּ֔ה\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb your son|בִּנְךָ֖\rb*\rb |גַּ֣ם\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb grandson—|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בְּנֶ֑ךָ\rb*  \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you have saved us|הוֹשַׁעְתָּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of Midian.”|מִדְיָֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb But Gideon|גִּדְע֔וֹן\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb “I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb rule|אֶמְשֹׁ֤ל\rb* \rb over you,|בָּכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb will|יִמְשֹׁ֥ל\rb* \rb my son.|בְּנִ֖י\rb*\rb |בָּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb shall rule|יִמְשֹׁ֥ל\rb* \rb over you.”|בָּכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb Then he|גִּדְע֗וֹן\rb* \rb added,|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb “Let me make a request|אֶשְׁאֲלָ֤ה\rb*\rb |שְׁאֵלָ֔ה\rb* \rb of you,|מִכֶּם֙\rb* \rb that each of you|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb give|וּתְנוּ־\rb* \rb me|לִ֕י\rb* \rb an earring|נֶ֣זֶם\rb* \rb from his plunder.”|שְׁלָל֑וֹ\rb* \rb (For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the enemies had gold|זָהָב֙\rb* \rb earrings|נִזְמֵ֤י\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they|הֵֽם׃\rb* \rb were Ishmaelites.)|יִשְׁמְעֵאלִ֖ים\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb “We will give them gladly,”|נָת֣וֹן\rb*\rb |נִתֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb they replied.|וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb*
\p \rb So they spread out|וַֽיִּפְרְשׂוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a garment,|הַשִּׂמְלָ֔ה\rb* \rb and each man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb threw|וַיַּשְׁלִ֣יכוּ\rb* \rb an earring|נֶ֥זֶם\rb* \rb from his plunder|שְׁלָלֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb onto it.|שָׁ֔מָּה\rb* \v 26 \rb The weight|מִשְׁקַ֞ל\rb* \rb of the gold|הַזָּהָב֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb earrings|נִזְמֵ֤י\rb* \rb he had requested|שָׁאָ֔ל\rb* \rb was|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb 1 ,700|אֶ֥לֶף\rb*\rb |וּשְׁבַע־\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb shekels,|זָהָ֑ב\rb*\f + \fr 8:26 \fqa 1,700 shekels \ft is approximately 42.7 pounds or 19.4 kilograms.\f* \rb in addition to|לְ֠בַד\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the crescent ornaments,|הַשַּׂהֲרֹנִ֨ים\rb* \rb the pendants,|וְהַנְּטִפ֜וֹת\rb* \rb the purple|הָאַרְגָּמָ֗ן\rb* \rb garments|וּבִגְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of|שֶׁעַל֙\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Midian,|מִדְיָ֔ן\rb*\rb |וּלְבַד֙\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb and the chains|הָ֣עֲנָק֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb from the necks|בְּצַוְּארֵ֥י\rb* \rb of their camels.|גְמַלֵּיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb From all this Gideon|גִדְע֜וֹן\rb* \rb made|וַיַּעַשׂ֩\rb*\rb |אוֹת֨וֹ\rb* \rb an ephod,|לְאֵפ֗וֹד\rb* \rb which he placed|וַיַּצֵּ֨ג\rb*\rb |אוֹת֤וֹ\rb* \rb in Ophrah,|בְּעָפְרָ֔ה\rb* \rb his hometown.|בְעִירוֹ֙\rb* \rb But soon all|כָֽל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb prostituted themselves|וַיִּזְנ֧וּ\rb* \rb by worshiping it|אַחֲרָ֖יו\rb* \rb there,|שָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb and it became|וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb a snare|לְמוֹקֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb to Gideon|לְגִדְע֥וֹן\rb* \rb and his household.|וּלְבֵית֖וֹ\rb*
\s1 Forty Years of Peace
