\s1 Tola
\p \v 1 \rb After the time|אַחֲרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Abimelech,|אֲבִימֶ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb a man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Issachar,|יִשָּׂשכָ֑ר\rb* \rb Tola|תּוֹלָ֧ע\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Puah,|פּוּאָ֛ה\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Dodo,|דּוֹד֖וֹ\rb* \rb rose up|וַיָּקָם֩\rb* \rb to save|לְהוֹשִׁ֣יעַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb He lived|יֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb in Shamir,|בְּשָׁמִ֖יר\rb* \rb in the hill country|בְּהַ֥ר\rb* \rb of Ephraim.|אֶפְרָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb Tola judged|וַיִּשְׁפֹּט֙\rb*\f + \fr 10:2 \ft Or \fqa governed \ft or \fqa led\ft ; here and throughout the book of Judges\f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb twenty-three|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְשָׁלֹ֖שׁ\rb* \rb years,|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and when he died,|וַיָּ֖מָת\rb* \rb he was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb in Shamir.|בְּשָׁמִֽיר׃פ\rb*
\s1 Jair
\p \v 3 \rb Tola|אַחֲרָ֔יו\rb* \rb was followed by|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb Jair|יָאִ֖יר\rb* \rb the Gileadite,|הַגִּלְעָדִ֑י\rb* \rb who judged|וַיִּשְׁפֹּט֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb twenty-two|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb* \v 4 \rb He had|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֗ים\rb* \rb who rode|רֹֽכְבִים֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb donkeys.|עֲיָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb And they had|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb thirty|וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb towns|עֲיָרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֞ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Gilead,|הַגִּלְעָֽד׃\rb* \rb which to|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb are called|יִקְרְא֣וּ׀\rb*\rb |חַוֺּ֣ת\rb* \rb Havvoth-jair.|יָאִ֗יר\rb*\f + \fr 10:4 \ft Or \fqa the villages of Jair\f*
\p \v 5 \rb When Jair|יָאִ֔יר\rb* \rb died,|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb* \rb he was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֖ר\rb* \rb in Kamon.|בְּקָמֽוֹן׃פ\rb*
\s1 Oppression by the Philistines and Ammonites
\p \v 6 \rb And again|וַיֹּסִ֣פוּ׀\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb did|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb evil|הָרַע֮\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָה֒\rb* \rb They served|וַיַּעַבְד֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Baals,|הַבְּעָלִ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Ashtoreths,|הָעַשְׁתָּר֡וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Aram,|אֲרָם֩\rb* \rb Sidon,|צִיד֜וֹן\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb Moab,|מוֹאָ֗ב\rb* \rb and|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֔וֹן\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb and Philistines.|פְלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb Thus they forsook|וַיַּעַזְב֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb serve Him.|עֲבָדֽוּהוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb So the anger|אַ֥ף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb against Israel,|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and He sold them|וַֽיִּמְכְּרֵם֙\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |וּבְיַ֖ד\rb* \rb and Ammonites,|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עַמּֽוֹן׃\rb* \v 8 \rb who that very|הַהִ֑יא\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb harassed|וַֽיִּרְעֲצ֤וּ\rb* \rb and oppressed|וַיְרֹֽצְצוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and they did so for eighteen|שְׁמֹנֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֜ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb on the other side|בְּעֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in Gilead,|בַּגִּלְעָֽד׃\rb* \rb the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Amorites.|הָאֱמֹרִ֖י\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb The Ammonites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּוֹן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb also|גַּם־\rb* \rb crossed|וַיַּעַבְר֤וּ\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֛ם\rb* \rb against Judah,|בִּיהוּדָ֥ה\rb* \rb Benjamin,|וּבְבִנְיָמִ֖ין\rb* \rb and the house|וּבְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Ephraim,|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb was in deep|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb distress.|וַתֵּ֥צֶר\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Then the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb cried out|וַֽיִּזְעֲקוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “We have sinned|חָטָ֣אנוּ\rb* \rb against You,|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb for we have indeed|וְכִ֤י\rb* \rb forsaken|עָזַ֙בְנוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our God|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb and served|וַֽנַּעֲבֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Baals.”|הַבְּעָלִֽים׃פ\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb replied,|וַ֥יֹּאמֶר\rb*\rb |הֲלֹ֤א\rb* \rb “When the Egyptians,|מִמִּצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |וּמִן־\rb* \rb Amorites,|הָ֣אֱמֹרִ֔י\rb*\rb |וּמִן־\rb* \rb Ammonites,|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֖וֹן\rb*\rb |וּמִן־\rb* \rb Philistines,|פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb* \v 12 \rb Sidonians,|וְצִידוֹנִ֤ים\rb* \rb Amalekites,|וַֽעֲמָלֵק֙\rb* \rb and Maonites|וּמָע֔וֹן\rb*\f + \fr 10:12 \ft Hebrew; some LXX manuscripts \fqa Midianites\f* \rb oppressed you|לָחֲצ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and you cried out|וַתִּצְעֲק֣וּ\rb* \rb to Me,|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb did I not save|וָאוֹשִׁ֥יעָה\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb from their hands?|מִיָּדָֽם׃\rb* \v 13 \rb But you|וְאַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb have forsaken|עֲזַבְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb Me|אוֹתִ֔י\rb* \rb and served|וַתַּעַבְד֖וּ\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֑ים\rb* \rb gods,|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb so|לָכֵ֥ן\rb* \rb I will no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|אוֹסִ֖יף\rb* \rb save|לְהוֹשִׁ֥יעַ\rb* \rb you.|אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 14 \rb Go|לְכ֗וּ\rb* \rb and cry out|וְזַֽעֲקוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the gods|הָ֣אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have chosen.|בְּחַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb Let them|הֵ֛מָּה\rb* \rb save|יוֹשִׁ֥יעוּ\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in your time|בְּעֵ֥ת\rb* \rb of trouble.”|צָרַתְכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb “We have sinned,”|חָטָ֔אנוּ\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֨וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb “Deal|עֲשֵׂה־\rb*\rb |אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb with us|לָ֔נוּ\rb*\rb |כְּכָל־\rb* \rb as You see|בְּעֵינֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb fit;|הַטּ֖וֹב\rb* \rb but|אַ֛ךְ\rb* \rb please|נָ֖א\rb* \rb deliver us today!”|הַצִּילֵ֥נוּ\rb*\rb |הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \v 16 \rb So they put away|וַיָּסִ֜ירוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the foreign|הַנֵּכָר֙\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb from among them|מִקִּרְבָּ֔ם\rb* \rb and served|וַיַּעַבְד֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and He|נַפְשׁ֖וֹ\rb* \rb could no longer bear|וַתִּקְצַ֥ר\rb* \rb the misery|בַּעֲמַ֥ל\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Then the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb were called to arms|וַיִּצָּֽעֲקוּ֙\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb in Gilead,|בַּגִּלְעָ֑ד\rb* \rb and the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb assembled|וַיֵּאָֽסְפוּ֙\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb at Mizpah.|בַּמִּצְפָּֽה׃\rb* \v 18 \rb And the rulers|שָׂרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Gilead|גִלְעָד֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֨וּ\rb*\rb |הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb another,|רֵעֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb “Whoever|מִ֣י\rb*\rb |הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb will launch|יָחֵ֔ל\rb* \rb the attack|לְהִלָּחֵ֖ם\rb* \rb against the Ammonites|בִּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֑וֹן\rb* \rb will be|יִֽהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the head|לְרֹ֔אשׁ\rb* \rb of all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb who live|יֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb in Gilead.”|גִלְעָֽד׃פ\rb*
\c 11
\s1 Jephthah Delivers Israel
\p \v 1 \rb Now Jephthah|וְיִפְתָּ֣ח\rb* \rb the Gileadite|הַגִּלְעָדִ֗י\rb* \rb was|הָיָה֙\rb* \rb a mighty man|גִּבּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb of valor;|חַ֔יִל\rb* \rb he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb was the son|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb of a prostitute,|זוֹנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and Gilead|גִּלְעָ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb was his|יִפְתָּֽח׃\rb* \rb father.|וַיּ֥וֹלֶד\rb* \v 2 \rb And Gilead’s|גִּלְעָ֛ד\rb*\rb |ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb wife|אֵֽשֶׁת־\rb* \rb bore him|וַתֵּ֧לֶד\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֑ים\rb* \rb who|בְֽנֵי־\rb*\rb |הָאִשָּׁ֜ה\rb* \rb grew up,|וַיִּגְדְּל֨וּ\rb* \rb drove Jephthah|יִפְתָּ֗ח\rb* \rb out,|וַיְגָרְשׁ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֤אמְרוּ\rb* \rb to him,|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb “You shall have no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb inheritance|תִנְחַ֣ל\rb* \rb in our father’s|אָבִ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb house,|בְּבֵית־\rb* \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb you|אָֽתָּה׃\rb* \rb are the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of another|אַחֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb woman.”|אִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb So Jephthah|יִפְתָּח֙\rb* \rb fled|וַיִּבְרַ֤ח\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb his brothers|אֶחָ֔יו\rb* \rb and settled|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Tob,|ט֑וֹב\rb* \rb where worthless men|רֵיקִ֔ים\rb* \rb gathered around|וַיִּֽתְלַקְּט֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb him|יִפְתָּח֙\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb and traveled|וַיֵּצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb with him.|עִמּֽוֹ׃פ\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Some time later,|וַיְהִ֖י\rb*\rb |מִיָּמִ֑ים\rb* \rb when the Ammonites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֖וֹן\rb* \rb fought|וַיִּלָּחֲמ֥וּ\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 5 \rb and|וַיְהִ֕י\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֖וֹן\rb* \rb made war|נִלְחֲמ֥וּ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb them,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Gilead|גִלְעָ֔ד\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּֽלְכוּ֙\rb* \rb to get|לָקַ֥חַת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jephthah|יִפְתָּ֖ח\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Tob.|טֽוֹב׃\rb* \v 6 \rb “Come,”|לְכָ֕ה\rb* \rb they said,|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |לְיִפְתָּ֔ח\rb* \rb “be|וְהָיִ֥יתָה\rb* \rb our|לָּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb commander,|לְקָצִ֑ין\rb* \rb so that we can fight|וְנִֽלָּחֲמָ֖ה\rb* \rb against the Ammonites.”|בִּבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עַמּֽוֹן׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Jephthah|יִפְתָּח֙\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to the elders|לְזִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Gilead,|גִלְעָ֔ד\rb* \rb “Did you|אַתֶּם֙\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹ֤א\rb* \rb hate|שְׂנֵאתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb me|אוֹתִ֔י\rb* \rb and expel me|וַתְּגָרְשׁ֖וּנִי\rb* \rb from my father’s|אָבִ֑י\rb* \rb house?|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb Why|וּמַדּ֜וּעַ\rb* \rb then have you come|בָּאתֶ֤ם\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַי֙\rb* \rb now,|עַ֔תָּה\rb* \rb when|כַּאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb you are in distress?”|צַ֥ר\rb*\rb |לָכֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb They|זִקְנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |גִלְעָ֜ד\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּאמְרוּ֩\rb* \rb Jephthah,|יִפְתָּ֗ח\rb* \rb “This is why|לָכֵן֙\rb* \rb we now|עַתָּה֙\rb* \rb turn|שַׁ֣בְנוּ\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to you,|אֶל־\rb* \rb that you may go|וְהָלַכְתָּ֣\rb* \rb with us,|עִמָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb fight|וְנִלְחַמְתָּ֖\rb* \rb the Ammonites,|בִּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֑וֹן\rb* \rb and become|וְהָיִ֤יתָ\rb* \rb leader|לְרֹ֔אשׁ\rb* \rb over all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb of us|לָּ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb who live|יֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb in Gilead.”|גִלְעָֽד׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb But Jephthah|יִפְתָּ֜ח\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb them,|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |גִלְעָ֗ד\rb* \rb “If|אִם־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֤ם\rb*\rb |אוֹתִי֙\rb* \rb take me back|מְשִׁיבִ֨ים\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵם֙\rb* \rb the Ammonites|בִּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb gives them|וְנָתַ֧ן\rb* \rb to me,|לְפָנָ֑י\rb* \rb will I|אָנֹכִ֕י\rb* \rb really be|אֶהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb leader?”|לְרֹֽאשׁ׃\rb*
