\p \v 13 \rb The king|מֶ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֜וֹן\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb Jephthah’s|יִפְתָּ֗ח\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb messengers,|מַלְאֲכֵ֣י\rb* \rb “When Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb came up|בַּעֲלוֹת֣וֹ\rb* \rb out of Egypt,|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb they seized|לָקַ֨ח\rb* \rb my land,|אַרְצִי֙\rb* \rb from the Arnon|מֵאַרְנ֥וֹן\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the Jabbok|הַיַּבֹּ֖ק\rb* \rb and all the way|וְעַד־\rb* \rb to the Jordan.|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb Now, therefore,|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb restore|הָשִׁ֥יבָה\rb* \rb it|אֶתְהֶ֖ן\rb* \rb peaceably.”|בְּשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Jephthah|יִפְתָּ֑ח\rb* \rb again|וַיּ֥וֹסֶף\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֙\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עַמּֽוֹן׃\rb* \v 15 \rb to tell|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb him,|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb Jephthah|יִפְתָּ֑ח\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb take away|לָקַ֤ח\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb or|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |אֶ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Ammonites.|עַמּֽוֹן׃\rb* \v 16 \rb But|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb when Israel came up|בַּעֲלוֹתָ֣ם\rb* \rb out of Egypt,|מִמִּצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb they|יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb traveled|וַיֵּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb through the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּר֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the Red|ס֔וּף\rb* \rb Sea|יַם־\rb*\f + \fr 11:16 \ft Or \fqa the Sea of Reeds\f* \rb and came|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb to Kadesh.|קָדֵֽשָׁה׃\rb* \v 17 \rb Then Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶלֶךְ֩\rb* \rb of Edom,|אֱד֨וֹם׀\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֜ר\rb* \rb ‘Please|נָּ֣א\rb* \rb let us pass|אֶעְבְּרָה־\rb* \rb through your land,’|בְאַרְצֶ֗ךָ\rb* \rb but the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱד֔וֹם\rb* \rb would not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb listen.|שָׁמַע֙\rb* \rb They also|וְגַ֨ם\rb* \rb sent|שָׁלַ֖ח\rb* \rb messengers to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Moab,|מוֹאָ֛ב\rb* \rb but he would not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb consent.|אָבָ֑ה\rb* \rb So Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb stayed|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb in Kadesh.|בְּקָדֵֽשׁ׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Then Israel traveled|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb through the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֗ר\rb* \rb and bypassed|וַיָּ֜סָב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the lands|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱדוֹם֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Moab.|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb They came|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb to|מִמִּזְרַח־\rb* \rb the east side|שֶׁ֙מֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb of the land|לְאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּן\rb* \rb on the other side|בְּעֵ֣בֶר\rb* \rb of the Arnon.|אַרְנ֑וֹן\rb* \rb But they did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb enter|בָ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb the territory|בִּגְב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Moab,|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb since|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the Arnon|אַרְנ֖וֹן\rb* \rb was its border.|גְּב֥וּל\rb*\rb |מוֹאָֽב׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb And Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Sihon|סִיח֥וֹן\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of the Amorites,|הָאֱמֹרִ֖י\rb* \rb who ruled|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb in Heshbon,|חֶשְׁבּ֑וֹן\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb ‘Please|נָּ֥א\rb* \rb let us pass|נַעְבְּרָה־\rb* \rb through your land|בְאַרְצְךָ֖\rb* \rb into|עַד־\rb* \rb our own place.’|מְקוֹמִֽי׃\rb* \v 20 \rb But Sihon|סִיח֤וֹן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb would not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb trust|הֶאֱמִ֨ין\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb to pass|עֲבֹ֣ר\rb* \rb through his territory.|בִּגְבֻל֔וֹ\rb* \rb So he|סִיחוֹן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gathered|וַיֶּאֱסֹ֤ף\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his people,|עַמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb encamped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֖וּ\rb* \rb in Jahaz,|בְּיָ֑הְצָה\rb* \rb and fought|וַיִּלָּ֖חֶם\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
