\s1 Jephthah Defeats Ephraim
\p \v 1 \rb Then the men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb assembled|וַיִּצָּעֵק֙\rb* \rb and crossed the Jordan|וַֽיַּעֲבֹ֖ר\rb* \rb to Zaphon.|צָפ֑וֹנָה\rb* \rb They said|וַיֹּאמְר֨וּ\rb* \rb to Jephthah,|לְיִפְתָּ֜ח\rb* \rb “Why|מַדּ֣וּעַ׀\rb* \rb have you crossed over|עָבַ֣רְתָּ׀\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֣ם\rb* \rb the Ammonites|בִּבְנֵי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֗וֹן\rb*\rb |וְלָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb without|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb calling us|קָרָ֙אתָ֙\rb* \rb to go|לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb with you?|עִמָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb We will burn your house|בֵּיתְךָ֕\rb* \rb down|נִשְׂרֹ֥ף\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb with you inside!”|בָּאֵֽשׁ׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb But Jephthah|יִפְתָּח֙\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb “My people|וְעַמִּ֥י\rb* \rb and I|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb had|הָיִ֛יתִי\rb* \rb a serious|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb conflict|רִ֗יב\rb* \rb with the Ammonites,|וּבְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֖וֹן\rb* \rb and when I called,|וָאֶזְעַ֣ק\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb you did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb save|הוֹשַׁעְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb me|אוֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb out of their hands.|מִיָּדָֽם׃\rb* \v 3 \rb When I saw|וָֽאֶרְאֶ֞ה\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you would not|אֵינְךָ֣\rb* \rb save me,|מוֹשִׁ֗יע\rb* \rb I risked|וָאָשִׂ֨ימָה\rb*\rb |בְכַפִּי֙\rb* \rb my life|נַפְשִׁ֤י\rb* \rb and crossed over|וָֽאֶעְבְּרָה֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Ammonites,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb delivered them|וַיִּתְּנֵ֥ם\rb* \rb into my hand.|בְּיָדִ֑י\rb* \rb Why then|וְלָמָ֞ה\rb* \rb have you come|עֲלִיתֶ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֛י\rb* \rb today|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּ֥חֶם\rb* \rb against me?”|בִּֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Jephthah then|יִפְתָּח֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gathered|וַיִּקְבֹּ֤ץ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of Gilead|גִלְעָ֔ד\rb* \rb and fought|וַיִּלָּ֖חֶם\rb* \rb against|אֶת־\rb* \rb Ephraim.|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb And the men|אַנְשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb of Gilead|גִלְעָ֜ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb struck them down|וַיַּכּוּ֩\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the Ephraimites|אֶפְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb had said,|אָמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb “You|אַתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb Gileadites|גִּלְעָ֕ד\rb* \rb are fugitives|פְּלִיטֵ֤י\rb* \rb in Ephraim,|אֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb living in the territories|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb and Manasseh.”|מְנַשֶּֽׁה׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb The Gileadites|גִּלְעָ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb captured|וַיִּלְכֹּ֥ד\rb* \rb the fords|מַעְבְּר֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb leading to Ephraim,|לְאֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and|וְֽ֠הָיָה\rb* \rb whenever|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb a fugitive|פְּלִיטֵ֤י\rb* \rb from Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb would say,|יֹאמְר֞וּ\rb* \rb “Let me cross over,”|אֶעֱבֹ֔רָה\rb* \rb the Gileadites|גִלְעָ֛ד\rb* \rb would ask|וַיֹּ֨אמְרוּ\rb* \rb him,|ל֧וֹ\rb*\rb |אַנְשֵֽׁי־\rb* \rb “Are you|אַ֖תָּה\rb* \rb an Ephraimite?”|הַֽאֶפְרָתִ֥י\rb*
\p \rb If he answered,|וַיֹּ֥אמֶֽר׀\rb* \rb “No,”|לֹֽא׃\rb* \v 6 \rb they told|וַיֹּ֣אמְרוּ\rb* \rb him,|לוֹ֩\rb* \rb “Please|נָ֨א\rb* \rb say|אֱמָר־\rb* \rb Shibboleth.”|שִׁבֹּ֜לֶת\rb*
\p \rb If he said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Sibboleth,”|סִבֹּ֗לֶת\rb* \rb because he could|יָכִין֙\rb* \rb not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb pronounce|לְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb it correctly,|כֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb they seized|וַיֹּאחֲז֣וּ\rb* \rb him|אוֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and killed him|וַיִּשְׁחָט֖וּהוּ\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the fords|מַעְבְּר֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the Jordan.|הַיַּרְדֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb So at that|הַהִיא֙\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֤ת\rb* \rb 42,000|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |אָֽלֶף׃\rb* \rb Ephraimites|מֵֽאֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb were killed.|וַיִּפֹּ֞ל\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Jephthah|יִפְתָּ֛ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb judged|וַיִּשְׁפֹּ֥ט\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb six|שֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years,|שָׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb and when he|יִפְתָּח֙\rb*\rb |הַגִּלְעָדִ֔י\rb* \rb died,|וַיָּ֗מָת\rb* \rb he was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֖ר\rb* \rb in one of the cities|בְּעָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Gilead.|גִלְעָֽד׃פ\rb*\f + \fr 12:7 \ft LXX \fqa in his city in Gilead\f*
\s1 Ibzan, Elon, and Abdon
\p \v 8 \rb After Jephthah,|אַֽחֲרָיו֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ibzan|אִבְצָ֖ן\rb* \rb of|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb Bethlehem|לָֽחֶם׃\rb* \rb judged|וַיִּשְׁפֹּ֤ט\rb* \rb Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \v 9 \rb He had|וַיְהִי־\rb* \rb thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb sons,|בָּנִ֗ים\rb* \rb as well as thirty|וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb daughters|בָּנוֹת֙\rb* \rb whom he gave in marriage|שִׁלַּ֣ח\rb* \rb to men outside his clan;|הַח֔וּצָה\rb* \rb and for his sons|לְבָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb he brought back|הֵבִ֥יא\rb* \rb thirty|וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb wives|בָּנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb elsewhere.|הַח֑וּץ\rb* \rb Ibzan judged|וַיִּשְׁפֹּ֥ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנִֽים׃\rb* \v 10 \rb Then Ibzan|אִבְצָ֔ן\rb* \rb died,|וַיָּ֣מָת\rb* \rb and he was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֖ר\rb*\rb |בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb in Bethlehem.|לָֽחֶם׃פ\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb After Ibzan,|אַֽחֲרָיו֙\rb* \rb Elon|אֵיל֖וֹן\rb* \rb the Zebulunite|הַזְּבֽוּלֹנִ֑י\rb* \rb judged|וַיִּשְׁפֹּ֤ט\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |וַיִּשְׁפֹּ֥ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb ten|עֶ֥שֶׂר\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנִֽים׃\rb* \v 12 \rb Then Elon|אֵל֣וֹן\rb* \rb the Zebulunite|הַזְּבֽוּלֹנִ֑י\rb* \rb died,|וַיָּ֖מָת\rb* \rb and he was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb in Aijalon|בְּאַיָּל֖וֹן\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Zebulun.|זְבוּלֻֽן׃פ\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb After Elon,|אַחֲרָ֖יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Abdon|עַבְדּ֥וֹן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hillel,|הִלֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb from Pirathon,|הַפִּרְעָתוֹנִֽי׃\rb* \rb judged|וַיִּשְׁפֹּ֥ט\rb* \rb Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \v 14 \rb He had|וַיְהִי־\rb* \rb forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֗ים\rb* \rb and thirty|וּשְׁלֹשִׁים֙\rb* \rb grandsons,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb who rode|רֹכְבִ֖ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb seventy|שִׁבְעִ֣ים\rb* \rb donkeys.|עֲיָרִ֑ם\rb* \rb And he judged|וַיִּשְׁפֹּ֥ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb eight|שְׁמֹנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנִֽים׃\rb* \v 15 \rb Then Abdon|עַבְדּ֥וֹן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hillel,|הִלֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb from Pirathon,|הַפִּרְעָתוֹנִ֑י\rb* \rb died,|וַיָּ֛מָת\rb* \rb and he was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֤ר\rb* \rb at Pirathon|בְּפִרְעָתוֹן֙\rb* \rb in|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb Ephraim,|אֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb in the hill country|בְּהַ֖ר\rb* \rb of the Amalekites.|הָעֲמָלֵקִֽי׃פ\rb*
\c 13
\s1 The Birth of Samson
\r \ref Numbers 6:1–21|NUM 6:1-21\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Again|וַיֹּסִ֙פוּ֙\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb did|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb so He|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb delivered them|וַיִּתְּנֵ֧ם\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb for forty|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָֽה׃פ\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb Now there was|וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֧ד\rb* \rb man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb from Zorah|מִצָּרְעָ֛ה\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמ֣וֹ\rb* \rb Manoah,|מָנ֑וֹחַ\rb* \rb from the clan|מִמִּשְׁפַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb of the Danites,|הַדָּנִ֖י\rb* \rb whose wife was|וְאִשְׁתּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb barren|עֲקָרָ֖ה\rb* \rb and had no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb children.|יָלָֽדָה׃\rb* \v 3 \rb The angel|מַלְאַךְ־\rb*\f + \fr 13:3 \ft Or \fqa Angel\ft ; here and throughout chapter 13; corresponding pronouns may also be capitalized.\f* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb appeared|וַיֵּרָ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to her,|אֵלֶ֗יהָ\rb* \rb “It is true|הִנֵּה־\rb*\rb |נָ֤א\rb* \rb that you|אַתְּ־\rb* \rb are barren|עֲקָרָה֙\rb* \rb and have no|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb children;|יָלַ֔דְתְּ\rb* \rb but you will conceive|וְהָרִ֖ית\rb* \rb and give birth to|וְיָלַ֥דְתְּ\rb* \rb a son.|בֵּֽן׃\rb* \v 4 \rb Now|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb please|נָ֔א\rb* \rb be careful|הִשָּׁ֣מְרִי\rb* \rb not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb to drink|תִּשְׁתִּ֖י\rb* \rb wine|יַ֣יִן\rb* \rb or strong drink,|וְשֵׁכָ֑ר\rb* \rb and not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb to eat|תֹּאכְלִ֖י\rb* \rb anything|כָּל־\rb* \rb unclean.|טָמֵֽא׃\rb* \v 5 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb behold,|הִנָּ֨ךְ\rb* \rb you will conceive|הָרָ֜ה\rb* \rb and give birth to|וְיֹלַ֣דְתְּ\rb* \rb a son.|בֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb And no|לֹא־\rb* \rb razor|וּמוֹרָה֙\rb* \rb shall touch|יַעֲלֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb his head,|רֹאשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the boy|הַנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a Nazirite|נְזִ֧יר\rb*\f + \fr 13:5 \ft Or \fqa set apart\f* \rb to God|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the womb,|הַבָּ֑טֶן\rb* \rb and he|וְה֗וּא\rb* \rb will begin|יָחֵ֛ל\rb* \rb the deliverance|לְהוֹשִׁ֥יעַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of the Philistines.”|פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb So the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֗ה\rb* \rb went|וַתָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb and told|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb her husband,|לְאִישָׁהּ֮\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֒\rb* \rb “A man|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb came|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb to me.|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb His appearance was like|וּמַרְאֵ֕הוּ\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb of God,|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb exceedingly|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb awesome.|נוֹרָ֣א\rb* \rb I did not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb ask him|שְׁאִלְתִּ֙יהוּ֙\rb* \rb where|אֵֽי־\rb* \rb he came from,|מִזֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and he did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb tell|הִגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb me|לִֽי׃\rb* \rb his name.|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \v 7 \rb But he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me,|לִ֔י\rb* \rb ‘Behold,|הִנָּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb you will conceive|הָרָ֖ה\rb* \rb and give birth to|וְיֹלַ֣דְתְּ\rb* \rb a son.|בֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb Now, therefore,|וְעַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb drink|תִּשְׁתִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb wine|יַ֣יִן\rb* \rb or strong drink,|וְשֵׁכָ֗ר\rb* \rb and do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb eat|תֹּֽאכְלִי֙\rb* \rb anything|כָּל־\rb* \rb unclean,|טֻמְאָ֔ה\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the boy|הַנַּ֔עַר\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb a Nazirite|נְזִ֤יר\rb* \rb to God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the womb|הַבֶּ֖טֶן\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the day|י֥וֹם\rb* \rb of his death.’”|מוֹתֽוֹ׃פ\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Then Manoah|מָנ֛וֹחַ\rb* \rb prayed|וַיֶּעְתַּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb “Please,|בִּ֣י\rb* \rb O Lord,|אֲדוֹנָ֔י\rb* \rb let the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֞ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb You sent us|שָׁלַ֗חְתָּ\rb* \rb come|יָבוֹא־\rb*\rb |נָ֥א\rb* \rb to us|אֵלֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb again|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb to teach us|וְיוֹרֵ֕נוּ\rb* \rb how|מַֽה־\rb* \rb to raise|נַּעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb the boy|לַנַּ֥עַר\rb* \rb who is to be born.”|הַיּוּלָּֽד׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb And God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb listened|וַיִּשְׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb to the voice|בְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of Manoah,|מָנ֑וֹחַ\rb* \rb and the angel|מַלְאַךְ֩\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֨ים\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb*\rb |ע֜וֹד\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֗ה\rb* \rb as she|וְהִיא֙\rb* \rb was sitting|יוֹשֶׁ֣בֶת\rb* \rb in the field;|בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb but her husband|אִישָׁ֖הּ\rb* \rb Manoah|וּמָנ֥וֹחַ\rb* \rb was not|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb with her.|עִמָּֽהּ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb The woman|לְאִישָׁ֑הּ\rb* \rb ran|וַתָּ֖רָץ\rb*\rb |וַתַּגֵּ֣ד\rb* \rb quickly|וַתְּמַהֵר֙\rb* \rb to tell|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb her husband,|הָֽאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb “Behold,|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָֽי׃\rb* \rb the other day|בַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb has reappeared!”|נִרְאָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֵלַי֙\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb So Manoah|מָנ֖וֹחַ\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֛קָם\rb* \rb and followed|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb his wife.|אִשְׁתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb When he came|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the man,|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb he asked,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Are you|הַאַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb spoke|דִּבַּ֥רְתָּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb my wife?”|הָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb*
\p \rb “I|אָֽנִי׃\rb* \rb am, ” he said.|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Then Manoah|מָנ֔וֹחַ\rb* \rb asked,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “When|עַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb your words|דְבָרֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb come to pass,|יָבֹ֣א\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb will be|יִּֽהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the boy’s|הַנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb rule of life|מִשְׁפַּט־\rb* \rb and mission?”|וּמַעֲשֵֽׂהוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb So the angel|מַלְאַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb* \rb Manoah,|מָנ֑וֹחַ\rb* \rb “Your wife|הָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb is to do|תִּשָּׁמֵֽר׃\rb* \rb everything|מִכֹּ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I told her.|אָמַ֥רְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \v 14 \rb She must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb eat|תֹאכַ֗ל\rb* \rb anything|מִכֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb comes|יֵצֵא֩\rb* \rb from the vine,|מִגֶּ֨פֶן\rb*\rb |הַיַּ֜יִן\rb* \rb nor drink|תֵּ֔שְׁתְּ\rb* \rb any wine|וְיַ֤יִן\rb* \rb or strong drink,|וְשֵׁכָר֙\rb* \rb nor|אַל־\rb* \rb eat|תֹּאכַ֑ל\rb* \rb anything|וְכָל־\rb* \rb unclean.|טֻמְאָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אַל־\rb* \rb She must do|תִּשְׁמֹֽר׃\rb* \rb everything|כֹּ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have commanded her.”|צִוִּיתִ֖יהָ\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb “Please|נָּ֣א\rb* \rb stay here,”|נַעְצְרָה־\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb Manoah|מָנ֖וֹחַ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb “and we will prepare|וְנַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb a young goat|גְּדִ֥י\rb*\rb |עִזִּֽים׃\rb* \rb for you.”|לְפָנֶ֖יךָ\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb And the angel|מַלְאַ֨ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb “Even if|אִם־\rb* \rb I stay,|תַּעְצְרֵ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb I will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb eat|אֹכַ֣ל\rb* \rb your food.|בְּלַחְמֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb you prepare|תַּעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb a burnt offering,|עֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb offer it|תַּעֲלֶ֑נָּה\rb* \rb to the LORD.”|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb Manoah|מָנ֔וֹחַ\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb know that|יָדַ֣ע\rb* \rb it was|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Then Manoah|מָנ֛וֹחַ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb “What|מִ֣י\rb* \rb is your name,|שְׁמֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb so that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb we may honor you|וְכִבַּדְנֽוּךָ׃\rb* \rb when your word|דִבְרֶיךָ\rb* \rb comes to pass?”|יָבֹ֥א\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb “Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb*\rb |זֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb do you ask|תִּשְׁאַ֣ל\rb* \rb my name,”|לִשְׁמִ֑י\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |לּוֹ֙\rb* \rb “since it|וְהוּא־\rb* \rb is beyond comprehension?”|פֶ֛לִאי׃ס\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Then Manoah|מָנ֜וֹחַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb a young goat|גְּדִ֤י\rb*\rb |הָעִזִּים֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and a grain offering|הַמִּנְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb and offered them|וַיַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb a rock|הַצּ֖וּר\rb* \rb to the LORD.|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb And as Manoah|וּמָנ֥וֹחַ\rb* \rb and his wife|וְאִשְׁתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb looked on,|רֹאִֽים׃\rb* \rb the LORD did|לַעֲשׂ֔וֹת\rb* \rb a marvelous thing.|וּמַפְלִ֣א\rb* \v 20 \rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb When the flame|הַלַּ֜הַב\rb* \rb went up|בַעֲל֨וֹת\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֤ל\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb to the sky,|הַשָּׁמַ֔יְמָה\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַךְ־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb ascended|וַיַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb in the|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb* \rb flame.|בְּלַ֣הַב\rb*
\p \rb When Manoah|וּמָנ֤וֹחַ\rb* \rb and his wife|וְאִשְׁתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb saw this,|רֹאִ֔ים\rb* \rb they fell|וַיִּפְּל֥וּ\rb* \rb facedown|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to the ground.|אָֽרְצָה׃\rb* \v 21 \rb And when the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb appear|לְהֵרָאֹ֖ה\rb* \rb again|יָ֤סַף\rb*\rb |עוֹד֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Manoah|מָנ֣וֹחַ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb his wife,|אִשְׁתּ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |אָ֚ז\rb* \rb Manoah|מָנ֔וֹחַ\rb* \rb realized|יָדַ֣ע\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it had been|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb “We are going to die,”|מ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |נָמ֑וּת\rb* \rb he|מָנ֛וֹחַ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his wife,|אִשְׁתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb “for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb we have seen|רָאִֽינוּ׃\rb* \rb God!”|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb But his wife|אִשְׁתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb replied,|וַתֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb “If|לוּ֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb had intended|חָפֵ֨ץ\rb* \rb to kill us,|לַהֲמִיתֵ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb He would not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb have accepted|לָקַ֤ח\rb* \rb the burnt offering|עֹלָ֣ה\rb* \rb and the grain offering|וּמִנְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb from our hands,|מִיָּדֵ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb nor would He|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb have shown|הֶרְאָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb us|אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these things|אֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb or spoken|הִשְׁמִיעָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb to us|וְכָעֵ֕ת\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb this way.”|כָּזֹֽאת׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb So the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb gave birth to|וַתֵּ֤לֶד\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb and named|וַתִּקְרָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Samson.|שִׁמְשׁ֑וֹן\rb* \rb The boy|הַנַּ֔עַר\rb* \rb grew,|וַיִּגְדַּ֣ל\rb* \rb and the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb blessed him.|וַֽיְבָרְכֵ֖הוּ\rb* \v 25 \rb And the Spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb began|וַתָּ֙חֶל֙\rb* \rb to stir him|לְפַעֲמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb at Mahaneh-dan,|בְּמַחֲנֵה־\rb*\f + \fr 13:25 \fqa Mahaneh-dan \ft means \fqa camp of Dan\ft .\f* \rb |דָ֑ן\rb*\rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb Zorah|צָרְעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb and Eshtaol.|אֶשְׁתָּאֹֽל׃פ\rb*
\c 14
\s1 Samson’s Marriage
\p \v 1 \rb One day Samson|שִׁמְשׁ֖וֹן\rb* \rb went down|וַיֵּ֥רֶד\rb* \rb to Timnah,|תִּמְנָ֑תָה\rb* \rb where he saw|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁ֛ה\rb* \rb a young Philistine|פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb* \rb woman.|מִבְּנ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |בְּתִמְנָ֖תָה\rb* \v 2 \rb So he returned|וַיַּ֗עַל\rb* \rb and told|וַיַּגֵּד֙\rb* \rb his father|לְאָבִ֣יו\rb* \rb and mother,|וּלְאִמּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁ֛ה\rb* \rb “I have seen|רָאִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb a daughter|מִבְּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb in Timnah.|בְתִמְנָ֖תָה\rb* \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb get|קְחוּ־\rb* \rb her|אוֹתָ֥הּ\rb* \rb for me|לִּ֖י\rb* \rb as a wife.”|לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb But his father|אָבִ֣יו\rb* \rb and mother|וְאִמּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb “Can’t you find|הַאֵין֩\rb* \rb a young woman|בִּבְנ֨וֹת\rb* \rb among your relatives|אַחֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb or among any|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb of our people?|עַמִּי֙\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Must you|אַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb go|הוֹלֵךְ֙\rb* \rb to the uncircumcised|הָעֲרֵלִ֑ים\rb* \rb Philistines|מִפְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb to get|לָקַ֣חַת\rb* \rb a wife?”|אִשָּׁ֔ה\rb*
\p \rb But Samson|שִׁמְשׁ֤וֹן\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb his father,|אָבִיו֙\rb* \rb “Get|קַֽח־\rb* \rb her|אוֹתָ֣הּ\rb* \rb for me,|לִ֔י\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb she|הִ֖יא\rb* \rb is pleasing|יָשְׁרָ֥ה\rb* \rb to my eyes.”|בְעֵינָֽי׃\rb* \v 4 \rb (Now his father|וְאָבִ֨יו\rb* \rb and mother|וְאִמּ֜וֹ\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb know|יָדְע֗וּ\rb*\rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb this|הִ֔יא\rb* \rb was from|כִּי־\rb* \rb the LORD,|מֵיְהוָה֙\rb* \rb who|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb was seeking|מְבַקֵּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb an occasion to move|תֹאֲנָ֥ה\rb* \rb against the Philistines;|מִפְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb for at that|הַהִ֔יא\rb* \rb time|וּבָעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb were ruling|מֹשְׁלִ֥ים\rb* \rb over Israel.)|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*
