\p \v 4 \rb Then Samson|שִׁמְשׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb and caught|וַיִּלְכֹּ֖ד\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb foxes.|שׁוּעָלִ֑ים\rb* \rb And he took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb torches,|לַפִּדִ֗ים\rb* \rb turned|וַיֶּ֤פֶן\rb* \rb the foxes tail-to-tail,|זָנָב֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |זָנָ֔ב\rb* \rb and fastened|וַיָּ֨שֶׂם\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֛ד\rb* \rb torch|לַפִּ֥יד\rb* \rb between|בֵּין־\rb* \rb each pair|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of tails.|הַזְּנָב֖וֹת\rb*\rb |בַּתָּֽוֶךְ׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Then he lit|וַיַּבְעֶר־\rb*\rb |אֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb the torches|בַּלַּפִּידִ֔ים\rb* \rb and released the foxes|וַיְשַׁלַּ֖ח\rb* \rb into the standing grain|בְּקָמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the Philistines,|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb burning up|וַיַּבְעֵ֛ר\rb* \rb the piles of grain|מִגָּדִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |וְעַד־\rb* \rb and the standing grain,|קָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb as well as|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the vineyards|כֶּ֥רֶם\rb* \rb and olive groves.|זָֽיִת׃\rb*
