\p \v 8 \rb So the lords|סַרְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb brought|וַיַּעֲלוּ־\rb* \rb her|לָ֞הּ\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעָ֛ה\rb* \rb fresh|לַחִ֖ים\rb* \rb bowstrings|יְתָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had not|לֹא־\rb* \rb been dried,|חֹרָ֑בוּ\rb* \rb and she tied him up|וַתַּאַסְרֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb with them.|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 9 \rb While the men|וְהָאֹרֵ֗ב\rb* \rb were hidden|יֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb in her|לָהּ֙\rb* \rb room,|בַּחֶ֔דֶר\rb* \rb she called out,|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb “Samson,|שִׁמְשׁ֑וֹן\rb* \rb the Philistines are|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֥ים\rb* \rb here!”|עָלֶ֖יךָ\rb*
