\p \v 13 \rb Then Delilah|דְּלִילָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַתֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Samson,|שִׁמְשׁ֗וֹן\rb* \rb “You have mocked|הֵתַ֤לְתָּ\rb* \rb me|בִּי֙\rb* \rb and lied to me|וַתְּדַבֵּ֤ר\rb*\rb |אֵלַי֙\rb*\rb |כְּזָבִ֔ים\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb all along!|הֵ֜נָּה\rb* \rb Tell|הַגִּ֣ידָה\rb* \rb me|לִּ֔י\rb* \rb how|בַּמֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb you can be tied up.”|תֵּאָסֵ֑ר\rb*
\p \rb He told her,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb “If|אִם־\rb* \rb you weave|תַּאַרְגִ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the seven|שֶׁ֛בַע\rb* \rb braids|מַחְלְפ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of my head|רֹאשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb into|עִם־\rb* \rb the web of a loom and tighten it with a pin, I will become as weak as any other man.|הַמַּסָּֽכֶת׃\rb*\f + \fr 16:13 \ft See LXX and Vulgate; Hebrew does not include \fqa and tighten it with a pin, I will become as weak as any other man.\f*”
