\p \v 21 \rb Then the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb seized him,|וַיֹּאחֲז֣וּהוּ\rb* \rb gouged out|וַֽיְנַקְּר֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his eyes,|עֵינָ֑יו\rb* \rb and brought him down|וַיּוֹרִ֨ידוּ\rb*\rb |אוֹת֜וֹ\rb* \rb to Gaza,|עַזָּ֗תָה\rb* \rb where he was bound|וַיַּאַסְר֙וּהוּ֙\rb* \rb with bronze shackles|בַּֽנְחֻשְׁתַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb and forced|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to grind|טוֹחֵ֖ן\rb* \rb grain in the prison.|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb*\rb |הָאֲסִירִים׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb However, the hair|שְׂעַר־\rb* \rb of his head|רֹאשׁ֛וֹ\rb* \rb began|וַיָּ֧חֶל\rb* \rb to grow|לְצַמֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb back after|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb it had been shaved.|גֻּלָּֽח׃פ\rb*
\s1 Samson’s Vengeance and Death
\p \v 23 \rb Now the lords|וְסַרְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֗ים\rb* \rb gathered together|נֶֽאֱסְפוּ֙\rb* \rb to offer|לִזְבֹּ֧חַ\rb* \rb a great|גָּד֛וֹל\rb* \rb sacrifice|זֶֽבַח־\rb* \rb to their god|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb Dagon.|לְדָג֥וֹן\rb* \rb They rejoiced|וּלְשִׂמְחָ֑ה\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “Our god|אֱלֹהֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb has delivered|נָתַ֤ן\rb* \rb Samson|שִׁמְשׁ֥וֹן\rb* \rb our enemy|אוֹיְבֵֽינוּ׃\rb* \rb into our hands.”|בְּיָדֵ֔נוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb And when the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb saw him,|וַיִּרְא֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb they praised|וַֽיְהַלְל֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their god,|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb saying:|כִּ֣י\rb*
\q1 \rb “Our god|אֱלֹהֵ֤ינוּ\rb* \rb has delivered|נָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb into our hands|בְיָדֵ֙נוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\q2 \rb our enemy|א֣וֹיְבֵ֔נוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb who destroyed|מַחֲרִ֣יב\rb* \rb our land|אַרְצֵ֔נוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and|וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb multiplied|הִרְבָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb our dead.”|חֲלָלֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb And|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb while their hearts|לִבָּ֔ם\rb*\rb |כִּי\rb* \rb were merry,|טוֹב\rb* \rb they said,|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “Call|קִרְא֥וּ\rb* \rb for Samson|לְשִׁמְשׁ֖וֹן\rb* \rb to entertain|וִישַֽׂחֶק־\rb* \rb us.”|לָ֑נוּ\rb* \rb So they called|וַיִּקְרְא֨וּ\rb* \rb Samson|לְשִׁמְשׁ֜וֹן\rb* \rb out of the prison|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |האסירים\rb* \rb to entertain them.|וַיְצַחֵק֙\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb And they stationed|וַיַּעֲמִ֥ידוּ\rb* \rb him|אוֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the pillars.|הָעַמּוּדִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb Samson|שִׁמְשׁ֜וֹן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the servant|הַנַּ֨עַר\rb* \rb who held|הַמַּחֲזִ֣יק\rb* \rb his hand,|בְּיָדוֹ֮\rb* \rb “Lead|הַנִּ֣יחָה\rb* \rb me|אוֹתִי֒\rb* \rb where I can feel|וְהֵימִשֵׁנִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the pillars|הָֽעַמֻּדִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb supporting|נָכ֣וֹן\rb* \rb the temple,|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb so I can lean|וְאֶשָּׁעֵ֖ן\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb against them.”|עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb Now the temple|וְהַבַּ֗יִת\rb* \rb was full|מָלֵ֤א\rb* \rb of men|הָֽאֲנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb and women;|וְהַנָּשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the lords|סַרְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb were there,|וְשָׁ֕מָּה\rb* \rb and about three|כִּשְׁלֹ֤שֶׁת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִים֙\rb* \rb men|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and women|וְאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb were on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the roof|הַגָּ֗ג\rb* \rb watching|הָרֹאִ֖ים\rb* \rb Samson|שִׁמְשֽׁוֹן׃\rb* \rb entertain them.|בִּשְׂח֥וֹק\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb Then Samson|שִׁמְשׁ֛וֹן\rb* \rb called out|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD:|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb “O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD,|יֱהֹוִ֡ה\rb* \rb please|נָא֩\rb* \rb remember me.|זָכְרֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb Strengthen me,|וְחַזְּקֵ֨נִי\rb*\rb |נָ֜א\rb* \rb O God,|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb just|אַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb once more,|הַפַּ֤עַם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb so that with one|אַחַ֛ת\rb* \rb vengeful blow|נְקַם־\rb* \rb I may pay back|וְאִנָּקְמָ֧ה\rb* \rb the Philistines|מִפְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃\rb* \rb for my two|מִשְּׁתֵ֥י\rb* \rb eyes.”|עֵינַ֖י\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb And Samson|שִׁמְשׁ֜וֹן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb reached out|וַיִּלְפֹּ֨ת\rb* \rb for the two|שְׁנֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb central|הַתָּ֗וֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb pillars|עַמּוּדֵ֣י\rb* \rb supporting|נָכ֣וֹן\rb* \rb the temple.|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb Bracing himself|וַיִּסָּמֵ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb with his right hand|בִּימִינ֖וֹ\rb* \rb on one pillar|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb and his left hand|בִּשְׂמֹאלֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb on the other,|וְאֶחָ֥ד\rb* \v 30 \rb Samson|שִׁמְשׁ֗וֹן\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Let me|נַפְשִׁי֮\rb* \rb die|תָּמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb the Philistines.”|פְּלִשְׁתִּים֒\rb*
\p \rb Then he pushed|וַיֵּ֣ט\rb* \rb with all his might,|בְּכֹ֔חַ\rb* \rb and the temple|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the lords|הַסְּרָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people in it.|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb So in his death|בְּמוֹת֔וֹ\rb*\rb |הַמֵּתִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he killed|הֵמִ֣ית\rb* \rb more|רַבִּ֕ים\rb* \rb than|מֵאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he had killed|הֵמִ֖ית\rb* \rb in his life.|בְּחַיָּֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb Then Samson’s brothers|אֶחָ֜יו\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb and his father’s|אָבִיהוּ֮\rb*\rb |וַיִּשְׂא֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֒\rb* \rb family|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb came down,|וַיֵּרְד֨וּ\rb* \rb carried him back,|וַֽיַּעֲל֣וּ׀\rb* \rb and buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb him|אוֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֤ין\rb* \rb Zorah|צָרְעָה֙\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and Eshtaol|אֶשְׁתָּאֹ֔ל\rb* \rb in the tomb|בְּקֶ֖בֶר\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb Manoah.|מָנ֣וֹחַ\rb* \rb And he|וְה֛וּא\rb* \rb had judged|שָׁפַ֥ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָֽה׃פ\rb*
\c 17
\s1 Micah’s Idolatry
\p \v 1 \rb Now|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb named|וּשְׁמ֥וֹ\rb* \rb Micah|מִיכָֽיְהוּ׃\rb* \rb from the hill country|מֵֽהַר־\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרָ֖יִם\rb* \v 2 \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to his mother,|לְאִמּ֡וֹ\rb* \rb “The eleven|אֶלֶף֩\rb* \rb hundred shekels|וּמֵאָ֨ה\rb* \rb of silver|הַכֶּ֜סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 17:2 \fqa 1,100 shekels \ft is approximately 27.6 pounds or 12.5 kilograms of silver; also in verse 3.\f* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb were taken|לֻֽקַּֽח־\rb* \rb from you|לָ֗ךְ\rb* \rb and|וְגַם֙\rb* \rb about which I heard|בְּאָזְנַ֔י\rb* \rb you|וְאַתִּי\rb* \rb utter|אָמַ֣רְתְּ\rb* \rb a curse—|אָלִית֙\rb* \rb I have|הִנֵּֽה־\rb* \rb the silver here|הַכֶּ֥סֶף\rb* \rb with me;|אִתִּ֖י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb took it.”|לְקַחְתִּ֑יו\rb*
\p \rb Then his mother|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb said,|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Blessed be|בָּר֥וּךְ\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִ֖י\rb* \rb by the LORD!”|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb And when he had returned|וַיָּ֛שֶׁב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the eleven|אֶֽלֶף־\rb* \rb hundred|וּמֵאָ֥ה\rb* \rb shekels of silver|הַכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb to his mother,|לְאִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb she|אִמּ֡וֹ\rb* \rb said,|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “I wholly dedicate|הַקְדֵּ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |הִקְדַּ֣שְׁתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the silver|הַכֶּסֶף֩\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֨ה\rb*\rb |מִיָּדִ֜י\rb* \rb for my son’s benefit,|לִבְנִ֗י\rb* \rb to make|לַֽעֲשׂוֹת֙\rb* \rb a graven image|פֶּ֣סֶל\rb* \rb and a molten idol.|וּמַסֵּכָ֔ה\rb* \rb Therefore I will now|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb return it|אֲשִׁיבֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb to you.”|לָֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb So he returned|וַיָּ֥שֶׁב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the silver|הַכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb to his mother,|לְאִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and she|אִמּוֹ֩\rb* \rb took|וַתִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb two hundred shekels|מָאתַ֨יִם\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֜סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 17:4 \fqa 200 shekels \ft is approximately 5 pounds or 2.3 kilograms of silver.\f* \rb and gave them|וַתִּתְּנֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb to a silversmith,|לַצּוֹרֵ֗ף\rb* \rb who made them|וַֽיַּעֲשֵׂ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb into a graven image|פֶּ֣סֶל\rb* \rb and a molten idol.|וּמַסֵּכָ֔ה\rb* \rb And they were placed|וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of Micah.|מִיכָֽיְהוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Now this man|וְהָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb Micah|מִיכָ֔ה\rb* \rb had|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb a shrine,|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb and he made|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb an ephod|אֵפוֹד֙\rb* \rb and some household idols,|וּתְרָפִ֔ים\rb* \rb and ordained|וַיְמַלֵּ֗א\rb*\f + \fr 17:5 \ft Hebrew \fqa filled the hand of\ft ; also in verse 12\f* \rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |יַ֤ד\rb*\rb one|אַחַד֙\rb* \rb of his sons|מִבָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb as|וַיְהִי־\rb* \rb his|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb priest.|לְכֹהֵֽן׃\rb* \v 6 \rb In those|הָהֵ֔ם\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb there was no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb in Israel;|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb everyone|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb did what was|יַעֲשֶֽׂה׃פ\rb* \rb right|הַיָּשָׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in his own eyes.|בְּעֵינָ֖יו\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb And there was|וַיְהִי־\rb* \rb a young|נַ֗עַר\rb*\rb |וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb Levite|לֵוִ֖י\rb*\rb |מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb from Bethlehem|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb* \rb in Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb who|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb had been residing|גָֽר־\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb* \rb within the clan|מִמִּשְׁפַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \v 8 \rb This man|הָאִ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb left|וַיֵּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb the city|מֵהָעִ֗יר\rb*\rb |מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Bethlehem|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb* \rb in Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb to settle|לָג֖וּר\rb* \rb where|בַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he could find a place.|יִמְצָ֑א\rb* \rb And as he traveled,|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |דַּרְכּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb he came|וַיָּבֹ֧א\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb Micah’s|מִיכָ֖ה\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb in the hill country|הַר־\rb* \rb of Ephraim.|אֶפְרַ֛יִם\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb “Where|מֵאַ֣יִן\rb* \rb are you from?”|תָּב֑וֹא\rb* \rb Micah|מִיכָ֖ה\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּאמֶר־\rb* \rb him.|ל֥וֹ\rb*
\p \rb “I|אָנֹ֗כִי\rb* \rb am a Levite|לֵוִ֣י\rb*\rb |מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb from Bethlehem|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb* \rb in Judah,”|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb he replied,|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb “and I|וְאָנֹכִ֣י\rb* \rb am on my way|הֹלֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb to settle|לָג֖וּר\rb* \rb wherever|בַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I can find a place.”|אֶמְצָֽא׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb “Stay|שְׁבָ֣ה\rb* \rb with me,”|עִמָּדִ֗י\rb* \rb Micah|מִיכָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to him,|ל֨וֹ\rb* \rb “and be|וֶֽהְיֵה־\rb* \rb my|לִי֮\rb* \rb father|לְאָ֣ב\rb* \rb and priest,|וּלְכֹהֵן֒\rb* \rb and I|וְאָנֹכִ֨י\rb* \rb will give|אֶֽתֶּן־\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֜\rb* \rb ten shekels|עֲשֶׂ֤רֶת\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֙סֶף֙\rb*\f + \fr 17:10 \fqa 10 shekels \ft is approximately 4 ounces or 114 grams of silver.\f* \rb per year,|לַיָּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb a suit|וְעֵ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb of clothes,|בְּגָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb and your provisions.”|וּמִחְיָתֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\p \rb So the Levite|הַלֵּוִֽי׃\rb* \rb went in|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \v 11 \rb and agreed|וַיּ֥וֹאֶל\rb*\rb |הַלֵּוִ֖י\rb* \rb to stay|לָשֶׁ֣בֶת\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb him,|הָאִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb and the young man|הַנַּ֙עַר֙\rb* \rb became|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb like a|כְּאַחַ֖ד\rb* \rb son|מִבָּנָֽיו׃\rb* \rb to Micah.|ל֔וֹ\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Micah|מִיכָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb ordained|וַיְמַלֵּ֤א\rb*\rb |יַ֣ד\rb* \rb the Levite,|הַלֵּוִ֔י\rb* \rb and the young man|הַנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb became|וַיְהִי־\rb* \rb his|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb priest|לְכֹהֵ֑ן\rb* \rb and lived|וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb in his|מִיכָֽה׃\rb* \rb house.|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \v 13 \rb Then Micah|מִיכָ֔ה\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Now|עַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb I know|יָדַ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will be good|יֵיטִ֥יב\rb* \rb to me,|לִ֑י\rb* \rb because|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb a Levite|הַלֵּוִ֖י\rb* \rb has become|הָיָה־\rb* \rb my|לִ֛י\rb* \rb priest.”|לְכֹהֵֽן׃\rb*
\c 18
\s1 The Danites Settle in Laish
\p \v 1 \rb In those|הָהֵ֔ם\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb there was no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb in Israel,|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and|וּבַיָּמִ֣ים\rb*\rb |הָהֵ֗ם\rb* \rb the tribe|שֵׁ֣בֶט\rb* \rb of the Danites|הַדָּנִ֞י\rb* \rb was looking for|מְבַקֶּשׁ־\rb*\rb |ל֤וֹ\rb* \rb territory|נַֽחֲלָה֙\rb* \rb to occupy.|לָשֶׁ֔בֶת\rb* \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb up to|עַד־\rb* \rb that|הַה֛וּא\rb* \rb time|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb they had not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb come into|נָ֨פְלָה\rb*\rb |לּ֜וֹ\rb* \rb an inheritance|בְּנַחֲלָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb among|בְּתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \v 2 \rb So the Danites|בְנֵי־\rb*\rb |דָ֣ן׀\rb* \rb sent out|וַיִּשְׁלְח֣וּ\rb* \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb from their clans,|מִֽמִּשְׁפַּחְתָּ֡ם\rb*\rb |מִקְצוֹתָם֩\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֨ים\rb* \rb of|בְּנֵי־\rb* \rb valor|חַ֜יִל\rb* \rb from Zorah|מִצָּרְעָ֣ה\rb* \rb and Eshtaol,|וּמֵֽאֶשְׁתָּאֹ֗ל\rb* \rb to spy out|לְרַגֵּ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb and explore it.|וּלְחָקְרָ֔הּ\rb* \rb “Go|לְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb and explore|חִקְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land,”|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb they told them.|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb*
\p \rb The men entered|וַיָּבֹ֤אוּ\rb* \rb the hill country|הַר־\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb and came to|עַד־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Micah,|מִיכָ֔ה\rb* \rb where they spent the night.|וַיָּלִ֖ינוּ\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb* \v 3 \rb And while they|הֵ֚מָּה\rb* \rb were near|עִם־\rb* \rb Micah’s|מִיכָ֔ה\rb* \rb house,|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb they|וְהֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb recognized|הִכִּ֔ירוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the voice|ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb of the young|הַנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb Levite;|הַלֵּוִ֑י\rb* \rb so they went over|וַיָּס֣וּרוּ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֗ם\rb* \rb and asked|וַיֹּ֤אמְרוּ\rb* \rb him,|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb “Who|מִֽי־\rb* \rb brought|הֱבִיאֲךָ֣\rb* \rb you here?|הֲלֹ֔ם\rb* \rb What|וּמָֽה־\rb* \rb are you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb doing|עֹשֶׂ֛ה\rb* \rb in this place?|בָּזֶ֖ה\rb* \rb Why|וּמַה־\rb* \rb are you|לְּךָ֥\rb* \rb here?”|פֹֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb “Micah|מִיכָ֑ה\rb* \rb has done|עָ֥שָׂה\rb* \rb this|כָּזֹ֣ה\rb* \rb and that|וְכָזֶ֔ה\rb* \rb for me,”|לִ֖י\rb* \rb he replied,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb “and he has hired me|וַיִּשְׂכְּרֵ֕נִי\rb* \rb to be|וָאֱהִי־\rb* \rb his|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb priest.”|לְכֹהֵֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Then they said|וַיֹּ֥אמְרוּ\rb* \rb to him,|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb “Please|נָ֣א\rb* \rb inquire|שְׁאַל־\rb* \rb of God|בֵאלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb to determine|וְנֵ֣דְעָ֔ה\rb* \rb whether we|אֲנַ֖חְנוּ\rb*\rb |הֹלְכִ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb will have a successful|הֲתַצְלִ֣יחַ\rb* \rb journey.”|דַּרְכֵּ֔נוּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb And the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb them,|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb “Go|לְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb in peace.|לְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb* \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb is watching over|נֹ֣כַח\rb* \rb your journey.”|דַּרְכְּכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |תֵּֽלְכוּ־\rb*\rb |בָֽהּ׃פ\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb So the five|חֲמֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb departed|וַיֵּלְכוּ֙\rb* \rb and came|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to Laish,|לָ֑יְשָׁה\rb* \rb where they saw|וַיִּרְא֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb that the people|הָעָ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |בְּקִרְבָּ֣הּ\rb* \rb were living|יוֹשֶֽׁבֶת־\rb* \rb securely,|לָ֠בֶטַח\rb* \rb like|כְּמִשְׁפַּ֨ט\rb* \rb the Sidonians,|צִדֹנִ֜ים\rb* \rb quiet|שֹׁקֵ֣ט׀\rb* \rb and unsuspecting.|וּבֹטֵ֗חַ\rb* \rb There was nothing|וְאֵין־\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֤ר\rb* \rb lacking|מַכְלִ֨ים\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb and no oppressive|יוֹרֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb ruler.|עֶ֔צֶר\rb* \rb And they|הֵ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb were far away|וּרְחֹקִ֥ים\rb* \rb from the Sidonians|מִצִּ֣דֹנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and had no|אֵין־\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb alliance|וְדָבָ֥ר\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb anyone.|אָדָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb When the men returned|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֲחֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb Zorah|צָרְעָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Eshtaol,|וְאֶשְׁתָּאֹ֑ל\rb* \rb their brothers|אֲחֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּאמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb them,|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb “What|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb did you find?”|אַתֶּֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb They answered,|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb “Come on,|ק֚וּמָה\rb* \rb let us go up|וְנַעֲלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb against them,|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb we have seen|רָאִ֙ינוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land,|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb and it is very|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb good.|טוֹבָ֖ה\rb* \rb Why would you fail to act?|וְאַתֶּ֣ם\rb*\rb |מַחְשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb hesitate|תֵּעָ֣צְל֔וּ\rb* \rb to go there|לָלֶ֥כֶת\rb*\rb |לָבֹ֖א\rb* \rb and take possession of|לָרֶ֥שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land!|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb When you enter,|כְּבֹאֲכֶ֞ם\rb* \rb you will come|תָּבֹ֣אוּ׀\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb an unsuspecting|בֹּטֵ֗חַ\rb* \rb people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb and a spacious|רַחֲבַ֣ת\rb*\rb |יָדַ֔יִם\rb* \rb land,|וְהָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb has delivered it|נְתָנָ֥הּ\rb* \rb into your hand.|בְּיֶדְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb It is a place|מָקוֹם֙\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb nothing|אֵֽין־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֣ם\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb on earth|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb is lacking.”|מַחְס֔וֹר\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb So six|שֵֽׁשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb Danites|הַדָּנִ֔י\rb* \rb departed|וַיִּסְע֤וּ\rb* \rb from|מִשָּׁם֙\rb*\rb |מִמִּשְׁפַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb Zorah|מִצָּרְעָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Eshtaol,|וּמֵאֶשְׁתָּאֹ֑ל\rb* \rb armed|חָג֖וּר\rb* \rb with weapons|כְּלֵ֥י\rb* \rb of war.|מִלְחָמָֽה׃\rb* \v 12 \rb They went up|וַֽיַּעֲל֗וּ\rb* \rb and camped|וַֽיַּחֲנ֛וּ\rb*\rb |בְּקִרְיַ֥ת\rb* \rb at Kiriath-jearim|יְעָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb in Judah.|בִּֽיהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb That is why|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֡ן\rb* \rb the|הַה֜וּא\rb* \rb place|לַמָּק֨וֹם\rb* \rb west|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb*\rb |קִרְיַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Kiriath-jearim|יְעָרִֽים׃\rb* \rb is called|קָרְאוּ֩\rb*\rb |מַחֲנֵה־\rb* \rb Mahaneh-dan|דָ֗ן\rb*\f + \fr 18:12 \fqa Mahaneh-dan \ft means \fqa camp of Dan\ft .\f* \rb to|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֕ה\rb* \rb day.|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \v 13 \rb And from there|מִשָּׁ֖ם\rb* \rb they traveled|וַיַּעַבְר֥וּ\rb* \rb to the hill country|הַר־\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and came|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb Micah’s|מִיכָֽה׃\rb* \rb house.|בֵּ֥ית\rb*
\s1 The Danites Take Micah’s Idols
\p \v 14 \rb |וַֽיַּעֲנ֞וּ\rb* \rb Then the five|חֲמֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb who had gone|הַהֹלְכִים֮\rb* \rb to spy out|לְרַגֵּל֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Laish|לַיִשׁ֒\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their brothers,|אֲחֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb “Did you know|הַיְדַעְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb one of these|הָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb houses|בַּבָּתִּ֤ים\rb* \rb has|יֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb an ephod,|אֵפ֣וֹד\rb* \rb household gods,|וּתְרָפִ֔ים\rb* \rb a graven image,|וּפֶ֖סֶל\rb* \rb and a molten idol?|וּמַסֵּכָ֑ה\rb* \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb think about|דְּע֥וּ\rb* \rb what|מַֽה־\rb* \rb you should do.”|תַּעֲשֽׂוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb So they turned|וַיָּס֣וּרוּ\rb* \rb aside there|שָׁ֔מָּה\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּבֹ֛אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the home|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of the young|הַנַּ֥עַר\rb* \rb Levite,|הַלֵּוִ֖י\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Micah,|מִיכָ֑ה\rb* \rb and greeted him.|וַיִּשְׁאֲלוּ־\rb*\rb |ל֖וֹ\rb*\rb |לְשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb The six|וְשֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb Danites|מִבְּנֵי־\rb*\rb |דָֽן׃\rb*\rb |אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb stood|נִצָּבִ֖ים\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb of the gate,|הַשָּׁ֑עַר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb armed|חֲגוּרִים֙\rb* \rb with their weapons|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of war.|מִלְחַמְתָּ֔ם\rb* \v 17 \rb |וַֽיַּעֲל֞וּ\rb* \rb And the five|חֲמֵ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb who had gone|הַהֹלְכִים֮\rb* \rb to spy out|לְרַגֵּ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָרֶץ֒\rb* \rb went inside|בָּ֣אוּ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔מָּה\rb* \rb and took|לָקְח֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the graven image,|הַפֶּ֙סֶל֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the ephod,|הָ֣אֵפ֔וֹד\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the household idols,|הַתְּרָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the molten idol,|הַמַּסֵּכָ֑ה\rb* \rb while the priest|וְהַכֹּהֵ֗ן\rb* \rb stood|נִצָּב֙\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb of the gate|הַשַּׁ֔עַר\rb* \rb with the six|וְשֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֣וֹת\rb* \rb armed|הֶחָג֖וּר\rb*\rb |כְּלֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַמִּלְחָמָֽה׃\rb* \rb men.|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb When they|וְאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb entered|בָּ֚אוּ\rb* \rb Micah’s|מִיכָ֔ה\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb and took|וַיִּקְחוּ֙\rb* \rb the graven image,|פֶּ֣סֶל\rb* \rb the ephod,|הָאֵפ֔וֹד\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the household idols,|הַתְּרָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the molten idol,|הַמַּסֵּכָ֑ה\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb “What|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb are you|אַתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb doing?”|עֹשִֽׂים׃\rb*
