\c 19
\s1 The Crime of the Benjamites
\r \ref Genesis 19:1–11|GEN 19:1-11\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Now|וַיְהִי֙\rb* \rb in those|הָהֵ֔ם\rb* \rb days,|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb when there was no|אֵ֣ין\rb* \rb king|וּמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb in Israel,|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb a Levite|לֵוִ֗י\rb* \rb who lived|גָּ֚ר\rb* \rb in the remote|בְּיַרְכְּתֵ֣י\rb* \rb hill country|הַר־\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb took|וַיִּֽקַּֽח־\rb* \rb for himself|לוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb a concubine|פִילֶ֔גֶשׁ\rb*\rb |מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb from Bethlehem|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb in Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 2 \rb But she|פִּֽילַגְשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb was unfaithful|וַתִּזְנֶ֤ה\rb* \rb to him|עָלָיו֙\rb*\f + \fr 19:2 \ft LXX \fqa became angry with him\f* \rb and left|וַתֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb him|מֵֽאִתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb to return to|אֶל־\rb* \rb her father’s|אָבִ֔יהָ\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb Bethlehem|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb in Judah.|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb After she had been|וַתְּהִי־\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֕ם\rb*\rb |יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb four|אַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb* \rb months,|חֳדָשִֽׁים׃\rb* \v 3 \rb her husband|אִישָׁ֜הּ\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֨קָם\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb after her|אַחֲרֶ֗יהָ\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb kindly|לִבָּהּ֙\rb* \rb to her|עַל־\rb* \rb and bring her back,|לַהֲשִׁיבוֹ\rb* \rb taking his servant|וְנַעֲר֥וֹ\rb*\rb |עִמּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and a pair|וְצֶ֣מֶד\rb* \rb of donkeys.|חֲמֹרִ֑ים\rb* \rb So the girl brought him|וַתְּבִיאֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb into her father’s|אָבִ֔יהָ\rb* \rb house,|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb and when her|הַֽנַּעֲרָ֔ה\rb* \rb father|אֲבִ֣י\rb* \rb saw him,|וַיִּרְאֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb he gladly|וַיִּשְׂמַ֖ח\rb* \rb welcomed him.|לִקְרָאתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 4 \rb His father-in-law,|חֹֽתְנוֹ֙\rb* \rb the girl’s|הַֽנַּעֲרָ֔ה\rb* \rb father,|אֲבִ֣י\rb* \rb persuaded him to stay,|וַיֶּחֱזַק־\rb*\rb |בּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb so he remained|וַיֵּ֥שֶׁב\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb days,|יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb eating,|וַיֹּאכְלוּ֙\rb* \rb drinking,|וַיִּשְׁתּ֔וּ\rb* \rb and lodging|וַיָּלִ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb there.|שָֽׁם׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb On the fourth|הָרְבִיעִ֔י\rb* \rb day,|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb they got up early|וַיַּשְׁכִּ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb in the morning|בַבֹּ֖קֶר\rb* \rb and prepared|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb to depart,|לָלֶ֑כֶת\rb* \rb but the girl’s|הַֽנַּעֲרָ֜ה\rb* \rb father|אֲבִ֨י\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his son-in-law,|חֲתָנ֗וֹ\rb* \rb “Refresh|סְעָ֧ד\rb* \rb your heart|לִבְּךָ֛\rb* \rb with a morsel|פַּת־\rb* \rb of bread,|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb and then|וְאַחַ֥ר\rb* \rb you can go.”|תֵּלֵֽכוּ׃\rb* \v 6 \rb So they sat down|וַיֵּשְׁב֗וּ\rb* \rb and the two|שְׁנֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb of them ate|וַיֹּאכְל֧וּ\rb* \rb and drank|וַיִּשְׁתּ֑וּ\rb* \rb together.|יַחְדָּ֖ו\rb* \rb Then the girl’s|הַֽנַּעֲרָה֙\rb* \rb father|אֲבִ֤י\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֜אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the man,|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb “Please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb agree|הֽוֹאֶל־\rb* \rb to stay overnight|וְלִ֖ין\rb* \rb and let your heart|לִבֶּֽךָ׃\rb* \rb be merry.”|וְיִטַ֥ב\rb* \v 7 \rb The man|הָאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֥קָם\rb* \rb to depart,|לָלֶ֑כֶת\rb* \rb but his father-in-law|חֹתְנ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וַיָּ֖שָׁב\rb* \rb persuaded|וַיִּפְצַר־\rb* \rb him,|בּוֹ֙\rb* \rb so he stayed|וַיָּ֥לֶן\rb* \rb there that night.|שָֽׁם׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb On the fifth|הַחֲמִישִׁי֮\rb* \rb day,|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb he got up early|וַיַּשְׁכֵּ֨ם\rb* \rb in the morning|בַּבֹּ֜קֶר\rb* \rb to depart,|לָלֶכֶת֒\rb* \rb but the girl’s|הַֽנַּעֲרָ֗ה\rb* \rb father|אֲבִ֣י\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb* \rb “Please|נָא֙\rb* \rb refresh|סְעָד־\rb* \rb your heart.”|לְבָ֣בְךָ֔\rb* \rb So they waited|וְהִֽתְמַהְמְה֖וּ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb late afternoon|נְט֣וֹת\rb*\rb |הַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb and the two|שְׁנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb of them ate.|וַיֹּאכְל֖וּ\rb* \v 9 \rb When the man|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֤קָם\rb* \rb to depart|לָלֶ֔כֶת\rb*\rb |ה֥וּא\rb* \rb with his concubine|וּפִילַגְשׁ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and his servant,|וְנַעֲר֑וֹ\rb* \rb his father-in-law,|חֹתְנ֣וֹ\rb* \rb the girl’s|הַֽנַּעֲרָ֡ה\rb* \rb father,|אֲבִ֣י\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb “Look,|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֜וֹם\rb* \rb is drawing|רָפָ֨ה\rb* \rb to a close.|לַעֲרֹ֗ב\rb* \rb Please|נָא֩\rb* \rb spend the night.|לִֽינוּ־\rb*\rb |נָ֞א\rb* \rb See,|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb the day|הַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb is almost over.|חֲנ֤וֹת\rb* \rb Spend the night|לִ֥ין\rb* \rb here,|פֹּה֙\rb* \rb that your heart|לְבָבֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb may be merry.|וְיִיטַ֣ב\rb* \rb Then you can get up early|וְהִשְׁכַּמְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb tomorrow|מָחָר֙\rb* \rb for your journey|לְדַרְכְּכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְהָלַכְתָּ֖\rb* \rb home.”|לְאֹהָלֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb But the man|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb was unwilling|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |אָבָ֤ה\rb* \rb to spend the night.|לָל֔וּן\rb* \rb He got up|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb and departed,|וַיֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb and arrived|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb opposite|נֹ֣כַח\rb* \rb Jebus|יְב֔וּס\rb* \rb (that is,|הִ֖יא\rb* \rb Jerusalem),|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb with|וְעִמּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb his two|צֶ֤מֶד\rb* \rb saddled|חֲבוּשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb donkeys|חֲמוֹרִים֙\rb* \rb and his concubine.|וּפִילַגְשׁ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |עִמּֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb When they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb were near|עִם־\rb* \rb Jebus|יְב֔וּס\rb* \rb and the day|וְהַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb was almost|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb gone,|רַ֣ד\rb* \rb the servant|הַנַּ֜עַר\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his master,|אֲדֹנָ֗יו\rb*\rb |לְכָה־\rb* \rb “Please,|נָּ֛א\rb* \rb let us stop|וְנָס֛וּרָה\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb Jebusite|הַיְבוּסִ֥י\rb* \rb city|עִֽיר־\rb* \rb and spend the night|וְנָלִ֥ין\rb* \rb here.”|בָּֽהּ׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb But his master|אֲדֹנָ֔יו\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb “We will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb turn aside|נָסוּר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the city|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of foreigners,|נָכְרִ֔י\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb there are no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb Israelites.|מִבְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |הֵ֑נָּה\rb* \rb We will go on|וְעָבַ֖רְנוּ\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb Gibeah.”|גִּבְעָֽה׃\rb* \v 13 \rb He continued,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |לְנַעֲר֔וֹ\rb* \rb “Come,|לְךָ֥\rb* \rb let us try to reach|וְנִקְרְבָ֖ה\rb* \rb one|בְּאַחַ֣ד\rb* \rb of these towns|הַמְּקֹמ֑וֹת\rb* \rb to spend the night|וְלַ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb in Gibeah|בַגִּבְעָ֖ה\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb* \rb Ramah.”|בָרָמָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb So they continued|וַיֵּלֵ֑כוּ\rb* \rb on their journey,|וַיַּעַבְר֖וּ\rb* \rb and the sun|הַשֶּׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb* \rb set|וַתָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb as they neared|אֵ֥צֶל\rb* \rb Gibeah|הַגִּבְעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in Benjamin.|לְבִנְיָמִֽן׃\rb* \v 15 \rb They stopped|וַיָּסֻ֣רוּ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb to go in|לָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb and lodge|לָל֣וּן\rb* \rb in Gibeah.|בַּגִּבְעָ֑ה\rb* \rb The Levite went in|וַיָּבֹ֗א\rb* \rb and sat down|וַיֵּ֙שֶׁב֙\rb* \rb in the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb square,|בִּרְח֣וֹב\rb* \rb but no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb one|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb would take|מְאַסֵּֽף־\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֥ם\rb* \rb into his home|הַבַּ֖יְתָה\rb* \rb for the night.|לָלֽוּן׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb |וְהִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb That evening|בָּעֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb an old|זָקֵ֗ן\rb* \rb man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |וְהָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb from the hill country|מֵהַ֣ר\rb* \rb of Ephraim,|אֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |וְהוּא־\rb* \rb who was residing|גָ֖ר\rb* \rb in Gibeah|בַּגִּבְעָ֑ה\rb* \rb (the men|וְאַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of that place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb were Benjamites),|יְמִינִֽי׃\rb* \rb came in|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb from|מִֽן־\rb* \rb his work|מַעֲשֵׂ֤הוּ\rb* \rb in|מִן־\rb* \rb the field.|הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb* \v 17 \rb When he looked up|וַיִּשָּׂ֣א\rb*\rb |עֵינָ֗יו\rb* \rb and saw|וַיַּ֛רְא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הָאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb the traveler|הָאֹרֵ֖חַ\rb* \rb in the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb* \rb square,|בִּרְחֹ֣ב\rb* \rb the old|הַזָּקֵ֛ן\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֧ישׁ\rb* \rb asked,|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb “Where|אָ֥נָה\rb* \rb are you going,|תֵלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb and where|וּמֵאַ֥יִן\rb* \rb have you come from?”|תָּבֽוֹא׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb The Levite replied,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb “We are|אֲנַ֜חְנוּ\rb* \rb traveling|עֹבְרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |מִבֵּֽית־\rb* \rb from Bethlehem|לֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb in Judah|יְהוּדָה֮\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the remote|יַרְכְּתֵ֣י\rb* \rb hill country|הַר־\rb* \rb of Ephraim,|אֶפְרַיִם֒\rb* \rb where|מִשָּׁ֣ם\rb* \rb I am from.|אָנֹ֔כִי\rb* \rb I went|וָאֵלֵ֕ךְ\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb Bethlehem|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb in Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and now I am|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb going|הֹלֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb of the LORD;|יְהוָה֙\rb*\f + \fr 19:18 \ft LXX \fqa I am going to my home\ft ; see verse 29.\f* \rb but no|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb one|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb has taken|מְאַסֵּ֥ף\rb* \rb me|אוֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb into his home,|הַבָּֽיְתָה׃\rb* \v 19 \rb even though there is|יֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb both|וְגַם־\rb* \rb straw|תֶּ֤בֶן\rb* \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb feed|מִסְפּוֹא֙\rb* \rb for our donkeys,|לַחֲמוֹרֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb and|וְ֠גַם\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb and wine|וָיַ֤יִן\rb*\rb |יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb for me|לִי֙\rb* \rb and the maidservant|וְלַֽאֲמָתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and young man|וְלַנַּ֖עַר\rb* \rb with me.|עִם־\rb* \rb There is nothing that|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb we, your servants,|עֲבָדֶ֑יךָ\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |דָּבָֽר׃\rb* \rb lack.”|מַחְס֖וֹר\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb “Peace|שָׁל֣וֹם\rb* \rb to you,”|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb the old|הַזָּקֵן֙\rb* \rb man.|הָאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb “Let me supply|עָלָ֑י\rb*\rb |רַ֥ק\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb you need.|מַחְסוֹרְךָ֖\rb* \rb Only|רַ֥ק\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb spend the night|תָּלַֽן׃\rb* \rb in the square.”|בָּרְח֖וֹב\rb* \v 21 \rb So he brought him|וַיְבִיאֵ֣הוּ\rb* \rb to his house|לְבֵית֔וֹ\rb* \rb and fed|וַיָּ֖בָול\rb* \rb his donkeys.|לַחֲמוֹרִ֑ים\rb* \rb And they washed|וַֽיִּרְחֲצוּ֙\rb* \rb their feet|רַגְלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and ate|וַיֹּאכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb and drank.|וַיִּשְׁתּֽוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb While they|הֵמָּה֮\rb* \rb were enjoying|מֵיטִיבִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb themselves,|לִבָּם֒\rb* \rb suddenly|וְהִנֵּה֩\rb* \rb the wicked|בְלִיַּ֗עַל\rb* \rb men|אַנְשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֜יר\rb*\rb |אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb surrounded|נָסַ֙בּוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house.|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb Pounding|מִֽתְדַּפְּקִ֖ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the door,|הַדָּ֑לֶת\rb* \rb they said|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the old|הַזָּקֵן֙\rb* \rb man|הָ֠אִישׁ\rb* \rb who owned|בַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb the house,|הַבַּ֤יִת\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “Bring out|הוֹצֵ֗א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb came|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your house,|בֵּיתְךָ֖\rb* \rb so we can have relations with him!”|וְנֵדָעֶֽנּוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb |הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb The owner|בַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb of the house|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb “No,|אַל־\rb* \rb my brothers,|אַחַ֖י\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb do this wicked thing!|תָּרֵ֣עוּ\rb*\rb |נָ֑א\rb* \rb After all,|אַ֠חֲרֵי\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אַל־\rb* \rb man|הָאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb is a guest|בָּ֞א\rb* \rb in my house.|בֵּיתִ֔י\rb* \rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb commit|תַּעֲשׂ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb outrage.|הַנְּבָלָ֥ה\rb* \v 24 \rb Look,|הִנֵּה֩\rb* \rb let me bring out|אוֹצִֽיאָה־\rb* \rb my virgin|הַבְּתוּלָ֜ה\rb* \rb daughter|בִתִּ֨י\rb* \rb and the man’s concubine,|וּפִֽילַגְשֵׁ֗הוּ\rb*\rb |נָּ֤א\rb*\rb |אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb and you can use|וְעַנּ֣וּ\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and do|וַעֲשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb with them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb as you wish.|הַטּ֖וֹב\rb*\rb |בְּעֵינֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb But do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb do|תַעֲשׂ֔וּ\rb* \rb such|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb a vile|הַנְּבָלָ֥ה\rb* \rb thing|דְּבַ֖ר\rb* \rb to this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb man.”|וְלָאִ֤ישׁ\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb But the men|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb would|אָב֤וּ\rb*\rb |הָאֲנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb listen to him.|לִשְׁמֹ֣עַֽ\rb* \rb So the Levite|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb took|וַיַּחֲזֵ֤ק\rb* \rb his concubine|בְּפִ֣ילַגְשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and sent her|וַיֹּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb outside|הַח֑וּץ\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and they raped|וַיֵּדְע֣וּ\rb* \rb her|א֠וֹתָהּ\rb* \rb and abused|וַיִּֽתְעַלְּלוּ־\rb* \rb her|בָ֤הּ\rb* \rb throughout|כָּל־\rb* \rb the night,|הַלַּ֙יְלָה֙\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |הַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb and at dawn|בַּעֲלוֹת\rb*\rb |הַשָּֽׁחַר׃\rb* \rb they let her go.|וַֽיְשַׁלְּח֖וּהָ\rb* \v 26 \rb Early that morning,|לִפְנ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |הַבֹּ֑קֶר\rb* \rb the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb went back|וַתָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּית־\rb*\rb |הָאִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb her master was staying,|אֲדוֹנֶ֥יהָ\rb* \rb collapsed|וַתִּפֹּ֞ל\rb* \rb at the doorway,|פֶּ֧תַח\rb* \rb and lay there until|עַד־\rb* \rb it was light.|הָאֽוֹר׃\rb*\rb |שָּׁ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb In the morning,|בַּבֹּ֗קֶר\rb* \rb when her master|אֲדֹנֶ֜יהָ\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֨קָם\rb* \rb and opened|וַיִּפְתַּח֙\rb* \rb the doors|דַּלְת֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb to go out|וַיֵּצֵ֖א\rb*\rb |לָלֶ֣כֶת\rb* \rb on his journey,|לְדַרְכּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb there was|וְהִנֵּ֧ה\rb*\rb |הָאִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb his concubine,|פִֽילַגְשׁ֗וֹ\rb* \rb collapsed|נֹפֶ֙לֶת֙\rb* \rb in the doorway|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb of the house,|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb with her hands|וְיָדֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the threshold.|הַסַּֽף׃\rb* \v 28 \rb “Get up,”|ק֥וּמִי\rb* \rb he told her.|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֛יהָ\rb* \rb “Let us go.”|וְנֵלֵ֖כָה\rb* \rb But there was no|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb response.|עֹנֶ֑ה\rb* \rb So the man|הָאִ֔ישׁ\rb*\rb |וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb put her|וַיִּקָּחֶ֙הָ֙\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb his donkey|הַחֲמ֔וֹר\rb* \rb and set out|וַיָּ֣קָם\rb* \rb for home.|לִמְקֹמֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb When he reached|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb his house,|בֵּית֗וֹ\rb* \rb he picked up|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a knife,|הַֽמַּאֲכֶ֙לֶת֙\rb* \rb took hold|וַיַּחֲזֵ֣ק\rb* \rb of his concubine,|בְּפִֽילַגְשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb cut her|וַֽיְנַתְּחֶ֙הָ֙\rb* \rb limb by limb|לַעֲצָמֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb into twelve|לִשְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb pieces,|נְתָחִ֑ים\rb* \rb and sent her|וַֽיְשַׁלְּחֶ֔הָ\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the territory|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 30 \rb And|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb everyone|כָל־\rb* \rb who saw|הָרֹאֶ֗ה\rb* \rb it said,|וְאָמַר֙\rb* \rb “Nothing|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb like this|כָּזֹ֔את\rb* \rb has been seen|נִרְאֲתָה֙\rb* \rb or done|נִהְיְתָ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb from the day|לְמִיּ֞וֹם\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb came out|עֲל֤וֹת\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb until|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day.|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Think it over,|שִֽׂימוּ־\rb*\rb |לָכֶ֥ם\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb take counsel,|עֻ֥צוּ\rb* \rb and speak up!”|וְדַבֵּֽרוּ׃פ\rb*
\c 20
\s1 The Decree of the Assembly
\p \v 1 \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb* \rb from Dan|לְמִדָּן֙\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |בְּאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb Beersheba|שֶׁ֔בַע\rb* \rb and from the land|וְאֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֑ד\rb* \rb came out,|וַיֵּצְאוּ֮\rb* \rb and the congregation|הָעֵדָ֜ה\rb* \rb assembled|וַתִּקָּהֵ֨ל\rb* \rb as one|אֶחָ֗ד\rb* \rb man|כְּאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb before|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb at Mizpah.|הַמִּצְפָּֽה׃\rb* \v 2 \rb The leaders|פִּנּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb and all|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb presented themselves|וַיִּֽתְיַצְּב֞וּ\rb* \rb in the assembly|בִּקְהַ֖ל\rb* \rb of God’s|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb people:|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb 400,000|אַרְבַּ֨ע\rb*\rb |מֵא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶ֛לֶף\rb* \rb men|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb on foot,|רַגְלִ֖י\rb* \rb armed|שֹׁ֥לֵֽף\rb* \rb with swords.|חָֽרֶב׃פ\rb* \v 3 \rb (Meanwhile the Benjamites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בִנְיָמִ֔ן\rb* \rb heard|וַֽיִּשְׁמְעוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb had gone up|עָל֥וּ\rb* \rb to Mizpah.)|הַמִּצְפָּ֑ה\rb* \rb And the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb asked,|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb “Tell|דַּבְּר֕וּ\rb* \rb us, how|אֵיכָ֥ה\rb* \rb did this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb wicked thing|הָרָעָ֥ה\rb* \rb happen?”|נִהְיְתָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb So the Levite,|הַלֵּוִ֗י\rb*\rb |אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb the husband|הָאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of the murdered|הַנִּרְצָחָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֑ר\rb* \rb woman,|הָאִשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb answered:|וַיַּ֜עַן\rb* \rb “I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb and my concubine|וּפִֽילַגְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb came|בָּ֛אתִי\rb* \rb to Gibeah|הַגִּבְעָ֙תָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Benjamin|לְבִנְיָמִ֔ן\rb* \rb to spend the night.|לָלֽוּן׃\rb* \v 5 \rb And during the night,|לָ֑יְלָה\rb* \rb the men|בַּעֲלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Gibeah|הַגִּבְעָ֔ה\rb* \rb rose up|וַיָּקֻ֤מוּ\rb* \rb against me|עָלַי֙\rb* \rb and surrounded|וַיָּסֹ֧בּוּ\rb*\rb |עָלַ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house.|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*\rb |אוֹתִי֙\rb* \rb They intended|דִּמּ֣וּ\rb* \rb to kill me,|לַהֲרֹ֔ג\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb but they abused|עִנּ֖וּ\rb* \rb my concubine,|פִּילַגְשִׁ֥י\rb* \rb and she died.|וַתָּמֹֽת׃\rb* \v 6 \rb Then I took|וָֽאֹחֵ֤ז\rb* \rb my concubine,|בְּפִֽילַגְשִׁי֙\rb* \rb cut her into pieces,|וָֽאֲנַתְּחֶ֔הָ\rb* \rb and sent her|וָֽאֲשַׁלְּחֶ֔הָ\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the land|שְׂדֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of Israel’s|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb inheritance,|נַחֲלַ֣ת\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they had committed|עָשׂ֛וּ\rb* \rb a lewd|זִמָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and disgraceful act|וּנְבָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Israel.|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 7 \rb Behold,|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb all|כֻלְּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb you Israelites,|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb give|הָב֥וּ\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb advice|דָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb and verdict|וְעֵצָ֖ה\rb* \rb here and now.”|הֲלֹֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb stood|וַיָּ֙קָם֙\rb* \rb as one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb man|כְּאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb and said,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Not one|לֹ֤א\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of us will return|נֵלֵךְ֙\rb* \rb to his tent|לְאָהֳל֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb or|נָס֖וּר\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb to his house.|לְבֵיתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 9 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb this|זֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb is what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb we will do|נַעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb to Gibeah:|לַגִּבְעָ֑ה\rb* \rb We will go against it|עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb as the lot dictates.|בְּגוֹרָֽל׃\rb* \v 10 \rb We will take|וְלָקַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָה֩\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֨ים\rb* \rb out of every hundred|לַמֵּאָ֜ה\rb* \rb from all|לְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb and a hundred|וּמֵאָ֤ה\rb* \rb out of every thousand,|לָאֶ֙לֶף֙\rb* \rb and a thousand|וְאֶ֣לֶף\rb* \rb out of every ten thousand,|לָרְבָבָ֔ה\rb* \rb to supply|לָקַ֥חַת\rb* \rb provisions|צֵדָ֖ה\rb* \rb for the army|לָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb when they go|לְבוֹאָם֙\rb* \rb to Gibeah|לְגֶ֣בַע\rb*\f + \fr 20:10 \ft One Hebrew manuscript; most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa Geba\ft , a variant of \fqa Gibeah\f* \rb in Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֔ן\rb* \rb to punish them|לַעֲשׂ֗וֹת\rb*\rb |כְּכָל־\rb* \rb for the atrocity|הַ֨נְּבָלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they have committed|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb in Israel.”|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
