\p \v 46 \rb That|הַה֑וּא\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |כָל־\rb*\rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb 25,000|עֶשְׂרִים֩\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶ֥לֶף\rb* \rb Benjamite|מִבִּנְיָמִ֗ן\rb*\rb |שֹׁ֥לֵֽף\rb* \rb swordsmen|חֶ֖רֶב\rb*\rb |אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb fell,|הַנֹּ֨פְלִ֜ים\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb men|אַנְשֵׁי־\rb* \rb of valor.|חָֽיִל׃\rb* \v 47 \rb But 600|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb men|אִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb turned|וַיִּפְנ֞וּ\rb* \rb and fled|וַיָּנֻ֤סוּ\rb* \rb into the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּ֙רָה֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the rock|סֶ֣לַע\rb* \rb of Rimmon,|הָֽרִמּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb where they stayed|וַיֵּֽשְׁבוּ֙\rb*\rb |בְּסֶ֣לַע\rb*\rb |רִמּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb four|אַרְבָּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb months.|חֳדָשִֽׁים׃\rb* \v 48 \rb And the men|וְאִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb turned back|שָׁ֣בוּ\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the other Benjamites|בְּנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |בִנְיָמִן֙\rb* \rb and put|וַיַּכּ֣וּם\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword|חֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb all|מְתֹם֙\rb* \rb the cities,|מֵעִ֤יר\rb* \rb including the animals|בְּהֵמָ֔ה\rb*\rb |עַ֖ד\rb* \rb and|עַד־\rb* \rb everything else|כָּל־\rb* \rb they found.|הַנִּמְצָ֑א\rb* \rb And they|גַּ֛ם\rb* \rb burned down|שִׁלְּח֥וּ\rb*\rb |בָאֵֽשׁ׃פ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the cities|הֶעָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb in their path.|הַנִּמְצָא֖וֹת\rb*
\c 21
\s1 Wives for the Benjamites
\p \v 1 \rb Now the men|וְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb had sworn an oath|נִשְׁבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb at Mizpah,|בַּמִּצְפָּ֖ה\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Not one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb of us|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb will give his daughter|בִּתּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb in marriage|יִתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb to a Benjamite.”|לְבִנְיָמִ֖ן\rb*\rb |לְאִשָּֽׁה׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb So the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb to Bethel|אֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and sat|וַיֵּ֤שְׁבוּ\rb* \rb there|שָׁם֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening,|הָעֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb lifting up|וַיִּשְׂא֣וּ\rb* \rb their voices|קוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb and weeping|וַיִּבְכּ֖וּ\rb*\rb |בְּכִ֥י\rb* \rb bitterly.|גָדֽוֹל׃\rb* \v 3 \rb “Why,|לָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb O LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,”|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb they cried out,|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “has this|זֹּ֖את\rb* \rb happened|הָ֥יְתָה\rb* \rb in Israel?|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb Today|הַיּ֛וֹם\rb* \rb in Israel|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb tribe|שֵׁ֥בֶט\rb* \rb is missing!”|לְהִפָּקֵ֥ד\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb The next day|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֔ת\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb got up early,|וַיַּשְׁכִּ֣ימוּ\rb* \rb built|וַיִּבְנוּ־\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb* \rb there,|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb and presented|וַיַּעֲל֥וּ\rb* \rb burnt offerings|עֹל֖וֹת\rb* \rb and peace offerings.|וּשְׁלָמִֽים׃פ\rb* \v 5 \rb The Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb asked,|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb “Who|מִ֠י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb among all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb come|עָלָ֧ה\rb* \rb to the assembly|בַקָּהָ֛ל\rb* \rb before|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD?”|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb they had taken|הָיְתָ֗ה\rb* \rb a solemn|הַגְּדוֹלָ֜ה\rb* \rb oath|הַשְּׁבוּעָ֨ה\rb* \rb that anyone|לַ֠אֲשֶׁר\rb* \rb who failed|לֹא־\rb* \rb to come up|עָלָ֨ה\rb* \rb before|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb at Mizpah|הַמִּצְפָּ֛ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb* \rb would surely be put to death.|מ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמָֽת׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb And the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb grieved|וַיִּנָּֽחֲמוּ֙\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb their brothers,|אָחִ֑יו\rb* \rb the Benjamites,|בִּנְיָמִ֖ן\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “Today|הַיּ֛וֹם\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb tribe|שֵׁ֥בֶט\rb* \rb is cut off|נִגְדַּ֥ע\rb* \rb from Israel.|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 7 \rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb should we do|נַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb about wives|לְנָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb for the survivors,|לַנּוֹתָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb since we|וַאֲנַ֙חְנוּ֙\rb* \rb have sworn|נִשְׁבַּ֣עְנוּ\rb* \rb by the LORD|בַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb not|לְבִלְתִּ֛י\rb* \rb to give|תֵּת־\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb our daughters|מִבְּנוֹתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb in marriage?”|לְנָשִֽׁים׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb So they asked,|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “Which|מִ֗י\rb* \rb one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb of the tribes|מִשִּׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb failed|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to come up|עָלָ֥ה\rb* \rb before|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb at Mizpah?”|הַמִּצְפָּ֑ה\rb* \rb And, in fact,|וְ֠הִנֵּה\rb* \rb no one|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |אִ֧ישׁ\rb* \rb from Jabesh-gilead|מִיָּבֵ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֖ד\rb* \rb had come|בָא־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֛ה\rb* \rb for the assembly.|הַקָּהָֽל׃\rb* \v 9 \rb For when the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb were counted,|וַיִּתְפָּקֵ֖ד\rb* \rb none|אֵֽין־\rb*\rb |אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb of the residents|מִיּוֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Jabesh-gilead|יָבֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָֽד׃\rb* \rb were there.|שָׁם֙\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb So the congregation|הָעֵדָ֗ה\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלְחוּ־\rb* \rb 12,000|שְׁנֵים־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶ֛לֶף\rb* \rb of|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb their most valiant|הֶחָ֑יִל\rb* \rb men|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb and commanded them:|וַיְצַוּ֨וּ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֜ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb “Go|לְ֠כוּ\rb* \rb and put|וְהִכִּיתֶ֞ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword|חֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb those living|יוֹשְׁבֵ֨י\rb* \rb in Jabesh-gilead,|יָבֵ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָד֙\rb* \rb including women|וְהַנָּשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb and children.|וְהַטָּֽף׃\rb* \v 11 \rb This|וְזֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb is what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you are to do:|תַּעֲשׂ֑וּ\rb* \rb Devote to destruction|תַּחֲרִֽימוּ׃\rb*\f + \fr 21:11 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb male,|זָכָ֗ר\rb* \rb as well as every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb female|אִשָּׁ֛ה\rb* \rb who has had relations with|יֹדַ֥עַת\rb*\rb |מִשְׁכַּב־\rb* \rb a man.”|זָכָ֖ר\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb So they found|וַֽיִּמְצְא֞וּ\rb* \rb among the inhabitants|מִיּוֹשְׁבֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb of Jabesh-gilead|יָבֵ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֗ד\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּ֤ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵאוֹת֙\rb* \rb young|נַעֲרָ֣ה\rb* \rb women|בְתוּלָ֔ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb had not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb had relations with|יָדְעָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |לְמִשְׁכַּ֣ב\rb* \rb a man,|זָכָ֑ר\rb* \rb and they brought|וַיָּבִ֨יאוּ\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֤ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶה֙\rb* \rb at Shiloh|שִׁלֹ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Canaan.|כְּנָֽעַן׃ס\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Then the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb congregation|הָ֣עֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb sent|וַֽיִּשְׁלְחוּ֙\rb* \rb a message|וַֽיְדַבְּרוּ֙\rb*\rb |וַיִּקְרְא֥וּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb of peace|שָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Benjamites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בִנְיָמִ֔ן\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb were at the rock|בְּסֶ֣לַע\rb* \rb of Rimmon.|רִמּ֑וֹן\rb* \v 14 \rb And at that|הַהִ֔יא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the Benjamites|בִּנְיָמִן֙\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּ֤שָׁב\rb* \rb and were given|וַיִּתְּנ֤וּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb the women|הַנָּשִׁ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb who were spared|חִיּ֔וּ\rb*\rb |מִנְּשֵׁ֖י\rb* \rb from Jabesh-gilead.|יָבֵ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֑ד\rb* \rb But there were not|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |מָצְא֥וּ\rb* \rb enough women|כֵּֽן׃\rb* \rb for all of them.|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb The people|וְהָעָ֥ם\rb* \rb grieved|נִחָ֖ם\rb* \rb for Benjamin,|לְבִנְיָמִ֑ן\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb had made|עָשָׂ֧ה\rb* \rb a void|פֶּ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb in the tribes|בְּשִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Then the elders|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the congregation|הָעֵדָ֔ה\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּֽאמְר֨וּ\rb* \rb “What|מַה־\rb* \rb should we do|נַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb about wives|לְנָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb for those who remain,|לַנּוֹתָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the women|אִשָּֽׁה׃\rb* \rb of Benjamin|מִבִּנְיָמִ֖ן\rb* \rb have been destroyed?”|נִשְׁמְדָ֥ה\rb* \v 17 \rb They added,|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “There must be heirs|יְרֻשַּׁ֥ת\rb* \rb for the survivors|פְּלֵיטָ֖ה\rb* \rb of Benjamin,|לְבִנְיָמִ֑ן\rb* \rb so that a tribe|שֵׁ֖בֶט\rb* \rb of Israel|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb be wiped out.|יִמָּחֶ֥ה\rb* \v 18 \rb But we|וַאֲנַ֗חְנוּ\rb* \rb cannot|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |נוּכַ֛ל\rb* \rb give|לָתֵת־\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb our daughters|מִבְּנוֹתֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb as wives.”|נָשִׁ֖ים\rb*
\p \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb had sworn,|נִשְׁבְּע֤וּ\rb* \rb “Cursed is|אָר֕וּר\rb* \rb he who gives|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb a wife|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb to a Benjamite.”|לְבִנְיָמִֽן׃ס\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb “But look,”|הִנֵּה֩\rb* \rb they said,|וַיֹּאמְר֡וּ\rb* \rb “there is a yearly|מִיָּמִ֣ים׀\rb*\rb |יָמִ֗ימָה\rb* \rb feast|חַג־\rb* \rb to the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb in Shiloh,|בְּשִׁל֜וֹ\rb* \rb which is|אֲשֶׁ֞ר\rb* \rb north|מִצְּפ֤וֹנָה\rb*\rb |לְבֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Bethel|אֵל֙\rb*\rb |מִזְרְחָ֣ה\rb* \rb east|הַשֶּׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the road|לִמְסִלָּ֔ה\rb* \rb that goes up|הָעֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb from|מִבֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵ֖ל\rb* \rb to Shechem,|שְׁכֶ֑מָה\rb* \rb and south|וּמִנֶּ֖גֶב\rb* \rb of Lebonah.”|לִלְבוֹנָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb So they commanded|וַיְצַו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Benjamites:|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |בִנְיָמִ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Go,|לְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb hide|וַאֲרַבְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb in the vineyards|בַּכְּרָמִֽים׃\rb* \v 21 \rb and watch.|וּרְאִיתֶ֗ם\rb* \rb When|אִם־\rb* \rb you see|וְ֠הִנֵּה\rb* \rb the daughters|בְנוֹת־\rb* \rb of Shiloh|שִׁילוֹ֮\rb* \rb come out|יֵ֨צְא֥וּ\rb* \rb to perform|לָח֣וּל\rb* \rb their dances,|בַּמְּחֹלוֹת֒\rb* \rb each of you|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb is to come out|וִֽיצָאתֶם֙\rb* \rb of the vineyards,|הַכְּרָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb catch|וַחֲטַפְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb for himself|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb a wife|אִשְׁתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the daughters|מִבְּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Shiloh,|שִׁיל֑וֹ\rb* \rb and go|וַהֲלַכְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb to the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Benjamin.|בִּנְיָמִֽן׃\rb* \v 22 \rb |וְהָיָ֡ה\rb* \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb their fathers|אֲבוֹתָם֩\rb* \rb or|א֨וֹ\rb* \rb brothers|אֲחֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb come|יָבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to us|אֵלֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb to complain,|לָרוֹב\rb* \rb we will tell them,|וְאָמַ֤רְנוּ\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb ‘Do us a favor|חָנּ֣וּנוּ\rb* \rb by helping them,|אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb since|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb we did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb get|לָקַ֛חְנוּ\rb* \rb wives|אִשְׁתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb for each of them|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb in the war.|בַּמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb Since|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb actually|כָּעֵ֥ת\rb* \rb give them|נְתַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb your daughters,|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb you have no guilt.’”|תֶּאְשָֽׁמוּ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb The Benjamites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בִנְיָמִ֔ן\rb* \rb did|וַיַּֽעֲשׂוּ־\rb* \rb as instructed|כֵן֙\rb* \rb and carried away|וַיִּשְׂא֤וּ\rb* \rb the number|לְמִסְפָּרָ֔ם\rb* \rb of women|נָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb they needed from|מִן־\rb* \rb the dancers|הַמְּחֹלְל֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they caught.|גָּזָ֑לוּ\rb* \rb They went|וַיֵּלְכ֗וּ\rb* \rb back|וַיָּשׁ֙וּבוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their own inheritance,|נַ֣חֲלָתָ֔ם\rb* \rb rebuilt|וַיִּבְנוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their cities,|הֶ֣עָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb and settled|וַיֵּשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb in them.|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 24 \rb And at that|הַהִ֔יא\rb* \rb time,|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb each|אִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb returned|וַיִּתְהַלְּכ֨וּ\rb* \rb from there|מִשָּׁ֤ם\rb* \rb to his own tribe|לְשִׁבְט֖וֹ\rb* \rb and clan,|וּלְמִשְׁפַּחְתּ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |וַיֵּצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb each|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |מִשָּׁ֔ם\rb* \rb to his own inheritance.|לְנַחֲלָתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb In those|הָהֵ֔ם\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb there was no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb king|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb in Israel;|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb everyone|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb did what was|יַעֲשֶֽׂה׃\rb* \rb right|הַיָּשָׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in his own eyes.|בְּעֵינָ֖יו\rb*
